    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Campus-Security-Specialist_JR50087-1": {
      "title": "Campus Security Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-18\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for a Campus Security Specialist to ensure the reliable operation, maintenance and continuous improvement of critical campus security, life-safety and building systems. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile . WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package 13th month Tet bonus for Vietnamese staff Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! Position Summary Property Services team has the responsibility to operate, maintain and enhance the buildings owned by RMIT University, oversee construction projects and ensure the provision of physical facilities services. Property Services consists of the following business units: • Projects • Facilities Management • Campus planning & operations The Campus Security Specialist is responsible for the ongoing health, programming and reliable operation including but not limited to the following systems. •           Electronic Access Control (EAC) •           Closed Circuit Television (CCTV) •           Building Management Systems (BMS) •           Fire Alarm Control System •           Lighting Controls •           Lift Controls •           Emergency Control Room •           Emergency Response System •           Workday for Contract Management of Security related suppliers Working arrangements: The standard working week for this position is Tuesday to Saturday to provide operational coverage over the weekend. The role will also participate in the Emergency Management Team (EMT) 24/7 on-call roster and may be required to respond outside standard working hours, subject to operational requirements. Reporting Line Reports to:  Security Manager Direct reports: Security Supervisor from Security Service Provide & Security admin Reporting lines may be adjusted in line with organisational changes. Key Accountabilities Develop University-wide Security programs, plans, policies, and procedures to ensure safety, and security and reduce the risk for staff, students' contractors, and visitors  Closely lead and manage day-to-day security service provider to ensure the effective management of security operations including emergency and crisis management across 3 campuses. Prioritize the deployment of operational resources across a broad program of work using a risk-based approach  Oversee security needs at all University events and for all University events including performing security risk assessments   Subject matter expert for security develops security solutions for complex University-wide security issues  Identify and improve security vulnerabilities and respond to instances of operational crisis to mitigate further operational legal and reputational issues  Manage stakeholder relationships, including security contractors staff student visitors, and emergency services whilst providing a high level of customer service  Actively evaluate on-campus incidents, recommend and take necessary actions to maintain the security of RMIT's students' administration, faculty, staff, and property Keep track of reported incidents for further review and reporting Create and present incident reports with recommendations for learning from experience and proposing new action plans to avoid repeating events  Lead the investigation of security incidents/complaints including interviews and review of CCTV and provide feedback to students, staff, and customers accordingly  Apply current and new technology to provide technical and operational solutions to senior internal members of staff and work closely with the external contract provider, in relation to day-to-day Security issues to develop a culture of crime prevention incident reduction and traffic management Provide comprehensive reporting on security for senior management including written proposals and reports for action where areas of concern are identified.  Provide forecast analysis and manage Security service budget to ensure high-quality security service with reasonable cost  Develop training plan, materials and provide necessary orientation and training regarding security rules and procedures to contracted security personnel  Collaborate on the development of emergency and continuity plans at various University locations may conduct related training exercises  Undertake any other duties as required by the line manager Key Selection Criteria Bachelor’s in public security or related field At least 5 years of experience in a security related position Sound understanding of legal requirements and standards with regards to public security in Vietnam Significant experience in security management (incl Electronic Security and Surveillance) in a large complex organization including experience in the supervision of large, outsourced security contracts and their related budgets Proven ability to manage day to day operations of a large security team including internal and contracted personnel Extensive experience in successful management of stakeholder relationships within a large complex organization ability to deliver high level of customer service to a wide variety of stakeholders and leadership of a team with a client focused approach to Security services delivery Extensive knowledge of electronic security and surveillance operational systems the security sector regulatory environment and the development and implementation of Security policies and procedures in a large complex organization Excellent written and verbal English and Vietnamese skills, with ability to communicate Ability to write reports and briefs in English9Good judgement and the ability to quickly assess options and make decisions and understanding of risk management in a large complex education organization Proven ability to priorities tasks works to deadlines, manage multiple deliverables work autonomously as well as a productive team member Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position and RMIT Values. HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 12 thg 9 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Hanoi/Expression-of-Interest---Casual-Academic_JR44896": {
      "title": "Expression of Interest – Casual Academic",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-12\nPart time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam welcome Expressions of Interest (EOI) from talented lecturers and researchers  to join our academic community and deliver high-quality teaching, research, and student engagement. This is an exciting opportunity for an educator-scholar who is passionate about shaping future-ready graduates and contributing to impactful research.  WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER   Competitive hourly rate.  Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources  A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!  Learn more about Casual ​Academic at RMIT Vietnam. CURRENT VACANCIES IN SEM 3, 2026 We are currently looking for Academic Casual staff to perform specified teaching-related duties, such as presenting lectures and tutorials, conducting practical classes or workshops, and marking with relevant courses/programs in The Business School below: International Business (Global Trade Operations, International Trade and Global Supply Chains, etc.) at SGS Campus Digital Marketing (C onsumer Psychology and Behaviour, Retailing courses) in Hanoi and SGS Campus HRM in Hanoi and SGS Campus Logistics and Supply Chain (Business courses) in Hanoi and SGS Campus Economics ( courses in Digital Economy program) in SGS Campus DISCIPLINES OF INTEREST  We welcome EOIs from candidates with expertise in areas including, but not limited to:  THE BUSSINESS SCHOOL Business Accounting Economics and Finance Human Resource Management Global Business Management Logistics and Supply Chain Management Digital Business Digital Marketing Tourism and Hospitality Management SCHOOL OF DESIGN & COMMUNICATION Professional Communication: Advertising, Digital Communication and Public Relations Digital Media : Interaction design, Animation, Digital imaging, Sound Design Studies: Graphics, Spatial Concepts, Illustration, User Experience Design Game Design : Game Design Studio, Coding Unity, C#  Digital Film and Video : Film-/video-making, Technical studio, Film theory Fashion Enterprise : Design and Product Development, Retail and Merchandising, Customer Relationship Management and Communication SCHOOL OF SCIENCE, ENGINEERING & TECHNOLOGY Engineering: Mechanical, Electrical, Electronics, Robotics, Mechatronics, Manufacturing, Automation  Computing & Technology: Computer Science, Software Engineering, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Cybersecurity  Aviation & Aerospace: Aviation management, aviation safety, airport operations, aerospace systems  Psychology: Clinical psychology, social psychology, Health psychology, Cognitive psychology  KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES SUMMARY    We are currently looking for Academic Casual staff to perform specified teaching-related duties, such as presenting lectures and tutorials, conducting practical classes or workshops, and marking. Casual rates for academic teaching duties include both the presentation or delivery time and the associated working time (including preparation, reasonably contemporaneous marking, and student consultation) and further information can be found in FaQ . ​ Key Selection Criteria   Master's degree (for Associate Lecturer) or PhD degree (for Lecturer )  Minimum 3 years of teaching experience in English-speaking universities in relevant field.  Demonstrated ability to prepare and deliver programs at undergraduate level, including online delivery, and the ability to produce high quality curriculum or program materials.  Industry or professional experience  Culturally adapt and agile     HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible.  COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 30 thg 12 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Calling-for-Expression-of-Interest-for-Indigenous-Talent-to-work-in-Academia--VE-and-Professional-roles-at-RMIT--all-campuses-_JR14035": {
      "title": "RMIT invites Aboriginal & Torres Strait Islander peoples to express your interest to work at RMIT (Melbourne, Bundoora or Brunswick campuses) in Professional, Vocational or Academic roles.",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-03-12\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT encourages Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Peoples to apply to be considered for Identified, Targeted, or mainstream roles (Designated EOI)* Explore roles as Teachers, Professional, or Academic staff Possibilities for fixed-term and ongoing roles with flexible hybrid working arrangements Benefit from 17% superannuation, 10 days cultural leave and specialist wellbeing and career support services ​ Why work at RMIT? At RMIT, we celebrate and honour the unique cultures and contributions of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples. We are committed to providing robust support and valuable opportunities during your employment and educational journey, enriched by networking opportunities and the facilities available through our Indigenous Staff Network and the Ngarara Willim Centre. \"The Ngarara Willim Centre is a culturally safe space, advocating for the self-determination and success of our Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students and community through dedicated support and empowerment.\" RMIT is a wonderful place to work in the heart of Melbourne CBD with campuses in Brunswick, Bundoora and Point Cook. We have a thriving and growing Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander community who are making an amazing difference at RMIT though engagement with external Indigenous partners, internal collaborations and training and educating staff on self determination, implementation of Indigenous perspectives, responsible practice and cultural safety. Hear from Professor Gary Thomas, Pro Vice Chancellor for Indigenous Education talk about how RMIT is transitioning through Reconciliation to Responsible Practice https://youtu.be/i5MIrtu3Xew?si=uTkzHyjeguJZlrci What’s on offer? RMIT University is excited to offer new opportunities in 2025-2026 at various levels specifically for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Peoples. We offer attractive salaries, with 17% super and 10 days cultural leave, we also offer hybrid working. See our list of benefits here   Benefits and recognition - RMIT University You could work in the Ngarara Willim Centre dedicated to Indigenous Education or within our Colleges/Portfolios including Vocational Education, STEM, Design, IT, Research or Business and Law. Positions include Identified and Targeted roles, along with mainstream roles. Please submit your EOI application with just a CV and I will be in contact with you following this to discuss possible opportunities at RMIT. You can also browse RMIT's career opportunities here , using \"Indigenous\" as a keyword for identified roles or to have a look at our mainstream roles and apply directly. For further details, contact Loretta Vaughan, Senior Talent Advisor - First Peoples Employment at loretta.vaughan@rmit.edu.au or phone 03 9925 0746 . *Special Measures This is an Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Designated Position, under ‘special measures’ of section 12 of the Equal Employment Opportunity Act 2010. Only Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are eligible to apply to this EOI. We look forward to hearing from you and helping to kickstart your career at RMIT! #LI-Hybrid Applications Close: 30 Dec 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Audio-Visual-Specialist_JR51003": {
      "title": "Audio Visual Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking an Audio Visual Specialist ensures the seamless operation, maintenance, and enhancement of audiovisual technologies across learning and meeting spaces to support teaching, events, and collaboration. The role also leads AV projects, manages vendors and stakeholders, develops user training resources, and recommends innovative solutions to improve the university's AV environment. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile. WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Audio Visual Specialist will play a crucial role in ensuring the smooth operation and maintenance of audiovisual systems within RMIT Vietnam's classrooms, theaters, and meeting rooms. This role will involve liaising with the Australian team to uphold the university's high standards for AV infrastructure and services. The role will also be responsible for the day-to-day management of AV services, as well as leading and executing projects to fit out new AV spaces and implement innovative initiatives. Key Accountabilities Summary Oversee the operation and maintenance of all audio-visual equipment, including projectors, sound systems, video conferencing systems, and control systems. Monitor the performance of AV systems and troubleshoot technical issues promptly. Work with external vendors on the delivery, implementation and handover of new AV projects and room refresh. Collaborate with the Australian team to understand and implement the university's AV standards and guidelines. Provide recommendations on new AV initiatives and prepare plans and requirements for RMIT Vietnam. Create and maintain AV user educational literacy, such as room operational guides, training demo videos and online FAQ assistance for AV technologies. Liaise with customers and stakeholders requesting AV fit-out services, understand and capture the business needs and operational requirements. Complete regular and ongoing reassessments and analysis of AV and provide input and recommendation for continuous improvement of tools and or processes. Managing AV documentation resources to include room information, schematics, equipment lists, technical and operational manuals, and AV software. Maintain depth of knowledge and understanding of AV industry trends and the range of vendor technologies to meet the AV requirements for the University. Other duties commensurate with the scope of the role Key Selection Criteria A Bachelor degree in relevant field Significant experience within a Technical AV environment working on large scale projects including vendor management. Demonstrated AV installation experience, project management experience desirable. Demonstrated experience in AV technical knowledgebase, AV design, and CAD packages. Demonstrated ability to build effective relationships in a collaborative and engaging manner with a broad range of internal and external stakeholders. Proven ability to work autonomously with minimal supervision. Demonstrated superior analytical and communication skills. Demonstrated ability to prioritise tasks and delivery a quality service to the University. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position and RMIT Values. More information is available in the Job Description . HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 1 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Associate-Registrar_JR50897": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-07\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking an  Associate Registrar to join Students and Education Portfolio (SEP) at RMIT Vietnam. The Associate Registrar at RMIT Vietnam plays a pivotal role in advancing the university's objectives and strategies to become a leading institution in Southeast Asia, overseeing crucial responsibilities related to academic records, student enrolment, and regulatory compliance, thereby contributing significantly to the overall success and reputation of the university in the region. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER Expatriates   Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates  Relocation allowance package from US$6,000  Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate and direct dependents (if applicable)  International repatriation flights for the staff and direct dependents at the end of their contract.  School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to US$20,000 per child or US$40,000 for two children per year.  Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Vietnamese candidates   Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates.  13th month Tet bonus   Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Other benefits   Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays)  Professional development and career advancement  Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources  A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!  THE STUDENTS AND EDUCATION PORTFOLIO The Students and Education Portfolio (SEP) at RMIT Vietnam leads the University’s learning and teaching excellence, curriculum innovation, and integrated student experience. Working in close partnership with academic schools and central portfolios, SEP advances RMIT’s Knowledge with Action strategy and RMIT Vietnam’s Country Commitment by embedding Active, Applied and Authentic (AAA) pedagogies across programs and ensuring students are prepared for future workplaces. SEP brings together academic development, digital innovation, student life, Library and Digital Services, and learning support functions to create an inclusive and engaging learning environment. The portfolio focuses on student success, wellbeing and retention; employability through industry-integrated and work-integrated learning; and the thoughtful integration of digital technologies, including AI, into teaching, assessment and student support. Through this work, SEP plays a central role in positioning RMIT Vietnam as a regional leader in transformative, future-ready education. ABOUT THE ROLE   The Associate Registrar Vietnam, Academic Registrar’s Group (ARG) Vietnam, is responsible for making of key strategic administrative, programming, financial and staffing decisions in relation to student lifecycle and student integrity at RMIT Vietnam. In addition, this position provides inputs in day-to-day operation of ARG in Vietnam and works closely with ARG in Melbourne to support RMIT Vietnam Executive Leadership Team (ELT) in developing seamless approaches to provide an equivalent standard of support and services to students and staff at RMIT Vietnam and to ensure academic policies and processes are best practised. Finally, the position plays a strategic role in large-scale projects such as RMIT scholarships, student system development, and graduation ceremonies to ensure budget, planning, transition, and execution are well in place. It is required that the position works both strategically and operationally across a diverse set of university departments and stakeholders, and to model RMIT values and behaviours in the following five key areas: Government Reporting, Academic Policy planning and Student Visa Compliance. Enrolments and Student Records, including Student Financials Assessment Support, Student Conduct and Complaints Academic Governance and Systems. Completions, Awards and Graduations This position is strategic in nature but retains operational oversight of activities by ARG in RMIT Vietnam  KEY ACCOUNTIBILITIES   To advance the vision of the Students and Education Portfolio (SEP) led by the Dean of Students, collaborate with the relevant leadership teams, develop and implement innovative strategies to ensure alignment with RMIT Vietnam’s regional objectives. To anticipate future trends in higher education and academic administration contributing to the development of RMIT Vietnam and the university as a whole. Working collaboratively with the Academic Registrar’s Group (ARG) leadership team, to own, develop and provide strategic direction in the areas of registry and governance for RMIT Vietnam to succeed with its operational and development goals and objectives. To facilitate functional alignment between RMIT Vietnam and Melbourne operations through respective teams, systems and processes. Identify, highlight, and tabulate proposals to control, prevent, mitigate, and report to higher management critical risks of non-compliance with the academic policies and procedures or scopes of services delivered beyond stipulated regulations or system potential failures. Be an authorised signatory designated by RMIT Vietnam Pro Vice-Chancellor and General Director for student-related documents released to relevant authorities, students or third parties. Be the single point of contact to provide student information and regular reports to statutory authorities following RMIT Privacy Policy and Delegation of Authority Policy. Lead, manage and enhance the delivery of key administrative services across the Student Lifecycle – from the first enrolment to graduation – for preparatory, undergraduate, and post-graduate levels at all RMIT Vietnam locations. Drive the execution of key events including graduation ceremonies and scholarship awards. Ensure governance of assessment support and student conduct processes to protect academic integrity and to best practice Student Conduct Policy and Student Conduct Regulations, facilitating functional alignment between RMIT Vietnam and Australia. Represent the Academic Registrar Group (Vietnam) on relevant working groups and committees, hearing sessions including but not limited to the RMIT Vietnam Incident Management Team (IMT) for matters concerning student complaints, student misconduct, and academic policy. Oversee and provide management support in (i) student-related complaints and (ii) third-party complaints aligning with policies and procedures of the university and in consultation with the ARG Complaint team and the Central Complaints and Investigation team in Australia. Proactive drive and be a conduit for policy review collaborating with RMIT global to provide a voice for RMIT Vietnam, enacting changes, and ensuring relevance to local operations. Be responsible for providing advice and guidance to staff and other stakeholders on academic policies and processes. Pro-actively disseminate changes through different channels including but not limited to training, workshops and communication platforms. Oversee, uplift, and enhance student systems operations and developments being gatekeeper to relevant student and academic platforms to the benefit of RMIT Vietnam. Oversee the development, review and publication of academic calendar, student guides and relevant process documentation; deliver training, workshops, information sessions and presentations for stakeholders and students: ensure information is effectively communicated and published across multiple channels to ensure students and staff are well informed about Student Lifecycle and Student Integrity processes and issues. Create awareness to facilitate functional and governance alignment between RMIT Vietnam and Australia. Liaise, communicate, and collaborate with Academic Schools, Student Connect, Finance and other key departments regularly to support and gather input on the Student Lifecycle and Student Integrity experience. Monitor and provide support on relevant compliance and quality issues and facilitate the resolution of complex issues. For full details of the accountability, please refer to the Job Description . KEY SELECTION CRITERIA A Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field (e.g. business administration, educational leadership, and management). A Master’s degree is desirable as is prior abroad experience. A minimum of 10 years of managerial experience of which at least 5 years of business/operational development experience in an education or training environment, preferably with multinational organisations. Demonstrated leadership and managerial experience in a similar position with excellent administration management and organisational skills, project management and the ability to drive and implement strategic initiatives. A forward-thinker who is one step ahead and has foresight in order to manage issues before they occur. A strong understanding of university policy, governance and processes related to the Student Lifecycle, Student Integrity, and strong operational management skills. Well-versed in Vietnam's local context, government relations and experience in working with local authorities and foreign government agencies, especially in matters related to international students. Demonstrated ability to work with a diverse group of stakeholders with strong presentation and negotiation skills. Track records in developing and implementing relevant policy, processes and protocols across an organisation; demonstrated problem-solving skills and proven experience in managing and providing solutions to complex issues. A data-driven person who embraces changes and improvements in quality management processes to drive continuous improvement. Experience working with databases, customer management systems and relevant software. Excellent communication skills, including written, verbal, and visual communication, experience in writing process documentation and reports, delivering presentations, and the ability to convey complex ideas to diverse audiences. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible.  COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to Viet Nguyen- Senior Talent Acquisition Advisor at  nguyen.vanviet@rmit.edu.vn    #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 5 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Lecturer--Management_JR46455": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-03\nFull time\n\nOverview: We are seeking a Lecturer in Management to join our academic community and deliver high-quality teaching, research, and student engagement. This is an exciting opportunity for an educator-scholar who is passionate about shaping future-ready graduates and contributing to impactful research. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available at Working at RMIT Vietnam . Our benefit: Expatriates   Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates Relocation allowance package of USD $6,000 Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate (and immediate family if applicable). International repatriation flights for the staff, their spouse, and children at the end of their contract. School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to $20,000 per child or $40,000 for two children per year.  Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance. Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Vietnamese candidates   Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates.  13th month bonus.  Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Others Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays). Professional development and career advancement.   Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources. A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!  RMIT Vietnam has been honoured with the respectable HR Asia Award as Top Employer to Work for in Asia. To find out more about RMIT Vietnam and our current vacancies, please visit our website: https://www.rmit.edu.vn/careers . The Business School – A Hub of Innovation, Excellence, and Global Impact   As the largest academic school at RMIT Vietnam, The Business School is home to over 9,000 students across our Ho Chi Minh City and Hanoi campuses. With a diverse and international faculty of more than 160  academic and professional staff from over 15 countries, The Business School offers a dynamic and inclusive environment that fosters excellence in teaching, research, and industry engagement.   Our faculty members are accomplished professionals who have studied, worked and researched in renowned institutions around the world. Their extensive work experience provides our students with valuable industry insights and in-depth knowledge.   We offer a comprehensive suite of programs—from undergraduate to doctoral levels—designed to prepare students for success in an increasingly complex and fast-paced global business environment.  The Business School is proud to be the first in Vietnam to earn  AACSB accreditation, affirming our commitment to world-class standards in business education. Our research strengths span blockchain, cybersecurity, smart cities, and sustainability, contributing to RMIT’s strategic research pillars and shaping the future of business innovation.  As we continue to grow and innovate, we invite passionate professionals to join us in shaping the future of business education in Vietnam and beyond.   More information about The Business School can be found here   Position Summary The Lecturer contributes to Teaching and Research, and Engagement in the Management Program within the Department of Management. The successful candidate will contribute to the development of the program to meet the needs of students and other stakeholders, ensure a consistent level of research is undertaken to support relevant research clusters in the Business School. He/She may deliver courses across related programs as directed. The incumbent also contributes to the strategic direction setting of the program, department, and School by working collaboratively with other relevant members of the department to plan and develop courses, programs, and engagement activities. The successful candidate assists the Senior Program Manager on occasion with administrative decisions and tasks. The scope of responsibilities includes supporting the formulation of strategic planning for the program, course management, where needed, quality assurance, student relationship management, human resource management, program budgeting and resource management and research planning. Key accountabilities Undertake independent teaching at undergraduate, honours and postgraduate level including: designing, conducting and moderating assessment; implementing improvements informed by course evaluation activities and student feedback. Undertake independent professional activities, scholarship and/or conduct high quality research activities appropriate to the profession or discipline including: managing individual projects within timelines and budgets and ensuring compliance with quality and reporting requirements; publishing research results in high quality outlets as lead or co-author; preparing and submitting external research funding applications; and supervising higher degree by research candidates. Undertake administration duties, which may include course coordination role or management of a small award program. Adhere to the requirements of the Academic Expectations and Development Framework of RMIT Vietnam. Our requirements Demonstrated ability to prepare and deliver courses related to Strategy, Leadership, Management, Design Thinking, or Innovation at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including online delivery, and the ability to produce high-quality curriculum or program materials. Ability to undertake course coordination role. Demonstrated capacity to work effectively with and to negotiate sensitively with students especially on issues related to effective learning. Emerging track record and recognition for quality research outputs which will contribute to existing Discipline and School research areas evidenced by publications, development of new research initiatives, competitive research funding, and industry links. Demonstrated ability to supervise higher degree by research candidates. Ability to build effective networks with colleagues and generate alternative funding projects through effective liaison with industry and government. Excellent interpersonal and communications skills appropriate for interacting with higher degree by research candidates, staff and industry, together with a strong commitment to teamwork and multidisciplinary collaboration. Recent and sustained performance regarding student outcomes, student experience and feedback; combined with experience and skill in a range of teaching settings. Ability to operate within own discipline and cross-disciplinary/multidisciplinary teams to achieve department and University strategic outcomes. Ability to work with external partners, industries, organisations and communities and can operate effectively to address complex issues or seek opportunities Ability to motivate, develop and inspire others through discipline leadership in the University environment Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position as per the RMIT Values Expected Research profile   To be considered for a lecturer position at RMIT Vietnam in The Business School, you will need to be able to meet the following research criteria.  For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3 years (Early Career Academic), although there are no requirements you are expected to be research active.   For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3- 5 years there are requirements of peer reviewed journal articles published within the previous five-year window, you need to be active in relevant research areas.   For candidates with a PhD awarded more than 5 years ago: you will be expected to demonstrate a minimum of 2 peer reviewed journal articles, of which must be ranked in Scimago or ABDC and preferably both in Q1/A ranking or equivalent, within the previous five-year window.  HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible.  COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application   is submitted through   our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant   about scams asking   for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 19 thg 9 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/College-of-Business-and-Law---Expression-of-Interest-for-Sessional-Teaching---School-of-Law_JR51143-1": {
      "title": "College of Business and Law - Expression of Interest for Sessional Teaching – School of Law",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-17\nPart time\n\nOverview: •    Casual hours commencing February 202 7   •    Based at the Emily McPherson Building located in Melbourne CBD campus but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University or online   About RMIT RMIT offers life-changing experiences for our students, and helps shape the world with research, innovation, teaching and industry engagement. With strong industry connections forged over 130 years, collaboration with industry remains integral to RMIT’s leadership in education, applied and innovative research, and to the development of highly skilled, globally focused graduates.     The College of Business and Law delivers innovative, industry-engaged education and applied research in a global context, supporting RMIT’s Ready for Life and Work strategy through student experience, staff purpose, research impact and global reach.    For further details about the College, please visit: College of Business and Law      School of Law     The School of Law, established in 2025 , evolved from the former Graduate School of Business and Law. Situated in the historic Emily McPherson Building, it offers RMIT law students an engaging and dynamic learning environment, enriched by state-of-the-art resources, experienced teaching staff, and strong industry connections.     As one of four schools within RMIT’s College of Business and Law, the School delivers the Bachelor of Laws (including double degrees) and the Juris Doctor program, both accredited by the Victorian Legal Admissions Board.     Committed to excellence in teaching and research, the School prepares students for the demands of the legal profession and beyond. Its curriculum covers all core law subjects, complemented by a wide range of electives and practical skills development, including advocacy, interviewing, and negotiation simulations. The School also fosters a collegial and supportive community that encourages both academic and professional growth.     Further information regarding RMIT’s School of Law and our programs can be found here.   Express Your Interest    We welcome expressions of interest from both external applicants and current RMIT casual employees interested in contributing to the School of Law programs.      To submit your expression of interest, please click ‘Apply’ and submit a current CV and covering letter addressing the following: 1- Please outline what type of work you would be interested in:    • Teaching    • Marking    • Online Teachin g (available only for sessional teachers based in Victoria)   2- Please briefly outline your academic and/or professional experience .   3- If you are interested in tutoring or teaching, please provide a summary of your teaching ability and your capacity to engage students positively and constructively .   4- If you would like to be considered for future casual research opportunities, please briefly outline your research interest .   Please note: The volume, nature and availability of sessional teaching will vary based on the needs of the school including course offerings, timetabling and student demand.     Although our needs and vacancies regularly change , there are opportunities that exist across our programs. By submitting an application, you will be included into a Talent Pool that will be reviewed across the year and may not guarantee a position.      Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children Check.   For further information about this position, please contact casualrecruitment@rmit.edu.au via email.     Applications Close: 17 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Casual-VE-Teacher---Mechanical--Aerospace---Civil-Engineering_JR51167": {
      "title": "Casual VE Teacher,  Mechanical, Aerospace & Civil Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-18\nPart time\n\nOverview: Casual hours  commencing ASAP   Teaching into Advanced Diploma of Engineering Technology (Civil Engineering Design) Based at the Melbourne City Campus   About You    As a Casual Teacher within RMIT’s College of Vocational Education, you will be mainly responsible for the delivery of course material, assessing students and the supervision of students enrolled in selected courses within the program.      You will participate in the program’s continuing review of course content and development, delivery, teaching methods (including online delivery methods) and methods of students’ assessment.   Your performance will be underpinned by participation in relevant activities which ensure your vocational competence meets and/or exceeds the education level being delivered and assessed.     We are looking for VE Teachers to assist in the program of Advanced Diploma of Engineering Technology (Civil Engineering Design). To be successful in this position, you’ll have as a minimum:     Qualification in Engineering (Civil Engineering Design)   Industry experience in Engineering   A valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check    Certificate IV in Training and Assessment (TAE40110 or higher)  is required About the College     The purpose of RMIT’s College of Vocational Education is to empower learners and our industry, community and government partners to succeed in the new world of work.     Our five-year strategic roadmap, ALiVE@RMIT, purposefully guides everything we do in vocational education to deliver our vision: to position RMIT as a leading multi-sector provider with global impact and influence.     Led by our Pro Vice Chancellor, the College of VE is reimagining how we deliver vocational education to create unique experiences for our students and partners, so we can:   •    lead in practice-based learning   •    empower learners for the future of work   •    engage industry and community at scale   •    grow for impact and influence     The College of VE is delivering impact through transformation that creates long-term change.   To  Apply     Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘Apply’ link at the top of this page.      For further information about this position, please contact Mykayla McCartin via Mykayla.mccartin@rmit.edu.au    Applications Close: 18 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Lecturer--International-Business_JR48414": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer, International Business",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Lecturer or Senior Lecturer in International Business to join our academic community in Ho Chi Minh City or Hanoi . In this role, you will deliver high-quality teaching, contribute to impactful research, and engage meaningfully with students. Applicants with teaching and research expertise in Global Business, Global Corporate Responsibility, Cross‑Cultural Management, Global Trade Operations, Political Economy of Global Business , or other closely related areas of International Business are strongly encouraged to apply WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER   Expatriates   Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates  Relocation allowance package from US$6,000  Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate and direct dependents (if applicable)  International repatriation flights for the staff and direct dependents at the end of their contract.  School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to US$20,000 per child or US$40,000 for two children per year.  Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Vietnamese candidates   Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates.  13th month Tet bonus   Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Other benefits   Generous annual leave, career leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays)  Professional development and career advancement  Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources  A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!  POSITION SUMMARY   Lecturer/Senior Lecturer contributes to Teaching and Research, and Engagement in the International Business Program within the Department of Management. The successful candidate will contribute to the development of the program to meet the needs of students and other stakeholders, ensure a consistent level of research is undertaken to support relevant research clusters in the Business School. He/She may deliver courses across related programs as directed. The incumbent also contributes to the strategic direction setting of the program, department, and School by working collaboratively with other relevant members of the department to plan and develop courses, programs, and engagement activities. The successful candidate assists the Senior Program Manager on occasion with administrative decisions and tasks. Key Accountabilities summary    Undertake independent teaching at undergraduate, honours and postgraduate level, including designing, conducting, and moderating assessment; implementing improvements informed by course evaluation activities and student feedback Undertake independent professional activities, scholarship and/or conduct high quality research activities appropriate to the profession or discipline including: managing individual projects within timelines and budgets and ensuring compliance with quality and reporting requirements; publishing research results in high quality journals as lead or co-author; preparing and submitting external research funding applications; and supervising HDR candidates Contribute to the development of a research-based culture within the program through individual and collaborative research activities Manage course amendment processes and course-related policies, pursuant to the School, College and University procedures and in liaison with RMIT Melbourne Key Selection Criteria   PhD or equivalent Doctoral qualification in International Business or closely related areas Experience in preparing and delivering undergraduate and postgraduate programs in the following courses: Global Business, Global Corporate Responsibility, Cross Cultural Management, Global Trade Operations, and Political Economy of Global Business . This includes online delivery and the creation of high-quality curriculum materials. Ability to coordinate and develop courses. Proven ability to work effectively with students, particularly on learning-related issues. Established track record in quality research outputs contributing to program and School research areas. Experience in supervising higher degree research candidates. Proven ability to generate alternative funding projects through effective networking with colleagues, industry, and government. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with a commitment to teamwork and multidisciplinary collaboration. Proven performance in student outcomes and experience, with skills in various teaching settings Expected Research profile   To be considered for a lecturer position at RMIT Vietnam in The Business School, you will need to be able to meet the following research criteria.  For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3 years (Early Career Academic), although there are no requirements you are expected to be research active.   For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3- 5 years there are requirements of peer reviewed journal articles published within the previous five-year window, you need to be active in relevant research areas.   For candidates with a PhD awarded more than 5 years ago: you will be expected to demonstrate a minimum of 2 peer reviewed journal articles, of which must be ranked in Scimago or ABDC and preferably both in Q1/A ranking or equivalent, within the previous five-year window.  To be considered for a Senior Lecturer position and above, The Business School operates a research active points system. Points are earned across a spectrum of research within a prior three-year window. Candidates for higher level positions will be considered against these criteria for shortlisting.  More information is available in the Job Description      HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be conducting a rolling recruitment process. Applications will be reviewed and progressed as they are received. Early submission is encouraged, as the University reserves the right to make an appointment prior to the advertised closing date. COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 18 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Lecturer--Senior-Lecturer---Digital-Marketing_JR48193": {
      "title": "Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer - Digital Marketing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-21\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Digital Marketing to contribute to teaching, research, and engagement within the Digital Marketing program in the Department of Business Innovation. We welcome applications from candidates with teaching and research expertise in areas including, but not limited to Digital Marketing Strategy and Planning, Digital Marketing Communications, Social Media and Mobile Marketing, and Contemporary Issues in Digital Marketing. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER   Expatriates   Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates  Relocation allowance package from US$6,000  Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate and direct dependents (if applicable)  International repatriation flights for the staff and direct dependents at the end of their contract.  School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to US$20,000 per child or US$40,000 for two children per year.  Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Vietnamese candidates   Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates.  13th month Tet bonus   Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Other benefits   Generous annual leave, career leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays)  Professional development and career advancement  Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources  A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!  POSITION SUMMARY   The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer contributes to Teaching and Research, and Engagement in the Digital Marketing Program within the Department of Business Innovation. The successful candidate will contribute to the development and delivery of undergraduate and postgraduate courses and programs to meet the needs of students and other stakeholders, ensure a consistent level of research is undertaken to support relevant research clusters in the Business School, and work collaboratively with other academic staff to support a strong research culture within the Digital Marketing team. The successful candidate may deliver courses across related programs as directed. The incumbent also contributes to the strategic direction-setting of the program, department, and School by working collaboratively with other relevant members of the department to plan and develop courses, programs, and engagement activities. This includes contributing to the design, development, amendment and continuous improvement of undergraduate and postgraduate courses, the development of new courses at both levels, and the initiation of teaching and learning initiatives relevant to Digital Marketing and related programs. The successful candidate assists the Senior Program Manager on occasion with administrative decisions and tasks. The scope of responsibilities includes supporting the formulation of strategic planning for the program, course management, where needed, quality assurance, student relationship management, human resource management, program budgeting and resource management and research planning. The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer will act in accordance with the Academic Expectations framework of RMIT University Vietnam. Key Selection Criteria   PhD or equivalent relevant Doctoral qualification Demonstrated ability to prepare and deliver programs at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including online delivery, and the ability to produce high-quality curriculum or program materials. Ability to undertake course coordination and development roles. Demonstrated capacity to work effectively with and to negotiate sensitively with students especially on issues related to effective learning. Established track record and recognition for quality research outputs which will contribute to existing program and School research areas evidenced by publications, development of new research initiatives, competitive research funding, and industry links. Demonstrated ability to supervise higher degree by research candidates. Ability to build effective networks with colleagues and generate alternative funding projects through effective liaison with industry and government. Excellent interpersonal and communications skills appropriate for interacting with higher degree by research candidates, staff and industry, together with a strong commitment to teamwork and multidisciplinary collaboration. Recent and sustained performance regarding student outcomes, student experience and feedback; combined with experience and skill in a range of teaching settings. Ability to operate within own discipline and cross-disciplinary/multidisciplinary teams to achieve department and University strategic outcomes. Ability to work effectively with external partners, industry, organisations and communities to address complex issues and identify opportunities. Ability to motivate, develop and inspire others through discipline leadership in the University environment. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model (Inclusion, Imagination, Agility, Courage, Passion and Impact). Expected Research profile   To be considered for a lecturer position at RMIT Vietnam in The Business School, you will need to be able to meet the following research criteria.  For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3 years (Early Career Academic), although there are no requirements you are expected to be research active.   For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3- 5 years there are requirements of peer reviewed journal articles published within the previous five-year window, you need to be active in relevant research areas.   For candidates with a PhD awarded more than 5 years ago: you will be expected to demonstrate a minimum of 2 peer reviewed journal articles, of which must be ranked in Scimago or ABDC and preferably both in Q1/A ranking or equivalent, within the previous five-year window.  To be considered for a Senior Lecturer position and above, The Business School operates a research active points system. Points are earned across a spectrum of research within a prior three-year window. Candidates for higher level positions will be considered against these criteria for shortlisting.  More information is available in the Job description    HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be conducting a rolling recruitment process. Applications will be reviewed and progressed as they are received. Early submission is encouraged, as the University reserves the right to make an appointment prior to the advertised closing date. COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 18 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Lecturer_JR50855": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Signal Processing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Continuing position Salary Academic Level B ($119,915 - $142,402 p.a.) + 17% Superannuation and Flexible Working Arrangements Primarily based at Melbourne City campus, and the potential to work across other RMIT campuses as required. About the Role Join RMIT’s School of Engineering as a Lecturer in Signal Processing and help shape the next generation of biomedical engineers. This continuing Level B role offers the opportunity to combine high-quality teaching with research in biomedical signal processing, machine learning and related areas, while contributing to an inclusive, industry-connected academic environment. You will teach across undergraduate, Masters and Graduate Diploma programs, develop contemporary curriculum, support student learning, and build partnerships with academic, industry and professional communities. You will work collaboratively with colleagues in Biomedical Engineering and may also contribute to course coordination, research supervision and initiatives that strengthen RMIT’s impact in health, technology and engineering. Why work with us? This is an opportunity for an emerging academic to grow their teaching, research and industry engagement profile in a university known for applied, work-connected learning and research with real-world impact. You will be part of a supportive STEM College community that values collaboration, accountability, respect and empowerment, with access to multidisciplinary networks across engineering, health innovation, digital technologies and industry partnerships.   To be successful in this position, you’ll have: Demonstrated track record in biomedical signal processing and machine learning Demonstrated ability to design, prepare and deliver programs at undergraduate and post-graduate levels (including online and blended delivery), and the ability to produce high-quality curriculum or program materials using inclusive learning and teaching approaches Ability to undertake course coordination role and embedding technology-enhanced course design and delivery. Demonstrated capacity to work effectively with and to negotiate sensitively with students especially on issues related to effective learning. Emerging track record and recognition for quality research outputs which will contribute to existing Discipline and School research areas evidenced by publications, development of new research initiatives, competitive research funding, and industry links. Demonstrated ability to supervise higher degree by research candidates. Ability to build effective networks with colleagues and generate alternative funding projects through effective liaison with industry and government, particularly in biomedical engineering sector. Excellent interpersonal and communications skills appropriate for interacting with higher degree by research candidates, staff and industry, together with a strong commitment to teamwork and multidisciplinary collaboration and inclusive practices.   Qualifications: Mandatory: PhD or equivalent  in relevant field. Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check. About the STEM College LEARN! GROW! DO! Together transforming the world through STEM STEM College is a community of exceptional researchers, teachers, inventors, designers and game changers, supported by talented professional staff. We deliver higher education programs across STEM disciplines at Bachelor, Master and PhD levels, with a strong focus on work-aligned, life-changing student experiences. Our research strengths span advanced manufacturing and design, computing technologies, health innovation and translational medicine, nano materials and devices, and sustainable systems. Industry is central to what we do, helping ensure our research creates real-world impact and our students graduate ready to contribute. We are proud of our inclusive and caring culture, and we support every member of our community to achieve their potential. In STEM we CARE – Collaboration, Accountability, Respect and Empowerment. For further information about the STEM College please visit the following site:  https://www.rmit.edu.au/about/schools-colleges/stem-college To Apply  Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing the Key Selection Criteria for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page. For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Professor Kate Fox via email kate.fox@rmt.edu.au For further information regarding recruitment processes, please contact Jennifer Pham, Senior Talent Acquisition Advisor via email at jennifer.pham2@rmit.edu.au Please do not share your application to this email address.       Position Description – Lecturer, Signal Processing Applications Close: 29 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Academic--Level-C-E--in-Communication-Network-Engineering_JR50820-2": {
      "title": "Academic (Level C-E) in Communication/Network Engineering",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Continuing position Salary Academic Level C ($146,897 - $169,387 p.a.), Level D ($176,883 - $194,868 p.a.) or Level E ($227,847 p.a.) + 17% Superannuation Based at the Melbourne CBD campus but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University   Teaching commitments can include offshore fly-in fly-out (FIFO) delivery.   About the Role RMIT University is seeking to appoint an outstanding academic in Communication/Network Engineering within the Department of Electrical and Electronic Engineering, School of Engineering. This is one continuing, full-time position that may be appointed at Academic Level C, D or E, depending on the successful candidate’s experience, track record and level of appointment sought. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching, research, industry engagement and academic leadership in areas including communication engineering, network engineering, network security, telecommunications infrastructure, wireless and space communications, 6G and beyond, and advanced communication and networking technologies. We are particularly interested in candidates with strong theoretical foundations and hands-on expertise in the design, development, integration and validation of telecommunications systems, including capability in areas such as software-defined radios, RFSoCs, RF and millimetre-wave systems and devices, high-speed signal processing, embedded system design, network simulators and emulators, network security simulators, and network testbeds such as ORAN. The appointment level will be determined with reference to the candidate’s demonstrated academic achievements, research profile, teaching capability, leadership experience and alignment with the relevant Academic Level C, D or E expectations. To be considered for appointment at Level C, you will have: An emerging nationally recognised research track record in communication engineering, networks and security, 6G and beyond, aerial and space communications, including substantial research outputs in high-quality outlets. Experience in the design and development of research testbeds, integrating hardware platforms and associated software systems to test, validate, and evaluate research outcomes in practical environments. Demonstrated ability to coordinate large courses and deliver high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate teaching, including curriculum development, assessment design and student-centred learning improvements. Experience developing and leading high-quality research projects, attracting external research funding, supervising higher degree by research candidates, and building productive research collaborations. To be considered for appointment at Level D, you will also have: A nationally recognised research track record with a substantial record of research outputs in high-quality outlets and emerging international recognition. Advanced knowledge and experience in the design and development of research testbeds, integrating hardware platforms and associated software systems to test and validate research outcomes, evaluate system performance, and demonstrate engineering concepts in practical and realistic operating environments. Extensive research leadership experience, including the ability to build and mentor collaborative research teams, attract and manage external research funding, and deliver high-quality outcomes. Demonstrated ability to lead advancement in teaching, implement program improvements, contribute to academic governance, and support scholarly development within the discipline. To be considered for appointment at Level E, you will also have: A distinguished national and internationally recognised research profile, with evidence of eminent standing and sustained contribution to the discipline. Extensive knowledge and experience in the design, development, and deployment of research testbeds, integrating hardware and software systems to test and validate research outcomes, demonstrate concepts in practical environments, and advance proposed solutions towards higher Technology Readiness Levels (TRLs). Proven ability to establish, sustain and grow research groups, centres or major research programs through external funding, partnerships and high-impact research outputs. Demonstrated strategic academic leadership, including leading teaching and research excellence, contributing to School, College and University strategy, and influencing the wider professional, industry or community sector. Qualifications: Mandatory for appointment at Level C, D or E: PhD in a related field or approved AQF equivalency with relevant industry experience.   Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.   Department of Electrical & Electronic Engineering The Department of Electrical & Electronic Engineering is one of RMIT’s largest departments, with a strong reputation for research and innovation across photonics, electrification, sensors, electronic manufacturing, power and automation/control, and telecommunication systems and networks. In 2025, the department's research grant income exceeded $17 million, with nearly $65 million secured over the past five years.   The Department leads major research initiatives including COMBS, the D2D manufacturing facility, COMAS and the national centre for electrification, and has strong engagement with defence and industry partners in RF systems, antennas, materials, space and wireless communications. The Department delivers undergraduate and postgraduate programs across electrical, power, control and automation; analog/digital, RF and microelectronics; embedded, computer and software; and communication and networks. The Department also delivers offshore teaching programs in Hong Kong and India and maintains strong industry partnerships across funded research, work-integrated learning, student placements and project co-supervision. To Apply  Submit your CV, cover letter, and a separate document addressing the Key Selection Criteria via the ‘Apply’ link below. In your cover letter, state the academic level you wish to be considered for: Level C, Level D or Level E. If you are open to more than one level, please indicate this clearly. For further information about this position, please see the Position Descriptions hyperlinked below or contact Professor Kandeepan Sithamparanathan via email kandeepan.sithamparanathan@rmit.edu.au   For further information regarding recruitment processes, please contact Jennifer Pham, Senior Talent Acquisition Advisor via email at jennifer.pham2@rmit.edu.au Please do not share your application to this email address.       Position Description – Senior Lecturer (Level C) Position Description – Associate Professor (Level D) Position Description – Professor (Level E) Applications Close: 26 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Head-of-Strategy---Operations_JR51285": {
      "title": "Head of Strategy & Operations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Continuing position 10C + 17% Superannuation and Flexible Working Arrangements Key strategic leadership role based at the Melbourne CBD campus   About the role   The Head of Strategy and Operations, Office of the Vice-President Engagement is a senior leadership role providing strategic and operational leadership to the Office and supporting the effective performance of the broader Engagement Portfolio.   Reporting directly to the Vice-President Engagement, you will act as a trusted strategic adviser and thought leader, providing high-level advice, anticipating emerging issues and opportunities, managing risk and helping shape and advance key Portfolio priorities.   You will lead complex strategic initiatives, cross-functional programs and priority projects, working with senior stakeholders across the University to drive alignment, collaboration and organisational outcomes. Leading a small team, you will also foster a high-performing, collaborative and service-oriented culture, while strengthening governance, systems, operating rhythms and ways of working to support effective decision-making and delivery.   Key Responsibilities   Act as the principal strategic adviser/chief of staff to the Vice-President Engagement, providing high-level advice and insights to support effective decision-making and University priorities. Lead complex strategic projects and cross-functional initiatives, managing risks, dependencies, budgets and delivery outcomes. Lead the Office of the Vice-President Engagement, fostering a high-performing, collaborative and service-focused culture. Contribute to the Portfolio Senior Leadership Team, supporting effective coordination and operations across the Portfolio. Oversee Portfolio planning, governance, performance, risk and reporting, ensuring alignment with strategic priorities. Drive operational efficiency and continuous improvement, including effective business processes, issue resolution and prioritisation. Support financial and resource management, including planning, budget oversight, monitoring and reporting.   To be successful in this position, you’ll have:   Prior tertiary engagement experience including alumni, philanthropy, industry engagement, marketing, communications and student recruitment, in support of the institution’s teaching, learning, research and engagement objectives. Strong experience either as a Chief of Staff or Senior Principle trusted advisor role, offering strategy development and executive support within a complex tertiary education institution. Proven leadership and stakeholder management, with the ability to build high-performing teams, influence outcomes and foster strong relationships. Demonstrated ability to lead complex strategic initiatives, manage competing priorities and deliver outcomes in fast-changing environments. Strong capability across governance, risk, strategic planning, problem-solving and executive communication Relevant post-graduate degree in public policy, MBA or equivalent qualifications and/or demonstrated experience  Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.   About the Portfolio   The Engagement Portfolio actively partners with RMIT's diverse communities to co-create value.  We protect and enhance RMIT’s global reputation, reach and revenue, working collaboratively across Colleges and other Portfolios to deliver the University’s mission and strategic priorities.​   We bring together key functions including current student and staff communications, global marketing, digital experience, global student recruitment, market insights, philanthropy, alumni and industry engagement.    To Apply  Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing the Key Selection Criteria for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.   For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Bianca Jenkins via email bianca.jenkins@rmit.edu.au.    PD Description   Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.     #LI-Hybrid Applications Close: 18 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/VE-Teacher---VE-Teacher--Engineering--Electrical---Telecoms_JR50780": {
      "title": "VE Teacher - Engineering, Electrical & Telecoms",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Continuing position   Salary teacher level T3.1 to T5 + 17% Superannuation   Based at the Melbourne CBD campuses however, but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University   Great benefits such as 17% Super, 720 teaching hours per year, 4 weeks leave + 2 weeks VE Leave, Strong Industry Connections, Value-Led and Inclusive Environment, generous annual, personal and parental leave, Employee Assistance Program, Medical Hub on Campus, Novated Car Leasing, 25% discount on some short courses, personal software discounts, among others     About the position   The VE Teacher – Engineering, Electrical & Telecoms is responsible for delivering high-quality vocational education and training within the engineering discipline at RMIT University. The role focuses on providing industry-relevant teaching and assessment in Electrical Engineering and Telecommunications, supporting students to develop practical skills, technical capability, and professional readiness for the engineering sector.  The successful candidate will be an Engineering professional with qualifications in Engineering or a related field, with preference given to candidates holding a Master’s or PhD qualification. Candidates will demonstrate teaching experience within Higher Education (HE) and/or Vocational Education (VE) environments, with the ability to deliver engaging, student-centred learning experiences.  The position requires the delivery of associate degree in engineering technology and competency-based training and assessment aligned with vocational education standards, including curriculum development, student support, and continuous improvement activities. A Certificate IV in Training and Assessment (TAE40116 or equivalent) is essential for this role. A proof of enrolment is required if Certificate IV in Training and Assessment (TAE40116 or equivalent) is not yet awarded.  The VE Teacher will work collaboratively with academic teams and industry stakeholders to ensure programs remain contemporary, practical, and aligned with industry expectations, contributing to RMIT’s commitment to excellence in applied and vocational education.    To be successful in this position, you’ll have:   Demonstrated skills and experience in grading and competency-based assessment.  Ability in ensuring current and contemporary vocational competence which meets and/or exceeds the education level being delivered and assessed.  Experience in relevant industry, and substantial discipline knowledge as it relates to this position.  Capacity to diagnose learning problems in students, propose and implement effective solutions.  Demonstrated skills in the use of relevant information and communication technologies.  Qualifications   Certificate 4 Training & Assessment (TAE40110 or higher)   Master or PhD in Engineering (preferably)    Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.     To Apply    Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing the Key selection criteria by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.  For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Mykayla via mykayla.mccartin@rmit.edu.au    Position Description -  VE Teacher: Engineering, Electrical & Telecoms #LI-Hybrid  Applications Close: 31 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/First-Nations-Research-Communications-Officer--Identified-_JR50773": {
      "title": "First Nations Research Communications Officer (Identified)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-28\nFull time\n\nOverview: Identified role for Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander candidates Full time, fixed-term position supporting First Nations digital inclusion research Hew 5 ($84,181p.a plus 17% superannuation and cultural leave) Flexible working arrangements, including hybrid working Based at RMIT City campus with some optional travel to research and field sites About the role RMIT University is seeking a creative and self-motivated Research Communications and Engagement Officer to help translate important research into accessible, engaging and culturally respectful communications. Working as part of the research team, you will contribute to the Measuring Digital Inclusion and Mapping the Digital Gap project. This work explores digital inclusion and the digital experiences of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples and communities, helping to communicate research findings in ways that are meaningful, accessible and useful to a range of audiences. Research translation is central to this role. You will turn research insights, data and project activities into clear and engaging content for digital platforms, reports, social media and stakeholder communications. Graphic design is a key part of the position, including creating social media content, reports, promotional materials and data visualisations. You will also help grow and improve the project’s social media presence, particularly across social media platforms , and support the maintenance and development of related digital content and web pages. The role will involve working closely with researchers and the wider ADM+S Centre operations team on project communications, engagement, web content and events. This is a largely self-managed position suited to someone who can work independently, take initiative and manage competing priorities without requiring close supervision. We are looking for someone with relevant communications, engagement or graphic design experiencenwho is passionate about communicating research and creating positive change for First Nations communities. About the project The role will contribute to research focused on measuring digital inclusion and mapping the digital gap, including the Mapping the Digital Gap and First Nations Digital Inclusion projects. For further information, please visit: Mapping the Digital Gap First Nations Digital Inclusion Mapping the Digital Gap on Facebook Key selection criteria Must be of Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander heritage as an essential selection criterion. Demonstrated understanding of the issues affecting Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander people Demonstrated high level ability to communicate sensitively and effectively with Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples Experience or training in communications, graphic design, public relations, engagement or a related field. Demonstrated experience in graphic design, particularly for digital communications, reports, publications or social media. Experience translating complex information, research or data into clear, engaging and accessible content for different audiences. Experience creating and improving social media content, particularly for Facebook and LinkedIn. The ability to develop digital graphics, reports and data visualisations. Familiarity with Adobe Creative Cloud products, particularly InDesign, Illustrator and Photoshop, and with Canva. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate respectfully and effectively with diverse audiences. Ability to work independently, manage your own workload, take initiative and meet deadlines with limited supervision. Ability to work collaboratively with researchers, project partners and the wider operations team. A commitment to culturally respectful and inclusive practice and to communicating research in ways that benefit Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples and communities. Desirable experience Working in an academic, research or community environment. Managing web content, including basic HTML, CSS or SEO Experience with social media reporting, analytics or digital engagement metrics. Experience using data visualisation tools or presenting research findings visually. Photography, filming or basic audio-visual equipment. Experience using Adobe Premiere Pro or After Effects. Qualifications A relevant bachelor’s degree with subsequent relevant experience in communications, public relations and/or engagement, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience, education or training, is required. Position Description Identified position This is an Identified position and being an Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person is considered a genuine occupational qualification in accordance with sections 26(3) and 28 of the Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic). The successful applicant will be required to provide confirmation of their Australian Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander heritage. RMIT is committed to creating a culturally safe, supportive and inclusive environment for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff and students. We warmly encourage applications from people who bring lived experience, cultural knowledge, community connections and a passion for sharing First Nations research and stories in respectful ways. Appointment to this position is subject to holding a valid Victorian Working with Children Check and other checks as required for the specific role. Maintaining a valid Working with Children Check is a condition of employment at RMIT. Applications close 11:59 pm Sunday 18 October 2026 To apply Please submit your CV and a covering letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the Apply link. For further information if required, please contact loretta.vaughan@rmit.edu.au - do not send your application here. Applications Close: 27 Sept 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Social-Media---Community-Specialist_JR51290": {
      "title": "Social Media & Community Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for a creative, strategic and social-savvy Social Media & Community Specialist to shape how our brand shows up online, grow and engage our communities, and create content that connects with prospective students and parents across Facebook, TikTok, Instagram, Threads and emerging platforms.   In line with our current recruitment and selection guidelines, this role is open to Vietnamese candidates only. Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity.   Portfolio requirement: Candidates should submit a portfolio demonstrating social media strategy, content planning, channel growth/community engagement and social content, clearly outlining their role and outcomes for selected examples.   WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.   Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile .   WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for candidates. 13th month bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!   POSITION SUMMARY The Social Media & Community Specialist is responsible for developing and leading RMIT Vietnam’s social media strategy and audience growth across platforms including Facebook, TikTok, Instagram, Threads and emerging social channels.   The role leads the development of engaging, audience-relevant content and social experiences that build brand love, brand consideration and meaningful relationships with prospective students and parents. The role uses audience insights, social listening, platform trends and performance data to shape channel strategy, content direction and continuous optimisation. You will also build and manage a network of content contributors, providing direction, coaching and governance to ensure a consistent, high-quality RMIT social presence. The role works closely with Marketing, Schools and other internal stakeholders to identify opportunities to strengthen RMIT’s presence and relevance in social conversations, while ensuring all activity is aligned with the RMIT brand and broader marketing objectives.   Key Accountabilities summary Social media strategy & channel growth Develop and execute RMIT Vietnam’s social media strategy across Facebook, TikTok, Instagram, Threads and emerging platforms, with a focus on brand love, consideration, audience growth and engagement. Define channel priorities, content pillars and growth opportunities based on audience insights, trends and performance data. Social content planning & creation Lead and develop social content plan, build content direction and initiate ideas for social channels Execute the aligned content plan, producing content from written to video formats Ensure content is relevant to priority audiences and aligned with RMIT’s brand, campaigns and broader marketing objectives. Community engagement & social listening Build meaningful relationships with prospective students and parents through proactive community engagement and social conversations. Monitor and generate social conversations, evaluate audience sentiment and emerging trends to identify brand opportunities and manage potential issues. Performance & optimisation Monitor channel and content performance, audience behaviour and competitor activity, translating insights into recommendations to improve reach, engagement and channel growth. Test new formats, creative approaches and platform opportunities to continuously optimise performance. Contributor network & collaboration Build and coordinate a network of social content contributors, providing guidance, feedback and quality standards to enable authentic and diverse social content. Collaborate with academic Schools and other stakeholders to identify stories and opportunities for social. Key Selection Criteria 4+ years' experience in social media, digital content or a related field, with demonstrated experience developing and executing social media strategies across multiple platforms. Strong experience in social channel strategy, audience growth, community engagement and platform-specific content, particularly Facebook, TikTok, and emerging platforms. Strong creative storytelling through copywriting and short-form video content creation, with a portfolio demonstrating high-quality social content and successful campaigns or channel initiatives. Demonstrated ability to use social media analytics, audience insights and trends to optimise content and channel performance. Experience coordinating, coaching or managing content contributors, creators, agencies or cross-functional teams. Strong stakeholder management, communication, organisation and prioritisation skills, with the ability to manage multiple channels and priorities in a fast-paced environment. Appointment to this position is subject to passing mandatory check. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model.   For full details of the accountability, please refer to the Job Description.   HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the University reserves the right to appoint prior to the closing date.   Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.   RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.   IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at nhu.tranngocquynh@rmit.edu.vn Applications Close: 1 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Assistant-Manager--Tax-Governance---Technology_JR51085": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager, Tax Governance & Technology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for an Assistant Manager, Tax Governance and Technology to support key tax compliance, governance and technology workstreams. The role will work closely with Finance teams and stakeholders to strengthen tax processes, data quality, controls and audit readiness in line with Vietnamese tax regulations and RMIT policies. Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Assistant Manager, Tax Governance and Technology manages key tax compliance, documentation, review and tax technology workstreams that support the effective operation of RMIT Vietnam’s tax function. The role reviews and analyses tax information, coordinates with Finance teams, internal stakeholders, external advisors and other relevant parties, and contributes to the accurate and timely delivery of tax obligations. It also contributes to tax governance, audit readiness, tax data quality, data automation, reconciliation, visualisation and continuous improvement of tax processes, controls, systems and documentation practices in accordance with Vietnamese tax regulations and RMIT policies. Reporting Line  Reports to:  Senior Manager, Reporting and Tax Direct Reports: Associate Director, Finance Reporting lines may be adjusted in line with organisational changes. Key Accountabilities Summary 1. Tax compliance, documentation and review Manage key tax compliance workstreams, including preparation and review of tax calculations, reconciliations, working papers and related tax reporting inputs for applicable tax obligations. Maintain and review tax records, supporting documentation, working papers and tax schedules to support tax filing, internal review, external audit, tax health check and tax authority inspection. Coordinate month-end and year-end tax-related processes, including tax reporting inputs, tax reconciliations, tax provisions and tax-related accounting matters. Ensure confidentiality, accuracy and integrity of tax information, records and supporting documents. 2. Tax analysis and risk identification Review and analyse tax-related data, transactions, supporting documents and reconciliations to identify discrepancies, documentation gaps or tax risk indicators. Prepare tax analysis and supporting information to assist with the review of tax treatments, tax positions and compliance matters within the role’s scope. 3. Tax audit, tax health check and advisor coordination Coordinate information and documentation to support tax audits, tax health checks, regulatory reviews and information requests from external auditors, external tax advisors and relevant authorities. Prepare and maintain tax audit files, reconciliations, supporting evidence, schedules and working papers for assigned tax areas. 4. Tax technology, data quality and process improvement Support tax technology-enabled improvement initiatives, including tax data quality review, compliance trackers, documentation repositories, dashboards, templates and other tools that support tax compliance and audit readiness Use available finance systems, spreadsheets, data tools and templates to support tax data preparation, reconciliation, mapping, exception review and identification of tax risk indicators Work with relevant Finance, systems and process stakeholders to identify practical opportunities to streamline tax compliance activities, reduce manual work, improve tax data visibility and strengthen controls over tax related information. Contribute to the improvement of tax processes, checklists, templates, guidance notes and internal controls to enhance efficiency, compliance, documentation quality and audit readiness. 5. Stakeholder engagement Coordinate with Finance teams, internal stakeholders and external advisors on tax-related matters, information requests, documentation requirements and agreed follow-up actions. Support the implementation of tax guidance, process updates, risk mitigation actions and compliance improvements across relevant Finance and business processes. Key Selection Criteria Demonstrated 5–8 years' relevant experience in tax and/or accounting within a complex organisation, preferably in an international, education, not-for-profit, foreign direct investment (FDI), or multinational environment. Bachelor’s degree in accounting, Finance, Commerce, Taxation, or a related discipline. Professional accounting or tax qualifications (e.g., CPA, CA, ACCA, CTA) are advantageous. Sound working knowledge of Vietnamese tax regulations, financial reporting and compliance requirements, including VAT, FCT, CIT, PIT, tax administration, invoice requirements and supporting documentation principles. Experience preparing, reviewing or coordinating tax calculations, tax returns, reconciliations, supporting schedules, working papers and tax documentation. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to review financial and tax information, identify discrepancies or risk indicators and support practical issue resolution. Experience using financial systems, spreadsheets, tax data, reporting templates, dashboards or data visualisation tools to support tax reporting, reconciliation, analysis and compliance activities. Well-developed organizational and time management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines and deliver accurate work with appropriate attention to detail. Strong communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to work collaboratively with Finance teams, internal stakeholders and external advisors on tax-related matters. Ability to contribute to tax process improvement, data quality review, reporting automation, documentation management and system-enabled compliance initiatives. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. Read more details at Job Description HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 17 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Digital-Learning-Coordinator--Learning-Design--LMS-Administrator-_JR51186-1": {
      "title": "Digital Learning Coordinator, Learning Design (LMS Administrator)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full time, continuing position   HEW 7 ($107,747 - $116,630) + 17% Superannuation   Based at the Melbourne City campus plus hybrid and flexible working arrangements     About the Position   As the Digital Learning Coordinator, Learning Design (LMS Administrator), you’ll play a key role in enhancing the digital learning experience across the College of Business and Law. Working closely with Learning Design, School Operations, Student Experience teams and IT Services, you will lead the administration, coordination and continuous improvement of the College's Learning Management System (Canvas), ensuring high-quality, student-centered learning experiences across multiple programs, cohorts and delivery modes.    This role is responsible for LMS administration, course readiness and governance, supporting successful teaching period go-lives, resolving complex LMS issues, and driving initiatives that improve student engagement, participation and success. You will also provide expert advice, training and guidance to stakeholders while contributing to process improvement, innovation and the adoption of new technologies.    To be successful in this position you'll have:   Demonstrated experience administering Learning Management Systems, preferably Canvas, including course rollovers, enrolments, permissions, integrations and course maintenance.  Proven experience designing, implementing and continuously improving digital learning and student engagement initiatives within a complex organisation.  Strong understanding of LMS governance, service delivery and operational processes, with the ability to manage competing priorities and resolve complex issues.  Highly developed stakeholder engagement and relationship management skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively across academic, professional and technical teams.  Excellent communication, training and influencing skills, with the ability to provide specialist advice and build capability in others.  Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, including the ability to use data and insights to inform decision-making and continuous improvement.  Demonstrated experience driving process improvement, service innovation and the implementation of new technologies and automation solutions.  Relevant tertiary qualifications and/or equivalent experience.      Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.     About the College of Business and Law   Read about the College in the Position Description linked below and visit the College of Business and Law webpage .  To Apply    Please submit your CV and cover letter addressing your interest and suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.     For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Medina via email medina.hubanic@rmit.edu.au .    Position Description    Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.        #LI-Hybrid  Applications Close: 18 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/VE-Teacher--Air-Conditioning-and-Refrigeration_JR50792": {
      "title": "VE Teacher, Air Conditioning and Refrigeration",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Fixed-Term position for 12 months Salary teacher level T3.1 to T5 + 17% Superannuation   Based at the Melbourne CBD or Bundoora campuses however, but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University     We are looking for current or aspiring VE Air Conditioning Teachers who have relevant industry and vocational teaching qualifications, or who are working towards a Certificate IV in Training & Assessment, Cert III and IV in Air-conditioning and Refrigeration, and Full Refrigeration and Air Conditioning Licence.    Great benefits such as 17% Superannuation, 720 teaching hours per year, 4 weeks leave plus 2 weeks VE leave     About the role     As a VE Teacher at RMIT, you will be mainly responsible for delivering course material, assessing students, and supervising students enrolled in selected courses in the schools.   Effective interpersonal and communication skills relevant to teaching and consultancy environments. This includes effective presentation and facilitation skills, and in the use of flexible teaching methods.   Skills and experience in competency-based assessment and ensuring current and contemporary vocational competence meets and/or exceeds the education level being delivered and assessed.   Experience in relevant industry, and substantial discipline knowledge as it relates to this position.   The capacity to diagnose learning problems in students and propose and implement effective solutions.     Qualifications   Certificate IV in Training & Assessment (TAE40110 as a minimum)   Certificate III and IV in Air-conditioning and Refrigeration  Full Refrigeration and Air Conditioning Licence     Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.     To Apply    Please submit your CV and cover letter addressing the Key selection criteria by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.  For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Mykayla via email at Mykayla.mccartin@rmit.edu.au        Position Description - VE Tacher, Air-conditioning and Refrigeration   If you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.      #LI-Hybrid  Applications Close: 31 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Senior-Manager--Process-Improvement_JR51330": {
      "title": "Senior Manager, Process Improvement",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Senior Manager, Process Improvement to lead business process optimisation, system and process improvement, and digital transformation initiatives across the University. This is an exciting opportunity for a strategic and hands-on improvement leader to drive meaningful change, simplify processes, leverage AI and automation, and deliver measurable improvements in productivity, efficiency and stakeholder experience.   WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.   Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile .   WHAT WE OFFER Expatriates Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates Relocation allowance package of US$6,000 Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate and direct dependents (if applicable) International repatriation flights for the staff and direct dependents at the end of their contract. School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to US$20,000 per child or US$40,000 for two children per year. Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Vietnamese candidates Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance   Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!   POSITION SUMMARY The Senior Manager, Process Improvement will lead a newly established team to lead business process optimisation, system and process improvement, and other digital transformation activities within RMIT Vietnam. The role will drive process analysis, stakeholder engagement, workshop facilitation and the development of practical, evidence-based recommendations to improve business performance, consistency and productivity. This role, along with their direct reports and key stakeholders, will identify process pain-points, identify root causes, challenge the assumptions of whether processes are needed at all and then drive improvements through to implementation.   A major focus will be on simplifying processes, reducing the number of manual steps and identifying opportunities to leverage Artificial Intelligence (AI) automation and other technology. The role will suit someone who is comfortable operating with autonomy, influencing stakeholders and talking accountability for outcomes, rather than simply managing a defined set of tasks.     Key Accountabilities summary Lead end-to-end continuous process improvement initiatives from problem identification and root cause assessments, through to implementation, measurement and benefits realisation. Engage collaboratively across key stakeholders and facilitate workshops to identify challenges and opportunities for process improvements. Provide expert advice to senior leaders on operational efficiency and business improvement strategies. Map and redesign end-user journeys, operational processes and workflows. Define project scope, stakeholder engagement plans and any necessary change management plans. Develop and analyse quantitative and qualitative data, such as operational data, productivity metrics and stakeholder insights to identify improvement opportunities. Apply Lean Six Sigma methodologies Challenge existing processes and determine whether activities are genuinely adding value for stakeholders and the organisation. Identify, propose and accelerate AI and Automation opportunities, with consideration of technologies such as workflow automation, robotic process automation, intelligent document processing, low-code solutions and generative AI. Establish and prioritise a pipeline of continuous process improvement initiatives based on stakeholder and organisational value, benefit and operational priorities. Develop and maintain process maps, procedures, workflow documentation, playbooks and supporting materials. Support change management, communication, training and adoption of new or refined process. Manage risk, dependencies and governance requirements for the whole program. Key Selection Criteria Proven experience in continuous process improvement with a demonstration of clear outcomes and business performance improvements, including productivity, quality, risk reduction and improvements to staff and student experiences. Demonstrated experience of leading diagnostic reviews, process mapping, and operational improvement programs. Experience of applying proven continuous improvement methodologies like Lean Six Sigma (formal recognition of Green or Black belt would be desirable). Outstanding stakeholder engagement, facilitation and influencing skills. The ability to translate complex findings into clear, actionable recommendations. Strong analytical and problem-solving capabilities. Experience in governing programs, managing risks and reporting where required. Previous experience in universities or a regulated service industry would be beneficial. High level of curiosity, initiative and resourcefulness. Demonstrated experience in identifying and delivering AI, automation and emerging technologies. Demonstrated success in change management. More information is available in the Job Description .   HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.   Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible.   Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.5 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.     RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.   IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at employment@rmit.edu.vn Applications Close: 1 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Strategic-Creative-Content-Manager_JR51289": {
      "title": "Strategic Creative Content Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for a Strategic Creative Content Manager to lead the strategic planning and direction of content across domestic and international markets. This role will shape our overarching content strategy, set creative priorities, guide audience and channel approaches, and lead a team of content specialists to deliver integrated, high-impact content that strengthens the RMIT brand and supports university goals.   Portfolio requirement: Candidates are required to submit a portfolio or a brief summary of relevant work demonstrating experience in strategic content planning, creative direction and integrated content campaigns.   Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity.   WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile .   WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, career leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!   POSITION SUMMARY The Strategic Creative Content Manager will lead the development and execution of content strategies for both domestic and international markets, working within the university’s marketing department. This role requires a creative and visionary leader who can manage a team of content writers with different expertise, oversee complex projects, and build innovative concepts that enhance the university's brand and engagement across diverse audiences. The Strategic Creative Content Manager will lead creative ideation, oversees content creation across various formats and channels, and tailors approaches for international audiences. The role requires strong collaboration with stakeholders to deliver high-quality content that aligns with university goals.   KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES SUMMARY Develop comprehensive content strategies for both domestic and international markets across all target audience segments (Undergraduate and Postgraduate) for the purpose of both acquisition and brand building, ensuring alignment with the university’s brand, goals, and value propositions. Deliver high quality content from ideation/concept to content production, ensuring the final delivery is appealing and engaging to achieve the communication objectives  Lead the Content team in storytelling for a wide range of formats (brochure, long or short form videos, brand campaigns, social media, etc.) Lead and manage a team of content writers, providing guidance, support, and feedback to ensure high-quality deliverables. Oversee the planning, execution, and monitoring of content-related projects, ensuring they are completed on time and meet quality standards. Collaborate effectively with internal stakeholders within the university to ensure content aligns with broader university strategies and objectives. Ensure all content maintains a consistent voice across languages and channels, adheres to the university's brand guidelines and quality standards, and effectively communicates key messages to various audiences. Conduct market research and analyse trends to inform content strategy and creative direction, staying up-to-date with industry developments and competitor activities.  Proactively build and maintain working relationships with key stakeholders, including external stakeholders, and RMIT senior management. Other duties commensurate with the scope of the role   Key Selection Criteria Tertiary qualification in a relevant discipline Minimum 5 years’ experience in content leadership role, with strong creative vision (content based) Experience in working in a marketing function or organisation with high digital media involvement. Having a fair understanding of the education industry is an advantage. Experience in successfully developing and managing cross-channel content strategies Highly creative in generating ideas for developing a wide range of different content formats, both digital and print Proven experience in creating targeted content that generates measurable ROI Proven planning, organisational, analytical and problem-solving skills with strong project management skills Proven interpersonal, influencing, negotiation, cross-cultural communication skills and strong team leadership Knowledge and commitment to agile ways of working and continuous improvement Proven ability to manage client and stakeholder relationships  Strong expertise in identifying customer drivers, buying and decision-making behaviour  Appointment to this position is subject to passing a mandatory check. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model.   For full details of the accountability, please refer to the Job Description .   HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the University reserves the right to appoint prior to the closing date.   Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.   RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.   IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at nhu.tranngocquynh@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 1 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Campaign-Coordinator_JR50956": {
      "title": "Campaign Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Continuing position Salary Professional Level 6 + 17% Superannuation and Flexible Working Arrangements Based at the Melbourne CBD campus, and hybrid ways of working About You You’re a versatile Marketing professional who knows how to turn audience insights into engaging, effective campaigns. Comfortable working across a range of audience segments, you can quickly adapt your messaging and approach to connect with them. You’ll bring hands-on experience coordinating multi-channel campaigns across digital, social and email, working with internal teams, creative agencies and external partners to deliver high-quality campaigns on time. With strong communication and stakeholder management skills, you’re confident juggling multiple priorities and using data and campaign insights to optimise performance and drive stronger results. To be successful in this position, you will have as a minimum: A tertiary qualification in Advertising, Marketing or a related field. Demonstrated understanding of marketing principles and practice. Demonstrated strong understanding of marketing via digital and social channels. Demonstrated high level of interpersonal and communication skills, including a proven ability to prepare copy for campaign activity including advertising, publications and the web. Demonstrated record of experience in customer service. Highly developed IT skills, including proficiency in Microsoft Office, and ideally experience in Adobe martech stack (including Marketo), Salesforce CRM, and exposure to the Adobe creative suite. An understanding of the marketing and campaign imperatives of a large university or complex business. Proven ability to work independently and as part of a team. Demonstrated experience in briefing content writers, designers and other creative and media suppliers. Email marketing campaign coordination experience necessary and automation experience looked upon favourably. Experience in contemporary and agile ways of working will be looked upon favourably. Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check. About the Portfolio The Engagement portfolio function’s vision is to bring to life RMIT’s strategy by putting the student and all of RMIT’s audiences at the heart of everything that we do and delivering a Customer Experience (CX) vision and insights to help guide the University deliver on our promise. The function is responsible for Global Marketing and our Brand, Digital and CX, Student Recruitment and Admissions, and Market Intelligence and Propositions (product and pricing strategy. The 300+ engagement team who are based across Australia, Vietnam, India and several other hubs, strive to deliver amazing experiences for all our audiences through contemporary ways of working. To Apply  Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page. Please note that applications will be reviewed as they are received. For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Jacqueline Lava, Talent Acquisition Advisor via email jacqueline.lava@rmit.edu.au . Position Description: Campaign Coordinator Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.   #LI-Hybrid Applications Close: 26 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Internal-Communications-Coordinator_JR51339-1": {
      "title": "Internal Communications Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-05\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for an Internal Communications Coordinator to help bring our employee communications to life. Working closely with the Senior Communications Business Partner, you’ll create engaging content across multiple channels, support stakeholders with communications advice, and help connect our people with RMIT’s purpose, priorities and impact across Vietnam and globally.   Portfolio: Candidates are encouraged to include a portfolio or examples of relevant communications work with their application. This may also be requested at a later stage of the selection process.   In line with our current recruitment and selection guidelines, this role is open to Vietnamese candidates only. Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity.   WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.   Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile .   WHAT WE OFFER Competitive gross remuneration package for candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance 20 days annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas break and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!   POSITION SUMMARY Reporting directly to the Senior Communications Business Partner, the Internal Communications Coordinator will support the delivery of the University’s communications to employees in Vietnam. This position will work closely with the Senior Communications Business Partner to deliver and measure impactful internal communications that contributes to the overall RMIT strategy. The position will require engagement across the University, well planned and written creative content and visuals, advising stakeholders on content creation and communications counsel, coordinating delivery across multiple channels and reporting for stakeholder engagement and continuous improvement. Our employees are what makes RMIT such a fantastic University, and so it is critical we foster the passion and engagement of our staff and help them connect the red thread of their work to our purpose and impact globally. The position will work alongside other functions in the University Communications team to share information and collaborate – both across teams and campuses in Vietnam, and with our Internal Communications colleagues in Australia.   KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES SUMMARY Develop and maintain strong collaborative relationships with professional and academic stakeholders in the University across global campuses. Support the Internal Communications team and the wider University Communications team in delivering communications campaigns that align with the Internal Communications Strategy Build regular reports to check success against metrics for all channels, including staff feedback, and look for continuous improvements throughout the cycle. Understand the value of employee engagement and the need to prioritise the leadership team as key stakeholders to help cascade the RMIT Vietnam strategic narrative Work with and brief University Events team in the delivery of effective online, offline and hybrid staff engagement events Communications Development and Delivery Own all existing internal communications channels, including development of content and graphics, and continually monitor and report to look for improvements to the employee experience Develop creative content for communication campaigns, messages, stories, slide packs, cheat sheets, Q&A, speeches etc in a timely manner, of high quality and to stakeholder expectations. Develop internal communication campaigns together with the internal comms team both locally and globally. Provide advice to the Senior Communications Business Partner regarding employee issues and opportunities for communications outcomes and solutions. Work collaboratively with specialists across the UniComms team to ensure a shared outcome. Ensure all internal communication content on University channels are accurate, effective, culturally sensitive, accessible, and conform to RMIT’s communications and branding guidelines. Create and publish updates for staff and students in the event of an Incident Management Team (IMT) or other incident comms. Other duties commensurate with the scope of the role   Key Selection Criteria A tertiary qualification in professional communication, public relations, and corporate communication. At least two years of experience working in a communications environment, with a background in coordinating and delivering communications projects and campaigns across multiple channels, multiple audiences for multiple-level stakeholders. Excellent communication skills, both written and oral, in English and (an advantage) in Vietnamese, being able to tell compelling stories and communicate with employees. Must have sound professional writing and editing skills and a keen eye for detail. Strong organisational and planning skills, along with good stakeholder management and relationship building skills. Ability to collect, analyse and synthesise information into context and deliver solutions. A good team player with ability to work effectively in teams or autonomously. Appointment to this position is subject to passing a mandatory check. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model.   For full details of the accountability, please refer to the Job Description .   HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.   Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the University reserves the right to appoint prior to the closing date.   Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.   RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.   IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at nhu.tranngocquynh@rmit.edu.vn Applications Close: 25 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Segment-Manager_JR50993": {
      "title": "Segment Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-12\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, continuing opportunity HEW 9 + 17% superannuation and flexible working arrangements Based at the Melbourne CBD, with hybrid ways of working   About You Adult learners are at the centre of this role. As Segment Manager, you will own the marketing strategy for this dedicated audience, shaping how prospective adult learners discover, consider and choose their next learning opportunity at RMIT. You will turn audience insight and business priorities into integrated campaigns across media, digital, social, email marketing, guiding activity from initial awareness through to application and conversion.   This is a highly collaborative role for a strategic marketer who understands that adult learners bring different goals, circumstances and decision-making needs to their study choices. You will bring cross-functional teams together, use performance data and attribution insights to improve results, and help grow RMIT's online, face-to-face and hybrid offerings for this audience. It is an opportunity to take on broader leadership, work with new products and make a visible contribution to adult learner acquisition and growth. To be successful in this position, you’ll have: Extensive experience developing audience-led or segment-based marketing strategies in a complex organisation. A strong track record delivering integrated, multi-channel campaigns that support acquisition, or engagement outcomes. The ability to translate market research, audience data, attribution and campaign performance into clear priorities and optimisation decisions. Experience coordinating activity across digital, media, social, email, creative and recruitment or sales touchpoints. Strong stakeholder management and influencing skills, with experience leading cross-functional initiatives without relying on direct authority. Sound commercial judgement and confidence working with marketing technology, campaign measurement, ROI and performance reporting. Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.   About the Portfolio   The Engagement Portfolio provides integrated, strategic leadership across RMIT to advance the University's reputation, reach and revenue. Its work spans domestic and international student recruitment, global marketing and intelligence, strategic communications, advancement, and industry engagement and partnerships.   To Apply   Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page. For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Guy Toogood, Senior Talent Acquisition Advisor via email guy.toogood@rmit.edu.au .    Position Description - Segment Manager   Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.     #LI-Hybrid Applications Close: 25 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Coordinator--Family-Engagement--8-month-contract-via-third-party-_JR51448": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Family Engagement (8-month contract via third party)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT is seeking a Coordinator, Family Engagement (8-month contract via third party) to lead the delivery and continuous improvement of family communications, engagement programs, and community-building initiatives that strengthen connections between families and the University, supporting student wellbeing, engagement, transition, and success across all RMIT Vietnam campuses. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile . POSITION SUMMARY The Coordinator, Family Engagement is responsible for leading the coordination, delivery, and continuous improvement of proactive family communications, engagement initiatives, and community-building activities for families and guardians of RMIT current students across all RMIT Vietnam campuses. The role leads the planning and delivery of family engagement programs and communication initiatives, including events, webinars, publications, and online engagement channels, to strengthen the connection between families and the University while supporting a positive and informed student experience. Working collaboratively with stakeholders across the University, the role contributes specialist expertise and insights to enhance family-inclusive practices, engagement approaches, and service improvement initiatives that support student transition, wellbeing, engagement, and success. The role is expected to exercise sound judgement, manage competing priorities effectively, and contribute to a student-centred, collaborative, and innovative team culture. Key Accountabilities Summary 1. Family Communications and Information Lead the design and delivery of proactive and comprehensive communications across multiple channels for families and guardians of RMIT current students to ensure families remain informed, connected, and better understand the student experience and University initiatives. This includes the coordination and development of family-facing communication resources and channels such as parent guides, newsletters, articles, web content, and other engagement materials. Work closely with Senior Advisors, Family Services and relevant stakeholders to identify enquiry trends, emerging issues, and feedback patterns, and develop proactive communications and information initiatives to address family needs and improve service effectiveness. 2. Family Events and Community Engagement Lead the planning and coordination of proactive family engagement initiatives, including in-person, online and hybrid events and activities (such as Family Welcome Day, Family Weekend, webinars), to strengthen engagement with the RMIT Family Community and enhance the family experience. Coordinate the operational delivery of family engagement events and activities, including stakeholder coordination, communications, budgeting, logistics, and post-event evaluation, ensuring a high standard of participant experience. Collaborate with internal stakeholders including Global Experience, Student Connect, Wellbeing, Library, Academic Schools and other University areas to deliver family engagement initiatives that support student transition, wellbeing, engagement, and success. 3. Projects, Service Improvement and Stakeholder Collaboration Lead or contribute to cross-functional projects and initiatives that enhance the experience, engagement, and support provided to families and guardians of students, including contributing to broader University initiatives such as Orientation and Experience Day. Collaborate with Marketing and relevant stakeholders to ensure aligned messaging, engagement approaches, and family-inclusive practices across communications and engagement activities. Utilise family and student feedback, enquiry insights, and engagement outcomes to inform communication strategies, engagement initiatives, and continuous improvement opportunities that contribute positively to student success and wellbeing. Provide specialist advice and guidance on family engagement practices, communication approaches, and service delivery considerations to support consistent and effective engagement across the University, including contributing to the development of family community of practice initiatives and collaborative engagement approaches. Build and maintain effective working relationships with internal and external stakeholders to support coordinated service delivery, stakeholder alignment, and successful engagement outcomes. Produce and coordinate reports, insights, and recommendations relating to family communication and engagement activities to support service enhancement and informed decision-making. Actively contribute feedback and improvement suggestions to the review of administrative processes, service delivery approaches, and engagement practices through Family Connect team discussions and cross-unit collaboration. Demonstrate a student-centred, collaborative, and innovative approach to continuously enhance the student and family experience. Perform other tasks as assigned by the Manager, Family Connect. Key Selection Criteria A Bachelor’s degree in a relevant discipline. Demonstrated experience in planning and coordinating events, engagement activities, or communication initiatives involving multiple stakeholders and competing priorities. Demonstrated ability to develop and deliver clear, engaging, and audience-appropriate communications across multiple channels for diverse audiences. Demonstrated ability to build and maintain effective working relationships with a diverse range of stakeholders through strong interpersonal, collaboration, and communication skills. Demonstrated analytical, problem-solving, and organisational skills, including the ability to identify trends, develop recommendations, and contribute to service improvements and engagement initiatives. High level written and verbal communication skills in both Vietnamese and English, with the ability to convey information clearly and effectively to different audiences. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively and flexibly in a high-volume, customer-focused environment, while effectively managing competing priorities and deadlines. Demonstrated commitment to continuous improvement, innovation, and student-centred service delivery. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. More information is available in the Job Description . Additional information: Competitive gross salary Contract duration: 8 months Private insurance HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page under your personal email. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 22 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Senior-Account-Payable_JR51025": {
      "title": "Senior Account Payable",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Senior Accounts Payable role is responsible for overseeing end-to-end accounts payable operations, ensuring accurate, timely, and compliant processing of payments, expense allocations, tax obligations, accruals, and financial reporting in accordance with accounting standards, regulatory requirements, and university policies. The position also serves as a key subject matter expert, partnering with stakeholders to resolve complex AP issues, strengthen financial controls, improve processes and systems, and support operational excellence across the University. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile. WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Senior Account Payable is responsible for coordinating and reviewing accounts payable activities to ensure compliance with applicable accounting standards, taxation requirements, regulatory obligations, and University policies and procedures. The role monitors and reviews payment processes to ensure the accurate, timely, and efficient processing of payments to vendors, staff, students, customers, and government authorities. The position also supports continuous process improvement, resolves complex accounts payable issues, and contributes to maintaining effective financial controls and service delivery across the University. Key Accountabilities Summary Stakeholder Management Foster a culture of integrity, accountability, continuous improvement, and high performance within the Accounts Payable function, with a focus on operational excellence, process efficiency, and service delivery. Build and maintain effective working relationships with key internal and external stakeholders, including University staff, suppliers, professional advisors, and relevant counterparts across the broader organisation. Provide specialist advice and technical expertise on accounts payable processes, accounting treatments, and compliance requirements, supporting consistent application of policies, procedures, and relevant legislation. Support the effective operation of the Accounts Payable function by coordinating workflow priorities, providing guidance to team members, and contributing to business continuity and service excellence as required. Pay Process Manage and oversee accounts payable processes to ensure the accurate, complete, and compliant recording of accounts payable and expense transactions in accordance with applicable accounting standards, taxation requirements, regulatory obligations, and University policies and procedures. Review and monitor payment activities to ensure accurate, timely, and efficient payments to suppliers, staff, students, customers, and relevant authorities, while maintaining compliance with legislative and organisational requirements. Provide management and stakeholders with accurate and timely information, reporting, and supporting documentation relating to accounts payable transactions, payment status, and related enquiries. Oversee the delivery of accounts payable support services and enquiry management processes, ensuring responsive, professional, and customer-focused service while maintaining appropriate financial controls and compliance requirements. Provide subject matter expertise on accounts payable processes, accounting treatments, and taxation matters, including the assessment and implementation of appropriate treatment for new or complex transaction types in accordance with relevant accounting standards, legislation, and University policies. Act as a key functional resource for accounts payable systems and related technologies, supporting system administration, process enhancement, user guidance, and continuous improvement initiatives. Contribute to projects, process improvement initiatives, and other duties commensurate with the scope and level of the position. Expense Allocation and Accrual Process Responsible for monthly pre-paid expense allocation processes to guarantee precise and timely recording of university expenses per VAS and AASB. Identify, update, and recommend appropriate allocation drivers for shared activity expenses to enable accurate and full recording and reporting of expenses by cost centre and campus in compliance with VAS, local laws and regulations. Lead year-end and month-end accrual procedures in accordance with VAS and AASB standards. Tax Responsible for compiling the monthly input Value added tax (VAT) invoice list and input VAT section on VAT returns for all campuses, including input VAT allocation as applicable. Ensure proper calculation and withholding of taxes, including but not limited to Foreign Contractor Withholding Tax (FCWT) and Personal Income Tax (PIT) where relevant, prior to payment processing. Ensure account payable transactions are adequately supported by documentation in adherence to local laws and regulations as well as University policies. Reporting Prepare and review accounts payable reporting, expense allocations, amortisation schedules, and related financial analysis to support accurate financial reporting and informed decision-making. Manage intercompany expense reporting and collaborate with relevant counterparties to ensure the accuracy, completeness, and timely resolution of intercompany balances. Monitor and analyse accounts payable trends, balances, and transactions, identifying issues, risks, and opportunities for process and reporting improvements. Provide accurate and timely accounts payable information, reports, analysis, and supporting documentation to management, auditors, tax authorities, and other stakeholders as required. Lead accounts payable reconciliation activities to ensure balances are accurately recorded, fully supported, and reconciled within financial and reconciliation systems, with reconciling items identified and resolved in a timely manner. Control and Compliance Ensure accounts payable transactions, records, and supporting documentation are maintained accurately and in compliance with applicable accounting standards, including VAS and AASB, as well as University policies and procedures. Monitor and review payment and expense documentation to ensure compliance with applicable taxation legislation, regulatory requirements, and internal control standards. Identify opportunities to strengthen accounts payable processes, controls, and service delivery, and lead the implementation of process improvements, system enhancements, and best practices to improve efficiency, compliance, and risk management. Key Selection Criteria Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, Commerce, or a related discipline, with a professional accounting qualification or progress towards such qualification being desirable. Minimum 5 years experience in accounts payable, financial accounting, audit, or a related finance function within a medium to large, complex organisation, preferably within a multinational, education, not-for-profit, FDI, or similarly regulated environment. Strong knowledge and practical application of accounting principles and standards, taxation legislation, regulatory requirements, and internal control frameworks, with the ability to interpret and apply these requirements to complex transactions and business scenarios. Comprehensive knowledge of Vietnamese taxation requirements relevant to accounts payable activities, including Value Added Tax (VAT), Personal Income Tax (PIT), Foreign Contractor Tax (FCT), and Corporate Income Tax (CIT). Demonstrated ability to manage competing priorities, work independently, and exercise sound judgement while contributing effectively within a collaborative team environment. Strong customer service orientation, with a commitment to delivering accurate, timely, and responsive support to stakeholders while maintaining compliance and financial controls. Well-developed interpersonal, communication, and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to build productive relationships, influence outcomes, and resolve complex issues with internal and external stakeholders. Demonstrated experience using enterprise financial systems and reconciliation tools, with the ability to leverage technology to improve efficiency, reporting, and process effectiveness. Experience with ERP platforms such as Workday is desirable. Proven analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify risks, investigate issues, recommend solutions, and contribute to continuous improvement initiatives. Ability to display appropriate behaviors in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. More information is available in the Job Description . HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 29 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Head-of-Health-and-Safety_JR51361": {
      "title": "Head of Health and Safety",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nOverview: ​​Full-time​, ​Continuing position​    10C + 17% Superannuation and Flexible Working Arrangements   Based at the ​Melbourne CBD​ campus, ​and hybrid ways of working​   About Role The Head of Health and Safety position, reporting into the Executive Director, Health, Safety and Risk is a specialist role responsible for managing a range of complex health and safety consultancies covering a wide range of legislation and risks. This role will encompass the management of key projects as identified by respective stakeholders and legislative changes as well as the review, development and implementation of innovative health and safety strategies, policies, and programs.  It is also accountable for the development and delivery of health and safety training packages and information sessions as well as regular reporting, analysis and monitoring of health and safety performance are also key aspects of the role. Responsible for leveraging extensive expertise in leading a comparable function and team, with full accountability for delivering strategic organisational health and safety outcomes through sound and effective decision-making. The role requires the ability to analyse complex organisational health and safety information and demonstrate expertise in the development and implementation of strategic health and safety initiatives aligned with broader people strategy.   To be successful in this position, you’ll have: Strong knowledge of OHS legislation and safety management systems, including psychosocial risk management, biological and radiation safety.   Proven leadership experience growing and nurturing team capability and engagement.  Excellent communication, influencing and negotiation skills, with the ability to drive change and a strong safety culture.   Strong experience delivering health and safety consultancy services within a large, diverse organisation, with ideally some public sector/government and/or Tertiary education sector exposure.  Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to develop practical solutions to complex issues.   Proven ability to build collaborative relationships with internal stakeholders to support business objectives.   Ability to work independently and collaboratively within a client-focused team.   Strong written communication skills, including reports, proposals, policies and audit documentation.  Tertiary qualification in occupational health and safety or a related field, or equivalent education and/or substantial relevant experience.   Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check. About the ​Portfolio​   The Health, Safety & Risk (HSR) team are a team of strategic professionals providing outstanding, client focused, proactive and effective solutions and services for all RMIT staff. Our success is achieved by understanding our business and operating as a business partner to our clients. We deliver responsive, innovative and practical solutions and services. The HSR team operate in a manner that supports the RMIT values and achievement of the business objectives. By providing tailored, quality services and products and ensuring a high level of expert support and advice, the HSR team will enhance College/Portfolio and Groups ability to meet their business objectives. This in turn will allow the University staff to better support the current and future student population at the University. To Apply    Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing ​the Key Selection Criteria​ for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.   For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Bianca Jenkins via email bianca.jenkins@rmit.edu.au.    Position Description Applications Close: 30 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Senior-Manager-Reporting-and-Tax_JR51084": {
      "title": "Senior Manager Reporting and Tax",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking an experienced Senior Manager, Reporting and Tax to lead financial reporting, accounting, tax and treasury functions, ensuring strong financial governance, compliance and effective decision-making across the University. This is a high-impact opportunity to provide strategic financial oversight, strengthen internal controls, and partner with senior leaders, auditors, regulators and RMIT stakeholders in Melbourne. The role will lead a team across financial reporting and tax, driving accurate statutory reporting, tax compliance, financial risk management and continuous improvement of finance processes and systems. This opportunity is open to Vietnamese candidates and can be based in either Ho Chi Minh City or Hanoi.     WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.   Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile .   WHAT WE OFFER Vietnamese candidates Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance   Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!   POSITION SUMMARY The Senior Manager, Reporting and Tax leads the organization’s financial reporting, general accounting, taxation, and treasury functions to ensure accurate, compliant, and effective financial management. The role provides strategic financial oversight, manages financial risks and governance, and partners with senior leadership, internal stakeholders, auditors, and regulatory authorities to support organizational objectives and continuous improvement initiatives.   Key Accountabilities summary   1. Leadership and team management Lead, coach, and develop finance team members to ensure high performance and continuous capability development. Drive continuous improvement and transformation initiatives to enhance operational efficiency and financial effectiveness. Lead and deliver Finance training program for the finance as well as non-finance staff Develop, foster, and maintain strong networks and relationships with key stakeholders, both in country and with RMIT Melbourne 2.    Reporting and treasury Lead and oversee financial reporting, general accounting, tax, and treasury operations to ensure accuracy, compliance, and timely delivery. Manage month-end and year-end financial close processes, statutory reporting (VAS, AASB), and financial statement preparation. Ensure compliance with accounting standards (VAS, AASB), taxation legislation, treasury requirements, and internal financial controls. Manage all activities necessary to fulfill annual VAS and AASB statutory year-end requirements, with the primary goal of achieving a clean audit. Provide strategic financial advice, analysis, and recommendations to support organizational decision-making and financial sustainability. Prepare reports, financial analysis, and presentations for senior leadership, committees, and external stakeholders. Provide strategic advice and guidance on accounting treatment, focusing on compliance and tax minimization. Drive understanding and accountability of financial accounting requirements and compliance across the University Accountable for University’s balance sheet and cash flow statement of annual budget and forecast. Oversee cash flow management, banking relationships, liquidity planning, and treasury activities. Optimize the usage of the University’s cash position to ensure the availability of cash for University operations and obligations while maximizing additional benefits derived from cash surplus for the University. Undertake other duties as assigned by the line manager. 3. Tax planning and Tax Management Manage tax planning and filling of the University to ensure fully optimize the eligible tax incentive for the University while ensure the compliance with tax laws and regulations. Oversea tax reporting ensuring robust control and compliance Manage the tax audit with tax authorities with the goal of achieving clean audit reports Provide strategic advice and guidance on tax treatment, focussing on compliance and tax minimisation  4. Internal Control System: Oversea and execute processes to ensure the integrity of financial reporting, regulatory compliance and prevent fraud. Lead and manage the audit on internal control system on both regular and ad-hoc basic. Ensure that Management and stakeholders are provided with quantitative, accurate and timely report on internal control system for decision making  5. Finance Business System management Lead train the trainer for finance related systems. Manage and execute the visibility and robust control of finance and related business processes via maintain and manage finance related systems enabling robust financial control processes, providing business intelligence capabilities to support the business decision making. Oversea and manage the accuracy and integrity of financial data compiled and recorded against operating activities over its entire life-cycle through information systems and financial controlling processes. Evaluate and provide strategic recommendations for continuous improvement opportunities of finance related systems including but not limited to finance (Workday), student finance management (SAMs), and online payment (Xetta) systems. 6. Control and Compliance Embed financial risk management into the Finance, develop and coordinate the maintenance of the risk register, ensuring that the Executive Team have all relevant information to review significant risks        Identify and take action upon actual or potential risks in the course of operation         Evaluate on a regular basis the effectiveness of relevant processes and controls, and discuss with the management team as necessary         Lead and effectively communicate on compliance with the Financial Procedures Manual, and ensure that all procedures and policies are business-focused. Lead on technical accounting compliance requirements, developing knowledge throughout the organization to ensure compliance and high-quality delivery of service Key Selection Criteria Minimum of 8-10 years relevant experience in financial reporting, general accounting, tax, and treasury management within a complex organization. Minimum 5 years’ experience in similar positions.Relevant tertiary qualification in Accounting, Finance or a related discipline, with CPA/CA/ Master of Finance qualification preferred. Strong knowledge of accounting standards (VAS, AASB, IFRS), taxation legislation, treasury management, financial governance, and regulatory compliance requirements. Demonstrated experience managing statutory reporting, financial close processes, audits, and financial controls. Proven ability to provide strategic financial advice, analysis, and recommendations to senior leadership. Strong experience in cash flow management, treasury operations, and financial risk management. Demonstrated leadership capability, including managing, coaching, and developing high-performing finance teams. Proven ability to improve financial processes, systems, controls, and reporting frameworks to enhance efficiency and compliance. Excellent stakeholder management and communication skills, with the ability to build effective relationships across all organizational levels and with external parties. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills with the ability to manage competing priorities in a complex environment. Excellent in ERP system and finance software. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model.  More information is available in the Job Description . HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note: This is a rolling recruitment process, and the position may close before the advertised closing date. We encourage candidates to apply early. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at employment@rmit.edu.vn Applications Close: 29 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Web-Application-Developer_JR51349": {
      "title": "Web Application Developer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nPart time\n\nOverview: •    Casual hours commencing as soon as possible •    HEW 7 + 12% superannuation •    Based at the Melbourne CBD campus, with flexible working arrangements About RMIT:   RMIT offers life-changing experiences for our students, and helps shape the world with research, innovation, teaching and industry engagement. With strong industry connections forged over 130 years, collaboration with industry remains integral to RMIT’s leadership in education, applied and innovative research, and to the development of highly skilled, globally focused graduates.   About Learning and Teaching:   The Learning and Teaching team works collaboratively to develop and implement innovative teaching strategies, support curriculum development, and uphold high standards of academic quality within the College of Business and Law. By integrating innovative teaching methods, facilitating professional development opportunities, and driving continuous improvement initiatives, LT&Q plays a crucial role in fostering an engaging and effective learning environment. For more information, please visit https://www.learningandteachinghub.com/ About the role:     Activities for this casual role include providing support with conversion of an Excel-based game simulation into a web application. Key tasks may include: Translate the existing Excel-based simulation, game mechanics, investment decisions, scoring and progression into an intuitive, responsive web application. Convert and implement the simulation logic by translating the existing formulas, rules and game mechanics into reliable web-based application logic. Assist learning designers and academics to improve the interface, dashboards and interactive features. Additional duties as required. Skills / Experience: Demonstrated experience developing and deploying web applications. Strong skills in modern web application development, including experience with relevant programming languages, frameworks and development tools. Knowledge of Programming Languages like Javascript and HTML preferred. Experience translating complex business logic, formulas or existing systems into web-based applications. Sound understanding of user experience and interactive interface design. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with non-technical stakeholders. Experience with testing, debugging and maintaining web applications. Reporting Line:   Reports to Senior Learning Designer Engagement Type:   This role is engaged on a casual, as-required basis. There is no guarantee of ongoing or regular work. Hours will vary depending on operational requirements.  Qualifications: A relevant tertiary qualification in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology or Web Development Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children Check. To Apply: Please submit your CV and covering letter by clicking on the ‘Apply’ link below. Please save as a PDF titled with your full name and JR51349, eg. John Smith CV JR51349.  Applications Close: 28 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Platform-Operations-and-Delivery-Coordinator_JR51146-2": {
      "title": "Platform Operations and Delivery Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nOverview: Salary: $110,000 + 12% superannuation  Work in a modern office building in Melbourne’s CBD on Franklin Street, within walking distance of the Queen Victoria Market and close to public transport  Hybrid working arrangements – a mix of work-from-home and office days  Access to benefits including salary packaging, purchase leave, discounted RMIT childcare services, subsidised gym membership, and an Employee Assistance Program (EAP)  Our values: Passion | Impact | Inclusion | Integrity | Courage | Imagination     About RMIT UP   RMIT UP, owned by RMIT University, provides education solutions for students, academics, and professionals in Australia and globally. Our key programs include Informit, Foundation Studies, ELICOS English for Academic Purposes (EAP), language testing.  About I nformit   We are the leading Australian scholarly and education resource for researchers, educators, librarians and learners by supporting the broadest range of publishers and research centres to promote bibliodiversity. We aggregate, organise and host a vast amount of authoritative content and make it accessible through our world class platform.   Founded in the RMIT University Library in 1989, Informit is a business unit within RMIT University Pathways (RMIT UP), Informit’s customers include all Australian and New Zealand university and state libraries, government, and other specialist libraries. With the recent development of our new product, Informit Explore, we are also increasingly present in schools and public libraries. We are committed to promoting publishing diversity, intellectual freedom and critical thinking; with our vision to be the hub of the publishing, research and library communities in Australia and beyond.    About the role    As the Platform Operations and Delivery Coordinator, you’ll play a key role in ensuring the reliable day-to-day operation and ongoing improvements of Informit’s digital platform.  Working closely with the Head of Platform, internal teams and external technology partners, you’ll  coordinate business requirements, testing, release activities, operational monitoring, incident management, content loading and service improvements. Additionally in this role You’ll also support complex customer onboarding and troubleshooting, working across teams to resolve platform, content, access and integration issues. A key part of the role is building strong relationships with vendors and stakeholders, maintaining effective operational processes and documentation, and identifying opportunities to improve the reliability, quality and customer experience of the platform.  This is an opportunity to make a meaningful contribution to the continued development of Informit and its role in connecting researchers, educators, libraries and communities with Australasian scholarly content.    About You    You’re a proactive and adaptable technology professional who enjoys working across people, platforms and processes. You’re comfortable coordinating complex operational and delivery activities, working with technical and non-technical stakeholders, and bringing structure to issues that require investigation, collaboration and follow-through.  You’ll bring:  Experience coordinating technology, platform or digital service operations, including incident management, testing, releases or service improvement.  Strong stakeholder management skills and the ability to build effective relationships with internal teams, vendors and external partners.  Excellent communication and negotiation skills, with the confidence to explain technical issues and requirements to a range of audiences.  Strong project and change management capability, with the ability to balance time, cost, quality and business outcomes.  Advanced digital and technology literacy, with the ability to navigate complex systems and interpret technical information.  A proactive and solutions-focused approach, with the ability to work independently, manage competing priorities and know when to escalate issues.  A commitment to continuous improvement and identifying ways to strengthen operational processes, service quality and customer experience.  Relevant tertiary qualifications in Information Technology, Information Management, Publishing or a related discipline.  Experience working with digital products or platforms, particularly within the information services or publishing sectors, will be highly regarded.     What we offer you    We value our people and are committed to providing a supportive, inclusive, and rewarding work environment. As part of our team, you’ll enjoy:    Exclusive employee discounts at leading retailers.    A strong focus on health and wellbeing, including RMIT-subsidised gym memberships, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) access and discounted childcare options.    Access to professional development training via LinkedIn Learning.   A positive workplace culture with a staff reward program, and a staff wellbeing program.      To Apply     Please submit your CV and a cover letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘Apply’ link. Cover letters should be addressed to HR.   Email HR:  applications.rmit.up@rmit.edu.au  (Please note: Applications will NOT be accepted via this email. To apply, submit your application via our website’s careers page  www.rmit.edu.au/up .)   Please note that we review and interview applications on a rolling basis, so we encourage you to apply as soon as possible rather than waiting until the closing date.   For more details, refer to the Position Description:   https://www.rmit.edu.au/content/dam/rmit/au/en/careers/position-descriptions/pd-platformoperationsanddeliverycoordinator-2026.pdf Pre-employment Checks: Appointment is subject to a successful Working with Children Check and National Police Check.      Our Commitment to Inclusion    At RMIT UP, we foster a culture of safety, wellbeing, and inclusion, ensuring everyone feels valued and respected. We embrace diversity and treat all individuals with fairness, regardless of gender, gender identity, marital or family status, sexual orientation, age, ethnicity, religious beliefs, cultural or socio-economic background, perspectives, or experiences.   We are an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child-safe organisation. We actively encourage applications from all sectors of the community, including Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander candidates.   As a Disability Confident Recruitment Team, we are happy to adjust the recruitment process to meet accessibility needs. Please contact us at  applications.rmit.up@rmit.edu.au  with your preferred communication method, and we will be in touch to discuss your requirements.   Read our Child Safety Policy:  Child Safety Policy    We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to responding to every applicant.   Applications Close: 25 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Hanoi/Officer--Academic-Registrar-s-Group--ARG--Operations-and-Projects_JR51382": {
      "title": "Officer, Academic Registrar’s Group (ARG) Operations and Projects",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for an ARG Operations & Projects Officer to support the delivery of Academic Registrar’s Group services, projects and events at the Hanoi campus. The role will coordinate local operations, administration, stakeholder communication and event logistics, while also supporting key initiatives such as graduation and scholarship ceremonies. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile . WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!   POSITION SUMMARY The ARG Operations & Projects Officer – Hanoi provides operational and administrative support to enable the effective delivery of Academic Registrar’s Group (ARG) services, projects, and events at the Hanoi campus. The role supports the coordination of local ARG operations, including administrative processes, communications, and event logistics, ensuring activities are delivered efficiently and in alignment with established procedures. It contributes to the delivery of key ARG initiatives and institutional events, such as graduation and scholarship ceremonies, with a focus on location-based coordination and execution in Hanoi. Working under the direction of the Manager, ARG, and with day-to-day guidance from the ARG Coordinator, the position supports workflow coordination, information management, and stakeholder communication to ensure consistent and high-quality service delivery. During non-peak ARG periods, the role may provide cross-functional administrative support to Enrolments and Student Records activities in Hanoi, as agreed between relevant managers, while maintaining ARG as the primary function. The role contributes to continuous improvement by identifying operational inefficiencies and supporting enhancements to processes, systems, and ways of working to improve efficiency and service quality. Reporting line: Reports to: Manager, Academic Registrar’s Group Indirectly reports to: Coordinator, Academic Registrar’s Group (ARG) (for day-to-day operational direction and project coordination) Coordination Responsibilities May coordinate and provide day-to-day guidance to casual or temporary staff engaged for ARG activities and events in Hanoi. This does not include formal supervisory or people management responsibility. Key relationships: Academic Registrar’s Group (ARG) teams; Enrolments and Student Records teams (Hanoi); Student Connect; Academic Schools; Student and Education Portfolio (SEP) units; Communications and Events teams; Finance and Procurement; and other relevant internal stakeholders. Reporting lines may be adjusted in line with organisational changes. KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES Provide operational and administrative support to enable the effective delivery of Academic Registrar’s Group (ARG) services, projects, and activities at the Hanoi campus, ensuring tasks are completed accurately and in a timely manner. Coordinate day-to-day ARG administrative processes and workflows in Hanoi, including managing requests, tracking tasks, and supporting efficient and consistent service delivery aligned with established procedures. Support the planning and delivery of ARG projects and initiatives, including graduation and scholarship ceremonies, with a focus on local coordination, logistics, scheduling, and on-the-ground execution at the Hanoi campus. Act as the key coordination point for ARG activities in Hanoi, facilitating communication between central ARG teams and local stakeholders to ensure alignment, timely delivery, and effective issue resolution. Support the preparation, coordination, and dissemination of ARG communications, including student and staff updates, guidance materials, and web content, ensuring information is accurate, accessible, and up to date. Maintain and organise operational records, documentation, and information related to ARG activities in Hanoi, ensuring accuracy, accessibility, and compliance with institutional requirements. Support financial and administrative processes related to ARG operations and events in Hanoi, including processing purchase requests, tracking expenditures, and coordinating with Finance and Procurement in line with established procedures. Collaborate with internal stakeholders across the student lifecycle, including Academic Schools, Student Connect, and Enrolments and Student Records teams, to support coordinated service delivery and effective execution of ARG activities. During non-peak ARG periods, provide cross-functional administrative support to Enrolments and Student Records activities in Hanoi, as agreed between relevant managers, including support for local operational tasks such as student records processing, visa-related administrative activities, or other agreed services. Contribute to continuous improvement by identifying operational inefficiencies and supporting the implementation of practical enhancements to processes, systems, and ways of working to improve efficiency and service quality. Other duties commensurate with the scope of the role   KEY SELECTION CRITERIA A relevant tertiary qualification in business administration, project management, communications, or a related discipline, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience. Demonstrated experience (typically 2–4 years) in administrative, operational, or project support roles, preferably within a higher education or complex organisational environment. Proven ability to coordinate tasks, manage competing priorities, and support the delivery of projects, events, or operational activities in a structured and timely manner. Strong organisational skills and attention to detail, with the ability to manage information, documentation, and processes accurately across multiple activities. Effective communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work collaboratively with a range of stakeholders and support clear and consistent information flow. Experience supporting the coordination of events or activities, including logistics, scheduling, and administrative processes, preferably in a multi-stakeholder environment. Demonstrated ability to adapt to changing priorities and support different operational areas as required, including the ability to provide cross-functional administrative support when needed. Familiarity with administrative and financial processes, including purchase requests, expense tracking, and coordination with finance functions. Proficiency in Microsoft Office and experience using enterprise systems, databases, or digital tools for administrative and operational purposes. Demonstrated commitment to service quality, teamwork, and continuous improvement. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model.     HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 5.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 26 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Digital-Coordinator_JR51324-1": {
      "title": "Digital Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Continuing position Salary Level HEW 6 + 17% Superannuation Based at the Melbourne CBD campus, and hybrid ways of working   About the role As Digital Coordinator, you will contribute to the success of the RMIT Strategy by delivering a timely, well-managed digital publishing service that meets best practice across RMIT. This will support an effective, engaging platform that creates transformational experiences for users as they access information, engage with RMIT, and collaborate to deliver business results.   This role is part of a small, dynamic and creative team who deliver university-wide governance, content architecture, planning and publishing services for RMIT websites. You will coordinate, produce content, edit, publish and test web content to ensure web content is up to date.   Experience in web design as well as understanding of accessibility and usability of websites are essential along with the ability to work closely with a range of stakeholders.   To be successful in this position, you will have: Experience in content authoring, editing and publishing (including knowledge of SEO, accessibility, usability, writing for web best practices and technical issues). Strong web design and development knowledge as well as experience using Adobe Experience Manager (AEM) content management system. Demonstrated experience in using Analytics and tagging software. Experience in Adobe Customer Journey Analytics will be preferred. Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills are essential as this role will work closely with a range of stakeholders and enhance their understanding of digital and search. Ability to understand and translate complex information into simple yet engaging content that appeals to a range of audiences.   Qualifications Industry certifications and experience in Adobe Experience Manager (AEM) and training preferably within large, complex knowledge-based organisations. Degree in a marketing, communications, IT or multimedia discipline or an equivalent combination of relevant experience, education and/or training.   Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.   About the Portfolio The Engagement Portfolio provides integrated, strategic leadership across the University to advance RMIT’s reputation, reach, and revenue, encompassing a range of functions, including domestic and international student recruitment; global marketing and intelligence; strategic communications; advancement function that includes donor relations, philanthropic advancement; and industry engagement and partnerships.   The portfolio leads the development and execution of major fundraising campaigns aligned with institutional priorities and stewards high-value partnerships with industry, government, and community to generate measurable impact. It enables data-informed decision-making through market insights to support integrated operations, strengthen relationship management, and enhance performance reporting.   Through innovation, collaboration, and strategic partnerships, the Engagement Portfolio plays a critical role in diversifying revenue streams and expanding RMIT’s presence in alignment with its long-term strategic objectives.   To Apply  Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.   For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Anna Burke (Senior Manager Digital Experience) via email anna.burke@rmit.edu.au . Please do not send your application to this contact.   Position Description – Digital Coordinator   #Li-Hybrid Applications Close: 20 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Program-Manager--Campus-Development_JR51082": {
      "title": "Program Manager, Campus Development",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking an experienced Program Manager, Campus Development to help shape the future of its campuses and learning environments. This is a high-impact opportunity to lead the delivery of major capital projects from feasibility and design through construction, commissioning and handover, bringing ambitious campus development plans to life. Working across senior leaders, academic and professional stakeholders, designers, consultants and contractors, the role will ensure projects are delivered safely, sustainably and to the highest standards — creating exceptional environments that enable students and staff to learn, work and thrive.     WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.   Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile .   WHAT WE OFFER Vietnamese candidates Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance   Expatriates Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates Relocation allowance package of US$6,000 Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate and direct dependents (if applicable) School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to US$20,000 per child or US$40,000 for two children per year. Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!   POSITION SUMMARY The Program Manager, Campus Development plays a key project leadership role within the infrastructure program delivery function and leads the strategic planning and end‑to‑end delivery of assigned major capital projects across RMIT Vietnam. The role is the single point of accountability for project scope, schedule, budget, risk, safety, quality and stakeholder engagement at the project level, operating within the program governance, commercial and risk frameworks set by the Associate Director, Infrastructure Program Delivery.   Working closely with the Associate Director, Infrastructure Program Delivery, campus users, academic and professional stakeholders, PM consultants, designers and contractors, the Senior Project Manager ensures projects support campus masterplans, are delivered safely and sustainably, and are smoothly transitioned into operational use in alignment with program‑level objectives and delivery frameworks.      Key Accountabilities summary   Project Leadership and Governance Define and control project scope, objectives, budgets, schedules and risk management plans for assigned campus development projects in line with the capital program and governance frameworks established by the Associate Director, Infrastructure Program Delivery. Establish and maintain project governance structures and reporting processes that align with infrastructure program delivery requirements and RMIT's capital planning and investment frameworks. Prepare and present project level business cases, feasibility and options analyses, progress reports and approval papers to internal governance forums and senior leadership, providing clear inputs to program level decision making led by the Associate Director, Infrastructure Program Delivery. Act as the primary point of accountability for overall project outcomes, including the performance of external PM consultants, design teams and contractors, with escalation of strategic, commercial or program wide issues to the Associate Director, Infrastructure Program Delivery. Planning, Design and Buildability Lead planning activities across feasibility, concept and schematic design stages, ensuring alignment with campus masterplans, user requirements and budget constraints. Review design documentation for buildability, operational and safety impacts, and lifecycle implications, ensuring designs are practical, maintainable and safe. Ensure design processes incorporate resilience, flexibility and high‑quality workplace and learning environments for staff and students. Ensure project level risks, constraints and opportunities are identified and fed into program level risk management and reporting processes. Delivery and Performance Management Plan, procure and manage consultants and contractors required to deliver assigned projects, following RMIT procurement policies and delegated authorities within the Infrastructure Program Delivery portfolio. Monitor construction progress, quality, safety, risk and cost performance against approved baselines, and report variances, forecasts and mitigation plans to the Associate Director, Infrastructure Program Delivery. Chair project meetings, manage interface issues and coordinate activities between internal stakeholders, external PM consultants, designers, contractors and authorities. Prepare regular project status reports, dashboards and briefs to support program level reporting to executive leadership and governance forums. Commercial and Contract Management Manage project budgets, contingency and cashflow forecasts within approved limits and within the overall capital program parameters set by the Associate Director, Infrastructure Program Delivery. Oversee the administration of project contracts, including variations, claims assessment, progress payments and commercial negotiations in accordance with RMIT policies and program level commercial strategies. Identify and manage project specific commercial and contractual risks and escalate material issues that may impact the broader portfolio to the Associate Director, Infrastructure Program Delivery. Operational Readiness and Handover Plan and manage project level commissioning, testing, defects rectification and handover activities to ensure assets are ready for occupation and use. Coordinate with Campus Operations, ICT, OH&S and other service units to ensure smooth transition from construction to operations and to align project handovers with program level campus activation plans. Ensure all as built documentation, warranties, O&M manuals and asset data are compiled and handed over in accordance with RMIT requirements. Sustainability and User Experience Embed sustainability and environmental best practice into planning, design and delivery, consistent with RMIT’s sustainability commitments and rating tools where applicable. Ensure campus developments provide safe, accessible and high quality environments that enhance student and staff experience. Stakeholder Engagement and Reporting Develop and maintain strong relationships with internal stakeholders (academic units, professional services, Campus Operations) and external stakeholders (authorities, landlords, consultants, contractors) for assigned projects. Lead project level stakeholder engagement, including briefings, consultation sessions and issue resolution forums, ensuring stakeholder needs and constraints are incorporated into project plans. Prepare and deliver clear project level communications (updates, notices of works and disruptions, briefing materials) in alignment with program level communication strategies set by the Associate Director, Infrastructure Program Delivery. Escalate complex stakeholder issues and risks with broader program implications to the Associate Director, Infrastructure Program Delivery. Leadership and Collaboration Provide day to day leadership and mentoring to Project Coordinators and project team members, aligned with the direction, performance expectations and delivery culture set by the Associate Director, Infrastructure Program Delivery. Foster a culture of safety, collaboration, accountability and continuous improvement within project teams. Contribute to the development and continuous improvement of project and program delivery processes, tools and templates across the Infrastructure Program Delivery function. Key Selection Criteria Relevant postgraduate qualification in Architecture, Engineering, Construction, Project Management, or a related discipline; or equivalent relevant experience. Extensive experience (typically 8–10+ years) successfully delivering large scale and complex infrastructure projects from inception to completion in commercial or institutional environments. Proven capability in procurement and commercial management, including development of procurement strategies, tendering, contract negotiation and administration. Strong experience in applying project management principles across planning, resource allocation, communication, documentation, implementation, evaluation and reporting. Demonstrated track record of delivering projects within agreed time, cost and quality parameters while managing complex risk and stakeholder environments. Sound understanding of OH&S, statutory, environmental and sustainability requirements in construction, including experience with high risk work controls and safety documentation. Excellent organisational and planning skills, with the ability to see the “big picture” while managing detailed project controls. Strong stakeholder management skills, with the ability to influence, negotiate and achieve business outcomes with diverse internal and external stakeholders. Experience with digital project management tools and collaboration platforms; experience with CAD is an advantage. Professional memberships and/or certifications (e.g. PMI, AIPM, RICS, Green Star/LEED) are desirable. Demonstrated alignment with RMIT Values and leadership behaviours.   More information is available in the Job Description .  HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note: This is a rolling recruitment process, and the position may close before the advertised closing date. We encourage candidates to apply early.  Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 6.5 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.   RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means.RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply.For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at employment@rmit.edu.vn Applications Close: 5 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Associate-Learning-Designer-----06-roles---Third-Party-Contract-_JR50647-2": {
      "title": "Associate Learning Designer -  (06 roles & Third-Party Contract)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-16\nFull time\n\nOverview: ***3-month third-party contract *** RMIT Vietnam is seeking a contingent worker for the Associate Learning Designer . While the position is advertised by RMIT Vietnam, the successful candidate will be employed and managed by an external service provider, who will be responsible for the labour contract. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile . POSITION SUMMARY The Associate Learning Designer supports the Learning Design team to create engaging online and blended learning experiences in the Learning Management System (Canvas) as part of a new digital uplift project. The Associate Learning Designer will work closely with the Learning Designers, Senior Learning Designers and Multimedia Designers to co-design blended learning experiences that are Active, Authentic and Applied. Reports directly to: Manager, Online Learning KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES Partner with academic stakeholders to influence and guide best-practice course design and facilitation skills for blended and online learning. Champion and ensure that all content adheres to RMIT VN learning design, UX, accessibility, copyright, and style guide standards. Interpret and make sense of advanced academic content to design learning sequences and activities that support the achievement of learning outcomes Design and build learning experiences through an inclusive design lens, ensuring content is representative, equitable, and accessible to a diverse student cohort. Construct learning experiences that actively promote interaction, social presence, and community among students and between students and faculty. Leverage AI tools and emerging technologies within learning design workflows to enhance operational efficiency and develop innovative instructional assets. Ensure all digital content and sequences directly support student achievement of defined course outcomes. Use a range of authoring and multimedia tools to build out complex learning sequences within the Canvas LMS. Build and format LMS pages using HTML, including the setup of course shells, assignments, and structural elements according to the style guide. Apply rigorous standards to all digital content to ensure WCAG 2.0 AA compliance. Carry out other duties as required to support the University’s evolving needs. KEY SELECTION CRITERIA Minimum bachelor’s degree in a field related to Education, Communication, Design, or Technology. Knowledge of pedagogical principles within higher education, specifically relating to blended, online, and inclusive learning design. Proven stakeholder management skills with the ability to build rapport and influence stakeholder behaviour to achieve high-quality educational outcomes. •Advanced English communication skills (written and spoken) with the ability to make sense of complex academic content and articulate design concepts clearly to non-experts. Familiarity with a range of learning management systems (ideally Canvas) and learning technologies. Basic to intermediate knowledge of HTML and CSS is an advantage. A proactive attitude with a demonstrated ability to pick up new ideas, AI tools, and emerging technologies quickly. Ability to collaborate effectively with peers and academic stakeholders, including the capacity to give and receive constructive professional feedback. Ability to work independently, show initiative, and manage tasks effectively to meet project deadlines. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the RMIT Behavioural Capability Framework (Connectedness, Commitment to Excellence, Imagination and Innovation, Impact, Inclusion, and Agility). Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, as per the RMIT Behavioural Capability Framework (Connectedness, Commitment to Excellence – Improve and Simplify; Imagination and Innovation;Impact; Inclusion; Agility). Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. Additional Information Contract duration: 03 months Working location: Saigon South Campus Highly competitive gross salary Annual leave: 1 day per working month Private Insurance Online library and supportive and collaborative environment that encourages professional growth and development HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS General 6.0 (or equivalent CEST 150).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process To be eligible for this position you must be a Vietnamese citizen .  Applications received from non-Vietnamese candidates will not be considered. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 21 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Senior-Policy-Advisor_JR50738": {
      "title": "Senior Policy Advisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, 12 Month Fixed Term Opportunity $121,213 - $136,507 + 17% Superannuation and Flexible Working Arrangements Based at the Melbourne CBD, and hybrid ways of working   About You Are you a policy professional who enjoys bringing structure, clarity and momentum to complex organisational challenges? In this role, you'll work at the centre of university governance, leading and supporting high-profile policy projects with impact across RMIT and the broader higher education sector. You'll partner with policy custodians, subject matter experts and senior stakeholders to develop, review and implement policy frameworks, facilitate working groups, coordinate consultation activities and guide complex initiatives through governance and approval processes. From shaping policy responses to emerging sector issues through to supporting major governance uplift initiatives, you'll play a key role in ensuring policy outcomes are practical, compliant and fit for purpose.   This opportunity will suit someone who thrives in a complex and highly regulated environment and enjoys managing policy work from concept through to implementation. You'll bring strong policy development and governance experience, the ability to build credibility with executive stakeholders, and the confidence to navigate competing priorities while maintaining momentum across multiple projects. In return, you'll gain exposure to nationally significant policy initiatives, work alongside a collaborative and supportive team, and further develop your strategic policy capability through diverse and challenging work that influences decision-making across the University. To be successful in this position, you’ll have: Strong experience in enterprise policy administration and policy development within a large, complex or highly regulated environment. A sound understanding of document hierarchies and how policy frameworks support strategic, operational, governance and regulatory objectives. Demonstrated experience managing complex policy projects independently, from initial scoping and consultation through to approval and implementation. Strong facilitation and stakeholder engagement skills, including experience working with policy custodians, subject matter experts, working groups and senior stakeholders. Excellent policy drafting, review, interpretation and analytical skills, with strong attention to detail. The ability to manage multiple competing priorities while maintaining project milestones, reporting requirements and policy review deadlines. The confidence to navigate complex or ambiguous issues, negotiate outcomes and provide practical policy and governance advice. Experience in tertiary education, government or another regulated sector. Experience developing policy frameworks or leading high-profile policy initiatives will be highly regarded.   Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.   About the Portfolio   The Office of the Vice-Chancellor Portfolio supports the Vice-Chancellor and President and provides specialist strategic advice and oversight across enterprise governance, compliance, policy, regulatory and student lifecycle functions. The University Secretariat and Academic Registrar's Group is responsible for governance, compliance, regulatory and student lifecycle activities across RMIT's Australian and international operations. The Central Policy function sits within this group and supports the development, review and governance of University policy documents.   To Apply   Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page. For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Sarah Davis, Manager Central Policy - sarah.davis@rmit.edu.au   Position Description - Senior Policy Advisor Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.     #LI-Hybrid Applications Close: 1 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Research-Fellow-in-Ecology-and-Restoration-Modelling_JR51230": {
      "title": "Research Fellow in Ecology and Restoration Modelling",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nPart time\n\nOverview: 1 x part time (0.8 to 0.85FTE), fixed term (until 30th of June or 30 July 2028) position available in the School of Science Salary Academic Level B ($119,915 - $142,402)  + 17% Superannuation Based at the City, but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University     About the Role   As a Research Fellow, you will work collaboratively with research teams and strategic partnerships across the School and Research Institutes to deliver high-quality research aligned with the University's research strategy and focus areas. The role involves planning, developing and undertaking independent and/or team-based research that contributes to advancing knowledge within your area of specialisation and supports outcomes with national impact and recognition. You will play a key role in designing and delivering research projects, building productivity-driven research networks across RMIT and with local and national partners, and embedding research expertise into the broader life of the School. The successful candidate will contribute to high-quality research outputs, engage in collaborative research initiatives, and support the growth of research funding opportunities through the development of strong internal and external partnerships. This position is well suited to a researcher who can work both independently and collaboratively, contribute to impactful research programs, and support the University's commitment to research excellence and innovation.   About You Key Selection Criteria Experience in ecological modelling, biodiversity and restoration modelling, and/or hydrological modelling. Fieldwork experience and driver’s license. Experience in coastal wetlands is preferred, but experience in other natural ecosystems is acceptable. Emerging track record and recognition for quality research outputs, including Q1 peer-reviewed publications. Evidence that the applicant will contribute to existing Discipline and School research areas evidenced, e.g. publications, development of new research initiatives, competitive research funding, and industry links. Demonstrate capacity to develop high-quality research ideas, while working independently and within teams. Ability to build effective networks with colleagues and generate alternative funding projects through effective liaison with industry and government. Excellent interpersonal and communications skills appropriate for interacting with higher degree by research candidates, staff and industry, together with a strong commitment to teamwork and multidisciplinary collaboration. Desired: Demonstrated ability to supervise higher degree by research candidates.     Qualifications: PhD or equivalent in relevant field   Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.   To Apply    Please submit your CV and covering letter and address the Key Selection Criteria for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page. If you have any role related questions, please connect with Dr. Stacey Trevathan-Tackett at stacey.trevathan-tackett@rmit.edu.au     Position Description - Research Fellow, Ecology and Restoration Modelling   Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.   Applications Close: 4 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Creative-Service-Lead--Vietnam-_JR50967": {
      "title": "Creative Service Lead (Vietnam)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Creative Service Lead to drive the quality and consistency of our creative output across Vietnam. This role will lead a multidisciplinary design team, strengthen creative delivery, and help turn ideas into compelling, on-brand work that supports our engagement priorities. Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile . WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration package for candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health Insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Creative Service Lead supports the delivery of high-quality and consistent creative outputs for the Vietnam Marketing, Communications, and University Event teams (called Vietnam Engagement stakeholders). Reporting to the Creative & Production Manager, this role leads the day-to-day graphic design function, supervises a team of designers across multiple disciplines, and ensures projects are delivered effectively, on brand, and aligned with business objectives. The position also supports workflow coordination, stakeholder collaboration, and continuous improvement of creative processes within the Vietnam team. KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES SUMMARY 1. Creative Delivery & Brand Management Lead the delivery of graphic design outputs across RMIT Vietnam marketing, communications, and event team Provide creative direction and feedback to designers across projects to ensure creative outputs well deliver the stakeholder briefs and aligned with RMIT brand guidelines and quality standards. 2. Team Supervision & Development Supervise and support a team of graphic, brand, motion graphic, and digital designers Allocate work and monitor team workload and delivery timelines Coach and develop team capability through regular feedback and guidance Foster a positive, collaborative, and creative team culture that encourages motivation, innovation, and continuous growth. 3. Stakeholder Management & Collaboration Partner with Marketing, Events, and Communications stakeholders for an effective workflow Manage project briefs, priorities, and delivery expectations Coordinate effectively with internal teams and external suppliers where required. 4. Workflow, Quality assurance & Continuous Improvement Support the implementation of creative workflows and approval processes Closely monitor project progress and ensure timely delivery of outputs Identify opportunities to improve team efficiency, creative quality, and collaboration Stay updated on design trends, tools, and creative best practices. Other duties commensurate with the scope of the role Key Selection Criteria Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field Strong creative thinking and visual storytelling capability, with the ability to develop concepts from idea to high-quality execution. Demonstrated strong expertise in graphic design across digital, print, campaign, and event collateral. Strong eye for layout, typography, branding, composition, and visual consistency. Proven experience with at least 3 years in leading or supervising design teams in a fast-paced environment Ability to provide clear creative direction, constructive feedback, and mentoring to designers. Strong collaboration and stakeholder management skills Advanced proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite and other relevant creative tools. Strong project management and organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Passion for design excellence, innovation, and continuous improvement. Ability to foster a positive, motivated, and collaborative creative team culture. Strong interest in emerging AI and creative technologies, with the ability to leverage AI tools to enhance creative ideas and team efficiency. Appointment to this position is subject to passing mandatory check. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. For full details of the accountability, please refer to the Job Description . HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the University reserves the right to appoint prior to the closing date. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at nhu.tranngocquynh@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 1 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Digital-Marketing-Coordinator_JR51353": {
      "title": "Digital Marketing Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for a Digital Marketing Coordinator to support the management and optimisation of our digital channels. In this role, you will work with stakeholders across the University to manage website content, improve user experience, and support digital marketing activities.   In line with our current recruitment and selection guidelines, this role is open to Vietnamese candidates only.   Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity.   WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.   Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile .   WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for candidates. 13th month bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!   POSITION SUMMARY The Digital Marketing Coordinator is responsible for managing task requests, content optimisation and publishing for the portfolio and relevant University stakeholders. Digital Marketing Coordinator will advise on content management, best practice web guidelines, implementation of the adobe-marketing suite to improve user experience on RMIT digital assets, web statistics analysis and search engine optimisation under supervision.  It is also this role’s responsibility to maintain and update best practice content on the website that is simple, accessible and helps achieve acquisition targets as well as enhance customer experience under supervision.   KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES SUMMARY Be part of a team of motivated, engaged and professionals who are proactive advisors and deliver outstanding digital support to the university through industry-leading web capability, delivery agility and a team culture. The Digital Marketing Coordinator is the main point of contact for RMIT web enquiries for public site web publishing enquiries.    Manage, priorities and complete content change requests with management of stakeholder relationships.  Manage the work queue and BAU publishing on RMIT public and staff website.  Undertake content remediation, including content archiving and deletion, content mapping and content improvement.  Role model the RMIT values and be an active member of the Web team. Provide support and guidance to other members of the Web team Marketing and Content Architecture and Management Coordinate with internal stakeholders to ensure content quality, relevance and accuracy; Maintain and improve working processes and Web guidelines; Provide best-practice advice and training to a range of internal stakeholders; Participate in the delivery of web projects, new initiatives, supporting key stakeholders across the university. Coordinate, publish, test and optimise the public website content to improve user experience and ensure that content remains up to date. Develop new marketing content whilst following RMIT guidelines and policies; digital best practices, digital accessibility, information architecture, as well as user and customer experience digital best practices. Continuously suggest marketing content improvement based on customer insights; Undertake content remediation, including content archiving and deletion, content mapping and content improvement. Improve RMIT Vietnam website for Search Engine Optimisation. Assist with performance marketing and event team landing page builds and optimisation for paid campaigns. Project management of small web team projects Monitoring and Evaluation and reporting Monitor customer journey and measure outcome based on agreed goals and KPIs; Produce concise analytical reports, and advise of new approaches to enhance customer experience through RMIT Vietnam Website; Provide data insight to optimize online promotion activities and campaign performance; Provide other support as defined by the Marketing Web Manager. KEY SELECTION CRITERIA Tertiary qualification in relevant disciplines and/or relevant work experience.  Experience in content authoring, editing and publishing (knowledge of accessibility, usability, writing for web guidelines, SEO and technical issues is well-regarded).   Experience with content management systems (AEM preferred but not essential)  Demonstrated experience in digital editing and web publishing (including knowledge of SEO, analytics, writing for web principles, accessibility, usability and technical issues)  Experience building and maintaining effective and productive stakeholder relationships Demonstrated experience in understanding and reporting on site performance and analytics   Demonstrated ability to apply policies, procedures and systems.  Demonstrated experience in coordination of digital projects and campaigns including planning, communication, implementation, evaluation, and reporting.  Demonstrated ability to work independently as well as in a team environment to achieve objectives within complex organisational structures.  Understanding of digital planning, delivery and measurement that contributed to organisational objectives. Understanding of new media and digital technology to improve outcomes. Appointment to this position is subject to passing mandatory check. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model.   For full details of the accountability, please refer to the Job Description. HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.   Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the University reserves the right to appoint prior to the closing date.   Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.   RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.   IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at nhu.tranngocquynh@rmit.edu.vn Applications Close: 18 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/EOI---VE-Teachers--Electrical_JR46931": {
      "title": "VE Teachers, Electrical",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nFull time\n\nOverview: Fixed-Term and casual positions RMIT College of Vocational Education – Bundoora Campus   Why work at RMIT? Great benefits, 720 teaching hours per year, 4 weeks leave + 2 weeks VE Leave and 17% Super, Strong Industry Connections, Value-Led and Inclusive Environment   We are seeking expressions of interest for current or aspiring VE Teachers, Electrical who have relevant industry qualifications and vocational teaching qualifications OR currently obtaining a Certificate IV in Training & Assessment and Cert III and IV in Electrical. Benefits working at RMIT - CoVE: 720 teaching hours per year, 4 weeks leave + 2 weeks VE Leave and 17% Super (fixed-term and Ongoing contracts). Trades Program Area Electrical & Instrumentation About the role    As a VE Teacher at RMIT, you will be mainly responsible for delivering course material, assessing students, and supervising students enrolled in selected courses in the schools.  Effective interpersonal and communication skills relevant to teaching and consultancy environments. This includes effective presentation and facilitation skills, and in the use of flexible teaching methods.  Skills and experience in competency-based assessment and ensuring current and contemporary vocational competence meets and/or exceeds the education level being delivered and assessed.  Experience in relevant industry, and substantial discipline knowledge as it relates to this position.  Relevant Qualifications - Certificate 4 Training & Assessment (enrolled or finished) as a minimum and relevant trades qualifications & licenses.   The capacity to diagnose learning problems in students and propose and implement effective solutions.  Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.   About The College of Vocational Education    The purpose of RMIT’s College of Vocational Education is to empower learners and our industry, community and government partners to succeed in the new world of work. Our five-year strategic roadmap, ALiVE@RMIT, purposefully guides everything we do in vocational education to deliver our vision: to position RMIT as a leading multi-sector provider with global impact and influence. Led by our Deputy Vice Chancellor, the College of VE is reimagining how we deliver vocational education to create unique experiences for our students and partners, so we can: •            lead in practice-based learning •            empower learners for the future of work •            engage industry and community at scale •            grow for impact and influence  The College of VE is delivering impact through transformation that creates long-term change. To register your interest, please submit your resume by clicking on the ‘Apply’ link. For further information please contact Mykayla via email at mykayla.mccartin@rmit.edu.au Position Description - VE Teacher, Electrical RMIT reserves the right to remove this job posting at any time. If you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.   Applications Close: 11 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Research-Assistant---Phenology_JR51198": {
      "title": "Research Assistant – Phenology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-14\nPart time\n\nOverview:   1 x part time (2 days per week), fixed term (until 30th of June 2029) position available in the School of Science    Salary Academic Level A ($83,985 - $113,917)  + 17% Superannuation pro rata   Based at the City, but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University      About the Role     This role supports the Australian Research Council (ARC) Discovery Project, Tracking Phenology Changes Linked to Climate Change and Biodiversity Loss , funded through to June 2029.  Working closely with the Phenological Data Specialist and Project Leader, you will enter historical phenological data into the project's database; including reading and interpreting historical records such as naturalists' diaries. You will be responsible for coding data, checking for errors and missing information using appropriate quality control methods, and mapping phenological observation locations.  The role also involves retrieving, confirming and updating data in storage, maintaining records of data input, and contributing to the achievement of project milestones and goals. You will work collaboratively with the Project Leader and other members of the research team, including the Phenological Database Manager and Higher Degree by Research candidate, to support the successful delivery of the project.    About You   Essential:   Demonstrated ability to accurately enter, code and interpret data from historical and varied source records (e.g. Naturalists' diaries) into a structured database in a required format.  Demonstrated strong computer literacy, including the ability to navigate and work within relational databases.   Demonstrated ability to implement quality control methods to check data for errors, inconsistencies and missing information/codes.  Demonstrated experience with geospatial mapping tools.  Demonstrated knowledge of Australian flora.  Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively within a team including data-related issues.  Demonstrated attention to detail, with sound grammar, punctuation and numeracy skills.   Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively in a small research team.    Desirable:   An interest in environmental history  A familiarly with AI programs such as Claude    Qualifications   A postgraduate degree in Geospatial Science or Environmental Science    Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.     To Apply      Please submit your CV and covering letter and address the Key Selection Criteria (outlined in the Position Description) for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.     For recruitment enquiries: Aleks Besia, Senior Talent Acquisition Advisor – Aleksandra.Besia@rmit.edu.au  For research project enquiries: Dr Marie Keatley, Lecturer, School of Science – marie.keatley@rmit.edu.au    Position description - Research Assistant, Phenology        Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.        Applications Close: 4 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Business-Analyst--06-month---Third-party-Contract-_JR50943": {
      "title": "Business Analyst (06-month & Third-party Contract)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Business Analyst (06-month & Third-party Contract) to define scope and requirements, identify business processes and help design functional aspects of solutions in alignment with business needs WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile. WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. Contract duration: 6 months Annual leave: 1 day per working month Free use of onsite sports and fitness facilities Library on campus and online - access to the RMIT Australia online library Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY Working as part of the ITS PMO, the Business Analyst will work closely with business and technical stakeholders in defining scope and requirements, identifying business processes and helping design functional aspects of solutions in alignment with business needs. Taking on a proactive role in helping shape a project from inception through to completion, the Business Analyst will work closely with architects, developers and testers in ensuring that the delivered solution meets business needs. The Business Analyst will become an expert in the business domain in which they operate and will provide consultative advice to stakeholders as required. Key Accountabilities Summary Identify and manage stakeholders, understand stakeholder interests and ensure that impacted stakeholders have a common understanding of new features or changes introduced by the solution. Define scope and high-level requirements for input into inception phase activities, e.g., business case development. Engage with stakeholders to understand user context and support follow-up IT enquiries. Guide business functions in RMIT VN to follow RMIT IT policy/strategies. Gather, analyse, and document detailed functional and non-functional requirements, ensuring that these are well understood by all impacted stakeholders and project team members. Gather, analyse, and document functional specifications, comprising of use cases, user interface designs and data attributes, where required. Gather, analyse, and document features, epics and user stories. Define, analyse, and document current and future state business processes using standards such as BPMN, identifying opportunities for process efficiency/improvements and incorporating these into the functional design of the solution to help achieve business goals. Perform requirements traceability of business analysis artefacts, ensuring that this is maintained throughout the project lifecycle. Key Selection Criteria Minimum 3 years’ experience working as business analyst in software project delivery, involving across project lifecycle. Previous experience in the higher education sector, including an understanding of the student lifecycle is a big plus. Good mix of business analysis and technical analysis skills. Demonstrated experience in stakeholder relationship management, requirements gathering and analysis, and business. Process development and use case development. Consultative and open-minded, with highly effective communication, interpersonal skills and attention to detail. Excellent analytical, problem solving, critical thinking and workshop facilitating skills. Experience in both waterfall and agile methodologies. More information is available in the Job Description . HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 2 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Technology-Vendor---Asset-Coordinator_JR50607": {
      "title": "Technology Vendor & Asset Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Technology Vendor & Asset Coordinator oversees the full lifecycle of IT assets, ensuring accurate asset tracking, inventory control, compliance, and operational readiness across the organization. The role also coordinates technology vendors and service providers, monitoring performance, supporting procurement and contract activities, and driving continuous service improvement through data analysis and stakeholder collaboration. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile. WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY This role is responsible for the day-to-day operations of Technology asset management and vendor contracts, ensuring seamless workflow coordination across internal teams, external stakeholders, and technology vendors. Acting as a bridge between management and operational execution, the position proactively resolves operational gaps to consistently deliver high-quality IT Services. Key Accountabilities Summary Technology Asset Management Coordinate the procurement, tracking, lifecycle management, commissioning, and disposal of technology assets in accordance with organisational policies, governance requirements, and operational needs. Maintain the accuracy and integrity of technology asset records across CMDB, Workday, and associated asset management systems, including asset registration, tagging, stocktaking, lifecycle updates, and related data administration. Support the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of technology asset management processes, procedures, and inventory controls to enhance operational efficiency and compliance. Plan, monitor, and coordinate technology asset refresh cycles, stock levels, and forward planning activities in collaboration with business units and ITS stakeholders to ensure operational readiness and positive customer experience. Coordinate asset audits, reconciliation activities, and associated financial asset recharge and transfer processes with Finance and relevant stakeholders to ensure accuracy, accountability, and compliance. Analyse and monitor asset data, usage trends, and operational risks to support informed decision-making, lifecycle planning, and continuous improvement initiatives. Vendor & Service Management Coordinate and monitor vendor and service provider performance to ensure services are delivered in accordance with agreed service levels, contractual obligations, and quality standards. Maintain and document vendor performance records, including formal performance feedback and reporting in alignment with RMIT procurement and governance requirements. Work closely with internal ITS teams and external service providers to coordinate the resolution of service issues, operational concerns, and vendor-related incidents. Develop and maintain effective working relationships with vendors, stakeholders, and service providers to support service delivery outcomes and operational continuity. Conduct service reviews, gather customer feedback, and analyse service performance trends to identify opportunities to improve staff and student experience. Monitor vendor compliance with contractual obligations and escalate potential risks, claims, disputes, or performance concerns as appropriate. Contract, Procurement & Governance Support Support all ITS procurement and contract lifecycle activities including RFx processes, vendor engagement, contract renewals, payments, budget forecasting documentation coordination, and governance compliance in partnership with Finance, Procurement, Legal, and relevant business stakeholders. Develop and maintain reporting mechanisms, dashboards, and service metrics relating to asset management, vendor performance, operational status, and risk management activities. Identify, track, and report risks relating to technology asset management, vendor performance, compliance, and service delivery. Undertake other duties commensurate with the scope and classification of the role. Key Selection Criteria A Bachelor’s degree relevant to business administration or relevant field  Familiarity with ServiceNow CMDB or other IT asset management tools. Working knowledge with PowerBI or other similar reporting tools. Knowledge of IT End-User-Technologies (EUT) such as laptops/desktops, monitors. communication devices etc. Advantageous to have knowledge of mobile device management solutions. At least 4 year of work experience in managing services for a large, multi-faceted organisations.  A proactive approach to planning, coordination and delivery of work.   Excellent interpersonal and negotiation skills, including the ability to communicate effectively with a diverse range of stakeholders.  Strong skills in coordination, organisation and customer/client liaison.  Familiarity with asset management procedures. Proven conceptual and analytical skills, and the ability to formulate and evaluate policy options.  Demonstrated knowledge and commitment to continuous improvement principles.  Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children check. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. More information is available in the Job Description . HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 1 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Senior-Lecturer--Human-Resources-Management_JR47270": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer, Human Resources Management",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nOverview: We are seeking a Senior Lecturer in Human Resource Management to join our academic community and deliver high-quality teaching, research, and student engagement. This is an exciting opportunity for an educator-scholar who is passionate about shaping future-ready graduates and contributing to impactful research. Teaching strengths in Human Resource Management broadly are welcomed, with additional advantage for expertise in People Analytics. Expected start date: Feb 2027 WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile . WHAT WE OFFER Expatriates Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates Relocation allowance package starting at US$6,000 Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate and direct dependents (if applicable) International repatriation flights for the staff and direct dependents at the end of their contract. School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to US$20,000 per child or US$40,000 for two children per year. Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam. Vietnamese candidates Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Other benefits Generous annual leave, career leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Senior Lecturer will contribute to the teaching and research efforts of the school. The incumbent is to make a significant contribution to the delivery of programs and to be actively involved in research, consulting and other professional activities. The Senior Lecturer will develop, engage in and lead high quality research projects that are aligned with the University’s research focus areas to achieve success in attracting research funding and to produce high quality outputs. The Senior Lecturer will have an important research leadership role in embedding their research expertise into the life of the school and will be required to develop high-quality, productivity-driven networks across RMIT and with local, national and global, internal and external partners. The Senior Lecturer may have responsibility for program management. Key Accountabilities summary Make original contributions in teaching and/or scholarship which expand knowledge or practice within the discipline including designing, conducting and moderating assessment, implementing improvements informed by course evaluation activities and student feedback. Conduct and lead high quality research, recognised at the national level: developing highly successful research teams; managing research projects and programs within timelines and budget and ensuring compliance with quality and reporting requirements; regularly publishing research results in high quality outlets as lead author and in collaboration with other researchers; identifying appropriate funding sources and prepare successful external research funding submissions; supervising higher degree by research candidates. Participate in the School/University strategy development and governance and make a significant contribution to administration activities of an organisational unit or an interdisciplinary area at undergraduate, honours and postgraduate level, which may include program management of a large award program or a number of smaller award programs. Adhere to the requirements of the Academic Expectations and Development Framework of RMIT Vietnam. Other duties commensurate with the scope of the role Key Selection Criteria PhD or equivalent Doctoral qualification in a relevant discipline Demonstrated ability to coordinate large courses; prepare and delivery programs at undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including high quality curriculum and program materials and ability to implement innovative approaches to student-centred learning and quality improvement. Demonstrated ability to support student issues related to effective learning, including demonstration of recent, strong and sustained performance regarding student outcomes, student experience and feedback; combined with notable experience and demonstrated skill in a wide range of teaching settings. Emerging nationally recognised research track record including substantial record of research outputs in high quality outlets. Extensive experience in research leadership with the ability to build and develop collaborative research teams, mentor academic staff to deliver high quality outcomes, attract and secure external research funding to sustain research effort and manage funded research projects including complex budgets and reporting requirements. Extensive experience in supervising higher degrees by research candidates to maximise research performance. Demonstrated ability to manage academic program team, supporting scholarly development of less experienced academic staff. Demonstrated understanding of and commitment to financial, governance and quality management systems within a university. Demonstrated high level of interpersonal, communication and negotiating skills including the ability to consult with senior executives, external bodies, produce executive reports, negotiate agreed directions, outcomes and targets within a collaborative environment. Ability to operate within and provide leadership across own discipline and cross-disciplinary/multidisciplinary teams to achieve Department and University strategic outcomes. Ability to work with external partners, industries, organisations and communities and can operate effectively to address complex issues or seek opportunities Ability to motivate, influence, develop and inspire others through discipline leadership in the University environment and with external partners and stakeholders Appointment to this position is subject to passing mandatory check as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. For full details of the accountability, please refer to the Job Description . Expected Research profile   To be considered for a lecturer position at RMIT Vietnam in The Business School, you will need to be able to meet the following research criteria.  For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3 years (Early Career Academic), although there are no requirements you are expected to be research active.   For candidates with a PhD awarded within the last 3- 5 years there are requirements of peer reviewed journal articles published within the previous five-year window, you need to be active in relevant research areas.   For candidates with a PhD awarded more than 5 years ago: you will be expected to demonstrate a minimum of 2 peer reviewed journal articles, of which must be ranked in Scimago or ABDC and preferably both in Q1/A ranking or equivalent, within the previous five-year window.  To be considered for a Senior Lecturer position and above, The Business School operates a research active points system. Points are earned across a spectrum of research within a prior three-year window. Candidates for higher level positions will be considered against these criteria for shortlisting.  HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the University reserves the right to appoint prior to the closing date. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at nhu.tranngocquynh@rmit.edu.vn Applications Close: 29 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/College-of-Business-and-Law---Expression-of-Interest-for-Sessional-Teaching--Economics----School-of-Economics--Finance-and-Marketing_JR51556": {
      "title": "College of Business and Law - Expression of Interest for Sessional Teaching (Economics) – School of Economics, Finance and Marketing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nOverview: • Casual hours commencing March 2027   • Based at the Melbourne CBD campus but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University About RMIT RMIT offers life-changing experiences for our students, and helps shape the world with research, innovation, teaching and industry engagement. With strong industry connections forged over 130 years, collaboration with industry remains integral to RMIT’s leadership in education, applied and innovative research, and to the development of highly skilled, globally focused graduates. About the School of Economics, Finance and Marketing The School aims to provide practical, relevant, and innovative economics, finance, marketing, blockchain enabled business and social impact programs; research; industry training and consulting which graduates, employers, industry and university peers acknowledge as amongst the best available in the international marketplace. We offer undergraduate programs in Economics, Finance and Marketing, postgraduate programs in Finance and in Marketing and Blockchain Enabled Business and higher degrees by research (Masters or PhD) in all three of our disciplines (Economics, Finance and Marketing). Our undergraduate programs are also offered at RMIT Vietnam and through our partnership with The Singapore Institute of Management. We are a multi-disciplinary team with cutting edge facilities looking to engage with others. Further information regarding RMIT’s Economics programs please explore our programs here .  Express Your Interest  We welcome expressions of interest from both external applicants and current RMIT casual employees interested in contributing to the Economics programs.  The Economics team is actively seeking skilled and qualified tutors with expertise in teaching economics and econometric courses across a diverse array of specialised domains. These areas include but are not limited to digital economics (including an interest in cryptoeconomics, cryptofinance, the impact of frontier technologies on economic systems, the economics of AI), behavioural economics, game theory, microeconomics, time series analysis, big data, and machine learning. Proficiency in statistical software such as R and proficiency in the Python programming language, along with knowledge of digital and blockchain technologies, are highly desirable qualifications for potential candidates. Please address the following questions in your application:  •    What type of work would you be interested in? – Teaching, Marking . •    Please briefly outline your academic and/or professional experience.  •    If you are interested in tutoring or teaching, please provide a summary of your teaching ability and your capacity to engage students positively and constructively.  •    If you would like to be considered for future casual research opportunities, please briefly outline your research interest.    Qualification:    A relevant tertiary degree and /or extensive project and administrative expertise in a complex tertiary education or similar service environment. Please note: The volume, nature and availability of sessional teaching will vary based on the needs of the school including course offerings, timetabling and student demand.   Although our needs and vacancies regularly change, there are opportunities that exist across our programs. By submitting an application you will be included into a Talent Pool that will be reviewed across the year and may not guarantee a position.  To submit your expression of interest, please click ‘Apply ’ and submit a current CV and covering letter outlining your interest for the role. Please save your application as a PDF titled with your full name and JR51556, eg. John Smith CV JR51556. Employment is subject to the successful attainment of an Employee Victorian Working with Children Check.  Applications Close: 12 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/College-of-Business-and-Law---Expression-of-Interest-for-Sessional-Teaching--Finance----School-of-Economics--Finance-and-Marketing_JR51558": {
      "title": "College of Business and Law - Expression of Interest for Sessional Teaching (Finance) – School of Economics, Finance and Marketing",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nPart time\n\nOverview: • Casual hours commencing March 2027   • Based at the Melbourne CBD campus but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University About RMIT RMIT offers life-changing experiences for our students, and helps shape the world with research, innovation, teaching and industry engagement. With strong industry connections forged over 130 years, collaboration with industry remains integral to RMIT’s leadership in education, applied and innovative research, and to the development of highly skilled, globally focused graduates. About the School of Economics, Finance and Marketing The School aims to provide practical, relevant, and innovative economics, finance, marketing, blockchain enabled business and social impact programs; research; industry training and consulting which graduates, employers, industry and university peers acknowledge as amongst the best available in the international marketplace. We offer undergraduate programs in Economics, Finance and Marketing, postgraduate programs in Finance and in Marketing and Blockchain Enabled Business and higher degrees by research (Masters or PhD) in all three of our disciplines (Economics, Finance and Marketing). Our undergraduate programs are also offered at RMIT Vietnam and through our partnership with The Singapore Institute of Management. We are a multi-disciplinary team with cutting edge facilities looking to engage with others. Further information regarding RMIT’s Finance programs please explore our programs here . Express Your Interest  We welcome expressions of interest from both external applicants and current RMIT casual employees interested in contributing to the Finance programs.  We have exciting opportunities for you to teach in a range of specialised areas in finance at both the undergraduate and postgraduate levels, including but not limited to risk management, sustainable finance, alternative securities, portfolio management, bonds, case studies in finance, financial modelling, fintech and machine learning in finance. Teaching opportunities are also available in the state-of-the-art RMIT Trading Facility, where students learn apply financial knowledge through market data in trading simulations and workshops. You'll guide them in multi-asset portfolio and risk analysis, hedging, money market, and foreign exchange trading using real-time market rates.   We are looking for passionate individuals who can inspire students and foster an engaging learning environment. If you have experience in sustainable finance, quantitative finance, trading, risk management, portfolio management or related fields, we encourage you to apply. Join our innovative approach to finance education and be part of shaping the future of finance.  Please address the following questions in your application:  •    What type of work would you be interested in? – Teaching – Marking •    Please briefly outline your academic and/or professional experience. •    If you are interested in tutoring or teaching, please provide a summary of your teaching ability and your capacity to engage students positively and constructively. •    If you would like to be considered for future casual research opportunities, please briefly outline your research interest.   Qualification: A relevant tertiary degree and /or extensive project and administrative expertise in a complex tertiary education or similar service environment. Please note: The volume, nature and availability of sessional teaching will vary based on the needs of the school including course offerings, timetabling and student demand. Although our needs and vacancies regularly change, there are opportunities that exist across our programs. By submitting an application you will be included into a Talent Pool that will be reviewed across the year and may not guarantee a position. To submit your expression of interest, please click ‘Apply’ and submit a current CV and covering letter outlining your interest for the role. Please save your application as a PDF titled with your full name and JR51558, eg. John Smith CV JR51558. Employment is subject to the successful attainment of an Employee Victorian Working with Children Check. Applications Close: 1 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
