    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Lecturer-Associate-Lecturer--Games_JR51369": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Associate Lecturer, Games",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Lecturer/ Associate Lecturer, Games to join our academic community and deliver high-quality teaching, and student engagement. This is an exciting opportunity for an educator-scholar who is passionate about shaping future-ready graduates and contributing to impactful research.  WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER Expatriates   Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates  Relocation allowance package from US$6,000  Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate and direct dependents (if applicable)  International repatriation flights for the staff and direct dependents at the end of their contract.  School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to US$20,000 per child or US$40,000 for two children per year.  Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Vietnamese candidates   Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates.  13th month Tet bonus   Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Other benefits   Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays)  Professional development and career advancement  Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources  A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!  SCHOOL OF COMMUNICATION & DESIGN (SCD) The School of Communication & Design is committed to providing an international learning environment that encourages cultural awareness, critical thinking, experimentation and — above all — the ability to think differently. Our students develop the competence, confidence and professionalism needed for successful careers in communication, design, games, fashion, film and video, and languages. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us/schools-and-centres/school-communication-design THE BACHELOR OF DESIGN (GAMES) PROGRAM  The Bachelor of Design (Games) at RMIT Vietnam equips students to become creative and technically proficient designers capable of shaping the future of interactive media. In an increasingly digital world driven by rapid technological advancement, the program fosters graduates who combine strong design fundamentals with forwardthinking innovation. Delivered through a dynamic studio-based learning environment, the degree integrates conceptual, technical, theoretical, and research-driven approaches to game design and development. Our teaching team comprises experienced academics and industry professionals who bring real-world insight and contemporary practice into the classroom. ABOUT THE ROLE The Lecturer/Associate Lecturer contributes to the teaching and academic activities of the University within disciplines related to their field of expertise. Both roles are expected to support a high-quality student experience, work collaboratively and collegially with academic colleagues, and contribute to the effective delivery and continuous development of the program. To comply with Vietnam’s employment requirement, all overseas candidates must have at least 3 years University teaching experience.       At the Associate Lecturer scale, the position contributes to undergraduate teaching in areas relevant to their field of expertise and supports the academic, administrative and coordination activities associated with course delivery. Responsibilities include preparing and delivering lectures, tutorials, studios and practical classes, assessment and feedback, course administration, and contributing to curriculum and teaching activities in line with University quality assurance requirements. The Associate Lecturer is expected to develop their teaching, scholarly and professional capabilities and, where appropriate, an emerging research profile aligned with School and University priorities. The role works with appropriate support and guidance while developing increasing autonomy in teaching, administration and academic practice.   At the Lecturer scale, the position contributes to the teaching, scholarly, research and professional activities of the University within their field of expertise. The Lecturer is responsible for undergraduate teaching and course coordination, maintaining and advancing their scholarly, research and/or professional capabilities, and contributing to the School’s research culture through activities appropriate to career stage. The role also contributes to curriculum development and continuous improvement of the student learning experience, while supporting the profile and development of the Games Design program through meaningful links and partnerships with academic, industry and professional communities. Both roles are expected to work collaboratively and collegially within the teaching team, contribute to the effective delivery and ongoing development of the program, and remain informed about developments in their discipline, professional practice and areas of specialisation.   Reports to: Program Manager, Bachelor of Design (Games) Key Accountabilities: Lecturer/Associate Lecturer Undertake undergraduate teaching, including designing, conducting and moderating assessment; curriculum development; and implementing improvements informed by peer review, course evaluation activities and student feedback. Contribute to industry engagement and program activities, including coordinating industry activities and relationships, showcases, guest talks, workshops and other program-related events. Undertake administrative duties, which may include course coordination or management and coordination of a small award program. Contribute to University and School service activities, including staff meetings, town halls, committees, marketing and recruitment activities, open events, school visits, workshops, and other industry and external engagement activities. Undertake independent professional activities appropriate to the profession or discipline and maintain currency in relevant areas of professional practice. Adhere to the requirements of the Academic Expectations and Development Framework of RMIT Vietnam. Undertake other duties as assigned in consultation with the Line Manager.   Lecturer In addition to the accountabilities above, the Lecturer is expected to: Undertake scholarship and high-quality research activities appropriate to the profession or discipline, including traditional and/or non-traditional research outputs. Manage individual research projects within agreed timelines and budgets and ensure compliance with relevant quality, ethics and reporting requirements. Publish and disseminate research outcomes in high-quality outlets as lead or co-author. Prepare and submit applications for external research funding and contribute to research initiatives, collaborations and the School’s broader research culture. Supervise Higher Degree by Research candidates, where appropriate.   Key Selection Criteria: For Associate Lecturer: A master's degree in a relevant discipline. Having commenced, or enrolled to commence, a Doctoral qualification is preferred. For Lecturer: A PhD or equivalent relevant Doctoral qualification from a recognised institution, with an emerging track record and growing recognition for research, scholarly and/or professional practice. Demonstrated ability to prepare and deliver teaching at undergraduate level, including online delivery; design, conduct and moderate assessment; and produce high-quality curriculum and program materials. Demonstrated ability to improve teaching and curriculum informed by peer review, course evaluation and student feedback. Proven expertise in three or more of the following areas, evidenced through relevant professional, academic and/or portfolio-based work: ** Game Art, including 2D/3D character, asset and environment design, Games Studies, Games Cultures and Games History, Games Programming ** Game Systems and Systems Design, Mobile Game Development ** Sound Design for Games and Interactive Media,Game development using Unreal Engine, Unity and/or Godot, Game production, exhibition, festival and/or events curation Demonstrated ability to guide students in the conceptual, aesthetic, technical and/or production development of games and interactive experiences. Ability to undertake course coordination responsibilities. Demonstrated capacity to work effectively with and negotiate sensitively with students, particularly on matters related to learning, assessment, and student development. Recent and sustained teaching performance in relation to student outcomes, student experience and feedback, combined with experience across a range of teaching settings.   For Lecturer, additionally: An emerging track record and recognition for quality research, scholarly and/or practice-based outputs that contribute to relevant Discipline and School research areas, evidenced through publications, traditional and/or non-traditional research outputs, development of research initiatives, contribution to competitive research funding opportunities, and engagement with industry, community and professional partners. Ability to supervise, or develop capacity to supervise, Higher Degree by Research candidates. Ability to develop effective academic, industry, and professional networks and contribute to research collaborations, external funding opportunities and industry-engaged projects. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills appropriate for working with students, Higher Degree by Research candidates, staff, industry and professional partners, together with a strong commitment to teamwork and multidisciplinary collaboration. Ability to operate effectively within their own discipline and across cross-disciplinary and multidisciplinary teams to contribute to School and University strategic outcomes. Ability to work effectively with external partners, industry, organisations and communities to address complex challenges, develop opportunities, and strengthen the profile and activities of the Games Design program. Ability to adapt to the rapidly changing landscape of games design, development and related technologies, and to maintain current disciplinary and professional knowledge. Ability to motivate, develop, and inspire others through discipline leadership in the University environment.  Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values, and RMIT Leadership Model.   HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit  resume, cover letter and portfolio . Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible.  COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam   Applications Close: 14 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/RMIT-Human-Research-Ethics-Committee-member-Volunteer-_JR51862": {
      "title": "RMIT Human Research Ethics Committee member(Volunteer)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nPart time\n\nOverview: Community Representatives to join RMIT Human Research Ethics Committee   Volunteer position Online meetings (Compensated )   Are you interested in facilitating ethical and responsible research that help shapes our world for the better? RMIT University is seeking community members to join its Human Research Ethics Committee (HREC) .   About the Role The HREC is responsible for reviewing and monitoring research involving human participants to ensure it is conducted ethically and in accordance with related standards and regulations. As a committee member, you will play an important role in supporting ethical research while representing community perspectives.   What we offer Volunteer position, with comprehensive induction and ongoing training , friendly, professional and supportive committee environment and hybrid participation (online and in-person). A modest payment (honoraria) provided to external committee members in recognition of the time and effort involved in reviewing applications and attending committee meetings.   We are seeking applicants in the following categories:   Community members who bring a broad community or consumer perspective and must have no paid affiliation with RMIT University Pastoral carers in the community (e.g. minister of religion, chaplain, Aboriginal Elder, or similar) People experienced in professional care or treatment (e.g. nurse, counsellor, social worker, allied health professional, or similar)   Committee members are expected to review research applications involving human participants, attend and actively participate in committee meetings and complete pre-meeting and post-meeting reading and preparation.   Committee Meetings are held on the third Wednesday of most months between 4:00 pm to 6:30 pm. To be eligible, you must be available to attend scheduled committee meetings and willing to undertake required reading and preparation and not be a current employee (or associated with) RMIT University.   To Apply Please submit a brief cover letter and résumé outlining your background, why you are interested in joining the committee and in which membership capacity.   For further information, please contact: Dr Peter Burke, HREC Secretary. Email: humanethics@rmit.edu.au   Please note:  Due to the critical nature of the role, we are running a rolling recruitment process and will be contacting candidates as soon as they apply, with early applications encouraged. Applications Close: 15 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Service-Connect-Advisor_JR51720": {
      "title": "Service Connect Advisor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nPart time\n\nOverview: •   Casual hours, Commencing January 2027 •   Based at Melbourne CBD campus and the potential to work across other RMIT Campus as required. Why join RMIT? Our people are at the heart of everything we do. At RMIT, we value innovation, collaboration and impact. Our values are the heart (durrung) of who we are and what we stand for at RMIT. They guide what we do, how we make decisions, and how we treat each other. About the role The Service Connect Advisor will provide frontline customer service and support for routine enquiries within established procedures and knowledge resources. The primary objective is to resolve enquiries at the first point of contact where possible, while providing a high level of customer service across all contact channels. The Advisor will take ownership of customer enquiries, provide clear and accurate information, and refer matters requiring further assistance to senior team members or the appropriate resolver group. The role will involve fact-finding, completing standard service requests, recording accurate information and contributing to the resolution of more difficult enquiries under guidance. The Advisor will identify and report knowledge gaps, unclear procedures and difficult or non-standard issues to senior team members. Please note: there may also be a requirement to work staggered start times depending on business requirements to cover the University core support hours. Reporting Line: Service Connect Team Lead Engagement Type This role is engaged on a casual, as-required basis. There is no guarantee of ongoing or regular work. Hours will vary depending on operational requirements. Key Selection Criteria: 1. Demonstrated customer service experience delivering professional support services in a customer service, contact centre, help desk, administration or similar environment. 2. A strong customer-centric mindset and commitment to providing respectful, timely and helpful service. 3. Demonstrated ability to clarify customer needs, gather relevant information and follow established procedures to support appropriate outcomes. 4. Demonstrated ability to provide accurate and timely information through multiple customer contact channels. 5. Demonstrated ability to recognise matters requiring additional assistance and escalate them appropriately. 6. Demonstrated ability to report knowledge gaps, unclear procedures and difficult or non-standard issues to senior team members. 7. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with colleagues and stakeholders to support a consistent customer experience. 8. Demonstrated ability to work with minimal supervision in a fast-paced environment and prioritise multiple tasks within required timeframes. 9. Strong problem-solving, interpersonal and written and verbal communication skills across multiple mediums, including telephone, ticketing tools and web chat. 10. Demonstrated ability to use a range of computer applications and to quickly learn new technologies and systems. Desirable 1. Experience in an IT service desk, contact centre, university or large, complex organisation. 2. Experience using ServiceNow, Workday, ADP Payroll or similar service management and enterprise systems. 3. Knowledge of IT service management principles and customer support processes. To Apply  Please submit your CV and short response to selection Criteria clicking on the ‘Apply’ link at the top of this page. Please submit your documents as First_Last Name CV –JR51720 For further information about this position, please contact Rachel Ledgerwood via email rachel.ledgerwood@rmit.edu.au Applications Close: 11 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Research-Assistant--AI-Consultancy_JR51577-2": {
      "title": "Research Assistant, AI Consultancy",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nPart time\n\nOverview: Part-time (0.5 FTE), fixed-term position for 12 months   Salary Academic Level A, starting at A6 ($106,129 pro rata) + 17% superannuation   Primarily based at the RMIT Business and Technology Studio in Werribee and the Melbourne City campus   About the position   As the Research Assistant, AI Consultancy, you will support the delivery, evaluation and continuous development of an RMIT research service that helps Wyndham businesses identify practical and responsible opportunities to adopt artificial intelligence (AI).  Working as part of the Enterprise AI and Data Analytics Hub, you will engage directly with businesses to understand their needs, assess their readiness for AI and identify and prioritise potential AI opportunities.  You will also help develop practical recommendations and pathways for further support, including AI Sprints and other relevant programs.  The role will contribute to research and knowledge-sharing activities arising from the program, including data collection and analysis, case studies, project and technical reports, research publications and funding applications.  You will work under limited supervision, with increasing autonomy as your skills and experience develop. There is some flexibility available around working days, with an agreed working pattern to be established following commencement.  To be successful in this position, you’ll have:   Experience undertaking research independently and as part of a team, including contributing to publications, conference presentations and research funding submissions.  Evidence of research outputs, such as publications, conference contributions and/or technical reports in a relevant field.  The ability to build relationships with industry and government and contribute to funding opportunities and projects.  The ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with colleagues, project leaders and industry partners.  Strong organisational skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines and adapt to changing requirements.  Strong written and verbal communication skills.  The ability to undertake relevant administrative activities associated with the role.  Qualifications   A qualification in a relevant discipline area, preferably a PhD or equivalent , is required.    Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.     About the College of Business and Law Want to learn more about the College you'll be supporting? Explore our College of Business and Law webpage and refer to the Position Description linked below for further information about the role and College.   To Apply    Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing the Key Selection Criteria for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.     For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below.    Position Description – Research Assistant, AI Consultancy    Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.      Applications Close: 15 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Performance-Marketing-Manager_JR50962": {
      "title": "Performance Marketing Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-27\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, fixed-term opportunity until November 2027 HEW 8 + 17% superannuation and flexible working arrangements Bring your hands-on SEM and Meta advertising expertise to a client-side performance marketing role   About You We’re looking for an experienced performance marketer with strong hands-on expertise in search engine marketing (SEM) and Meta advertising.You’ll take campaign briefs and turn them into effective paid media activity, from understanding the audience and selecting channels through to execution, optimisation, measurement and reporting, to support RMIT’s student recruitment and marketing objectives.   This role suits someone who can move comfortably between the technical and strategic sides of paid media. You’ll work with agencies and internal stakeholders, you need be comfortable getting into the detail of campaign performance, challenging results and turning data and insights into actionable recommendations. If you’ve built your experience agency-side and are looking to move client-side, this is an opportunity to bring that expertise into a role where you can focus more deeply on one organisation. To be successful in this position, you’ll have: Demonstrated hands-on experience managing and optimising search engine marketing campaigns, with strong knowledge of Google Ads, Adobe Search, search strategy, bidding and conversion optimisation Practical experience  managing Meta advertising campaigns, including audience targeting, campaign set up, optimisation and performance analysis. Strong knowledge of paid media planning and strategy skills with the ability to select appropriate channels and translate campaign objectives into effective media activityStrong analytical and reporting capabilities, including interpreting campaign metrics, attribution and performance reporting to inform recommendations. Strong stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to work effectively and collaboratively with internal teams and brief agency partners. Demonstrated experience in a performance marketing or paid media role; media agency or relevant education or services-sector experience will be highly regarded. Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.   About the Portfolio   The Engagement Portfolio provides integrated, strategic leadership across RMIT to advance the University’s reputation, reach and revenue. Its functions include domestic and international student recruitment, global marketing and intelligence, strategic communications, advancement, and industry engagement and partnerships. Through data-informed decision-making, innovation and collaboration, the portfolio supports RMIT’s long-term strategic objectives.   To Apply   Please submit your CV and covering letter outlining your hands-on experience in search engine marketing and Meta advertising by clicking on the ‘Apply’ link at the top of this page. For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Sarah [surname and email to be confirmed].   Position Description - Performance Marketing Manager Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, position description links may not work on LinkedIn advertisements.     #LI-Hybrid Applications Close: 9 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Market-Intelligence---Data-Analyst_JR51011": {
      "title": "Market Intelligence & Data Analyst",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Market Intelligence & Data Analyst to turn complex data into clear, decision-ready insights that shape how we understand our market, customers and performance. Sitting within the Market Intelligence & Strategy team, this role combines advanced quantitative analysis, statistical modelling and business intelligence to uncover trends, identify risks and support strategic decisions across brand, products, pricing, competitors and the student experience. In line with our current recruitment and selection guidelines, this role is open to Vietnamese candidates only. Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile . WHAT WE OFFER Competitive gross remuneration package for candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance 20 days annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas break and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Market Intelligence & Data Analyst is the quantitative analytics specialist of the Market Intelligence & Strategy department. The role is responsible for the department’s quantitative data analysis, statistical modelling and business-intelligence capability – turning large and complex datasets into rigorous, decision-ready insight on brand, products, pricing, competitors and market performance. It owns the design and delivery of advanced quantitative analyses, predictive and statistical models, and the dashboards, automation and data infrastructure that make insight available across the University. The role works closely with the Manager, Market Research, the Market Analyst & Research Project Lead and the Senior Qualitative Research Specialist, and engages internal stakeholders across Schools, Student Recruitment, Marketing and Finance as well as counterparts in Melbourne. It identifies risks, improves and streamlines quantitative research design and data processes, and is expected to advance the analytics maturity of the department. The position is mainly based in Ho Chi Minh City, but the scope of work covers both Vietnam and other regional markets following the University’s direction. KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES SUMMARY The role’s accountabilities are organised into four functional areas: (1) Quantitative analysis and statistical modelling; (2) Business intelligence, dashboards and automation; (3) Data strategy, management and governance; and (4) Insight delivery and continuous improvement. 1. Quantitative Analysis & Statistical Modelling Lead all quantitative data processing, interpretation, analysis and modelling for the department, applying advanced statistical and analytical techniques to datasets spanning Products, Pricing, Brand and Market Performance. Design and build statistical and predictive models – for example regression, segmentation and clustering, forecasting and trend analysis, significance and hypothesis testing, and survey/weighting analysis – to explain drivers and anticipate market movements. Guide the team on the selection of appropriate quantitative methods and techniques, set standards for analytical rigour, and ensure the validity, reliability and reproducibility of quantitative outputs. Develop and refine quantitative research designs (sampling, instrument and weighting design) in partnership with the research team to ensure data is collected in a statistically sound way. 2. Business Intelligence, Dashboards & Automation Create reports, visualisations and interactive dashboards using a range of database and BI technologies (e.g. Power BI) to make quantitative insight accessible to market research and stakeholder audiences. Develop and maintain the in-house market intelligence hub, producing regular and ad-hoc reports on brand, products, pricing, competitors, promotion and channels. Formulate and implement processes for automated insight and performance metrics to management using advanced BI tools, and build tools, tests and dashboards that operationalise key findings. 3. Data Strategy, Management & Governance Establish and implement the strategy for gathering, managing and disseminating data and performance metrics across the wide range of data owned by the department. Model database needs based on project requirements and maintain data dictionaries and documentation associated with these data models. Ensure adherence to ethical and professional requirements and to RMIT Privacy, Compliance, Risk & Regulation in the handling, storage and use of data. 4. Insight Delivery & Continuous Improvement Drive quantitative project milestones to completion – building partnerships, defining accountability, and leading the activities that operationalise key findings – and provide recommendations that inform and enhance decision-making. Create and deliver impactful presentations and ad-hoc analyses for mid-level and senior audiences to aid management decision-making and business planning. Continually refine market intelligence and quantitative research processes by identifying inefficiencies and suggest and implement tools and methods that enable the digital and regional-expansion initiatives of the University. Other duties commensurate with the scope of the role Key Selection Criteria Bachelor’s degree in data science, business analytics, statistics, economics, marketing or another quantitative discipline. At least 3–4 years’ experience in a similar quantitative analytics or data-analyst role, in market research or a comparable data-intensive industry. Strong quantitative and statistical skills, with demonstrated experience applying advanced techniques such as regression, segmentation/clustering, forecasting and trend analysis, and significance/hypothesis testing. Advanced proficiency working with large and complex datasets, predominantly in Excel and SQL; statistical analysis using tools such as SPSS, R or Python; Power BI or equivalent a strong advantage. Demonstrated experience designing and validating quantitative analyses and models, with a focus on rigour, accuracy and reproducibility. Experience with data visualisation and BI tools (e.g. Power BI) to communicate business insights through clear, well-designed reports and dashboards. Experience modelling database needs and maintaining data dictionaries, documentation and data-governance practices. Strong business acumen and problem-solving skills, with the ability to translate complex quantitative findings into actionable recommendations. Excellent written and verbal communication, with the ability to deliver impactful presentations to mid- and senior-level audiences; attention to detail and strong quality control. Well-developed interpersonal skills including coordination, liaison and communication, both written and spoken, in English and Vietnamese, across a broad range of stakeholders. Strong project-management capability and commitment to continuous improvement, with the ability to organise and prioritise multiple projects in a fast-paced environment. Appointment to this position is subject to passing a background check as outlined in the RMIT Vietnam Background Check Matrix. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. For full details of the accountability, please refer to the Job Description . HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the University reserves the right to appoint prior to the closing date. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at nhu.tranngocquynh@rmit.edu.vn Applications Close: 15 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/PMO-and-Commercial-Senior-Coordinator_JR51789": {
      "title": "PMO and Commercial Senior Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for a PMO & Commercial Senior Coordinator to support its infrastructure portfolio through contract administration, procurement coordination and expenditure tracking. Working with project teams and senior leaders, you’ll help strengthen governance and provide clear, timely visibility of project performance. Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The PMO & Commercial Senior Coordinator is the operational engine of the Vietnam Infrastructure PMO, delivering commercial and contract administration in line with PMO governance standards and RMIT policy. The role manages the end-to-end lifecycle of consultant, contractor and vendor contracts – from drafting, routing and execution through to variations, payment certification and close-out – while overseeing procurement transactions, expenditure and commitment tracking on RMIT's ERP system (Workday) for all infrastructure projects. Acting as a central point of contact for commercial and contract matters, the role maintains the PMO's contract repository, master schedule of record and performance dashboards, giving senior leadership timely, accurate visibility of project and portfolio status. The position also drives consistency across the PMO by deploying standardised templates and tools and supporting continuous improvement of commercial and administrative processes. With strong attention to detail and sound commercial judgement, the PMO & Commercial Senior Coordinator safeguards governance and control across Vietnam Infrastructure's portfolio. Reporting Line  Reports to:  Head of Commercial Strategy and Planning Reporting lines may be adjusted in line with organisational changes. Key Accountabilities Summary Commercial & Contract Administration Managing the contract administration of various contracts, including consultant contracts, ensuring compliance with RMIT policies and legal standards, while also facilitating the drafting, review, and execution of contracts with consultants, contractors and vendors. Oversee the commercial aspects of infrastructure projects, such as business case preparation, procurement service requests, budget tracking, cost analysis, and financial reporting, in close collaboration with external consultants and finance teams to ensure project finances are managed effectively and cost-effectively. Manage consultant contracts from inception to completion, ensuring deliverables align with RMIT project goals, and collaborate with consultants to define project scopes, timelines, and performance metrics. Coordinate the routing, approval and execution of contract documents, and ensure all signed agreements are properly archived and logged in the contract register. Oversee the handling of variations to contracts, ensuring proper documentation and communication. Ensure that all contractual obligations, including variations, comply with relevant regulations and standards, and work with RMIT Risk and Legal to identify and mitigating potential risks related to contracts, variations, and financial matters. Implement and uphold high standards in contract administration processes, including variations, and conduct regular reviews to ensure accuracy and compliance with RMIT University policies. Draft and review standard commercial contracts, letters of engagement and variation documents, using RMIT's Commercial Toolkit templates and in accordance with RMIT policies and legal standards. Check and verify payment documentation and supporting evidence (invoices, milestone certificates, VAT invoices) for accuracy and completeness prior to submission for approval and payment processing. Track and monitor performance bonds, bank guarantees and other contractual security instruments, including expiry and renewal dates, and facilitate vendor payment milestones in line with contract terms. Address issues related to contract administration, variations, or financial matters within the team and different RMIT departments, seeking resolutions that align with RMIT University policies. PMO Governance & Stakeholder Coordination Coordinate executive briefings and maintain the master schedule of record for the Infrastructure PMO, ensuring senior leadership has timely and accurate visibility of program and governance status. Coordinate and maintain the centralised repository of all PMO project paperwork, contracts and records, ensuring documents are properly filed, version-controlled and readily retrievable for audit and reporting purposes. Act as a point of contact for stakeholders on contract and financial matters, and communicate effectively with vendors, consultants, and partners to ensure the smooth execution of contractual obligations. Collaborate with RMIT departments, including Finance, Legal and project teams, to ensure alignment in contract and commercial activities, and facilitate effective communication between project stakeholders. Data, Systems & Reporting Process and monitor commercial transactions, purchase orders, and payment requests on the ERP system (Workday), ensuring data accuracy and timely processing in line with PMO SOPs. Develop and maintain accurate documentation related to contracts, contract payments and project activities, and prepare regular reports on project budgets and financials, highlighting key metrics and providing insights. Consolidate weekly and monthly project updates into Power BI/Excel dashboards, developing and maintaining accurate, timely reporting and performance insights for senior leadership review. PMO Governance, Framework & Process Develop and maintain the Infrastructure Commercial Toolkit  covering procedures, workflows, tender and contract administration templates, the risk register, evaluation forms and user guides from sourcing to contract close-out. Work with Procurement, Legal, Finance and project teams to confirm requirements and keep the toolkit aligned with University policies and approval frameworks. Support project teams to apply it consistently across infrastructure projects through guidance, training and updates based on their feedback Design and deploy standardized templates (including Tender and Variation Order forms) across project teams and provide guidance and training on their correct usage to ensure consistency and compliance with PMO standards. Evaluate and enhance administrative processes related to contracts, variations and commercial management, and implement improvements to increase efficiency and accuracy in administrative tasks. Record and maintain notes on PMO processes, procedures and policy updates, supporting the PMO's monitoring of SOP compliance across the Infrastructure portfolio. Other duties as required by line manager Key Selection Criteria Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. Strong knowledge of construction contracts, commercial law, and relevant regulations. Demonstrated 3-5 years experience in project management and/or project documentation control (construction projects preferred). Proficient IT skills including the use of email, MS Office, and other office software. Excellent commercial and financial acumen and the ability to analyse complex financial data. Excellent reporting skills including budget and cost reporting, project KPI reporting, project dashboards using related software. Working knowledge of ERP systems (e.g. Workday) for processing commercial transactions, purchase orders and document workflows. Analytical, systems-oriented mindset with the ability to translate procurement and project data into operational insight to support commercial decision-making. Working knowledge of drafting and reviewing standard commercial contracts and related legal/commercial documentation. Highly skilled in drafting, writing business reports and letters. Proven experience coordinating and executing administrative and reporting work with complex stakeholders such as accountants, finance personnel, project managers and external parties such as consultants and contractors. Hands-on experience in project procure-to-pay (P2P) administrative processes. Experience in a customer service environment. Demonstrated ability to work in a team environment. Strong interpersonal and negotiation skills, including the ability to communicate effectively with a wide range of stakeholders. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, as per the RMIT Behavioural Capability Framework (Connectedness, Commitment to Excellence (Continuous Improvement), Innovation, Outcomes Focus, Open Thinking, Resilience). Qualifications and Checks Mandatory Bachelor’s degree in business, commerce, finance or a related field Proven experience as a Commercial Manager or in a similar role is preferred. Proficiency in project management and financial management software. Proficient with Office software such as Word, Excel, PowerPoint, PDF. Proficient English business communication and writing skills. Experience in P2P procurement administrative work. Sound understanding of project management methodologies, frameworks and tools. Familiarity with PMO governance processes, Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) and document/record management practices. Well-developed skills in preparing business reports and correspondence. Preferred Proven experience in construction or related industry. Knowledge of and experience using tools such as Power BI to create project dashboards and reports. Exposure to Source-to-Pay or other procurement systems, and to process automation or digital enablement initiatives, is an advantage. PMP certification is a plus. Read more details at Job Description HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 21 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Learning-Design-Assistant--2-positions_JR51816-1": {
      "title": "Learning Design Assistant- 2 positions",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nOverview: ***2-month third-party contract *** RMIT Vietnam is seeking a contingent worker for the Learning Design Assistant . While the position is advertised by RMIT Vietnam, the successful candidate will be employed and managed by an external service provider, who will be responsible for the labour contract. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile . POSITION SUMMARY The Assistant will support the Learning Design team in developing and enhancing blended and online learning experiences at RMIT Vietnam. Under the guidance of experienced team members, the Intern will assist in preparing digital learning materials, building and formatting content in Canvas LMS, and conducting accessibility and quality checks. Reports directly to: Manager, Online Learning KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES Support the Learning Design team in developing and improving blended and online learning experiences in collaboration with academic stakeholders. Assist in reviewing and formatting learning materials to align with RMIT Vietnam’s learning design, user experience (UX), accessibility, copyright, and style guide standards. Help review academic content and organize information into clear, engaging learning sequences and activities that support course learning outcomes. Contribute to the development of inclusive learning materials that consider the diverse needs, backgrounds, and abilities of students. Assist in creating learning activities that encourage student engagement, interaction, and collaboration with peers and academic staff. Explore and use AI tools and emerging technologies to support learning design tasks, improve efficiency, and develop instructional materials. Help ensure that digital learning content and activities align with defined course learning outcomes. Support the development and formatting of learning materials using authoring tools, multimedia applications, and the Canvas Learning Management System (LMS). Assist in building and formatting Canvas LMS pages using basic HTML and existing templates, including course content, assignments, and other structural elements. Support accessibility checks to help ensure digital learning materials follow WCAG 2.0 AA guidelines. Participate in team discussions, feedback sessions, and other design activities to build knowledge and practical skills. Carry out other related duties as required to support the Learning Design team and the University’s evolving needs.   KEY SELECTION CRITERIA Currently pursuing or recently completed a Bachelor’s degree in Communication, Design, Digital Media, Technology, Education or a related field. Basic understanding of learning and teaching principles, with an interest in blended learning, online education, and inclusive learning design. Good written and verbal English communication skills, with the ability to organize information clearly and communicate effectively with team members and stakeholders. Familiarity with digital learning platforms or Learning Management Systems (LMS), preferably Canvas, is an advantage. Basic knowledge of HTML and CSS, or a willingness to learn, is an advantage. Proficiency in common digital productivity tools and an interest in exploring multimedia authoring tools, AI applications, and emerging educational technologies. A proactive and curious mindset, with the ability to learn new concepts, tools, and processes quickly. Ability to work collaboratively, build positive working relationships, and give and receive constructive feedback. Good organizational and time-management skills, with the ability to manage assigned tasks and meet deadlines. Attention to detail and a willingness to learn and apply guidelines, feedback, and quality standards. Demonstrated behaviors aligned with RMIT’s values and Behavioral Capability Framework, including Connectedness, Commitment to Excellence, Imagination and Innovation, Impact, Inclusion, and Agility.   Additional Information Contract duration: 02 months Working location: Saigon South Campus Highly competitive gross salary Annual leave: 1 day per working month Private Insurance Online library and supportive and collaborative environment that encourages professional growth and development HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS General 6.0 (or equivalent CEST 150).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process To be eligible for this position you must be a Vietnamese citizen .  Applications received from non-Vietnamese candidates will not be considered. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam   Applications Close: 31 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/OH-S-Specialist_JR50731": {
      "title": "OH&S Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Fixed Term position until June 2028 Salary Professional HEW 8 ($121,213 - $136,507) + 17% Superannuation and Flexible Working Arrangements Based at the Melbourne CBD campus About the Role The OH&S Specialist is responsible for providing operational expertise and technical leadership to advance the safety, hazard prevention, and risk management initiatives across RMIT facilities and manufacturing partner organisations. The role works closely with industry representatives, regulatory stakeholders, and academic leaders to drive the integration of evidence-based safety practices into advanced manufacturing environments. The position focuses heavily on investigating current and emerging workplace hazards associated with automation, robotics, and Industry 4.0/5.0 systems, ensuring all activities align with WorkSafe Victoria expectations and relevant statutory legislation. The position will lead the development, implementation, and evaluation of hazard-specific training modules, benchmarking reports, and comprehensive OH&S frameworks designed to support risk management across diverse manufacturing environments. This includes designing and delivering tailored industry guidance materials, leading pilot testing for safety interventions, and facilitating collaborative workshops and consultation sessions with key stakeholders. Additionally, the Specialist will collect, analyse, and interpret complex workplace health and safety data to deliver actionable insights, inform decision-making, and contribute to project evaluation, reporting, and continuous improvement processes. To be successful in this position, you’ll have:   Degree in Occupational Health and Safety, Ergonomics, Human Factors Engineering, or a related discipline. Demonstrated experience conducting workplace risk assessments, safety audits, and hazard investigations. Strong knowledge of Australian WH&S/OH&S legislation, standards, and risk management principles. Experience developing safety procedures, training programs, or guidance materials. Excellent stakeholder engagement and communication skills, including working with industry partners. Strong analytical, report-writing, and project management skills. Ability to work independently while contributing effectively to multidisciplinary project teams.   Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.   About the School The School of Property, Construction and Project Management is a leading provider of programs in construction management, project management, property and valuation, occupational health and safety, and sustainable building across the Asia–Pacific region. With a highly industry‑focused approach, the School maintains more than 300 industry connections through its Employer of Choice program, giving students valuable workplace experience and access to employers. It also maintains strong links with the global research community, offering excellent facilities for postgraduate research and fostering interdisciplinary collaboration across programs. For more information see https://www.rmit.edu.au/about/our-education/academic-schools/property-construction-and-project-management/about To Apply  Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link above.   For further information about this position, please see Position Description below or contact Jessica Bernardo (Senior Talent Acquisition Advisor) via email jessica.bernardo@rmit.edu.au . PD – OH&S Specialist Applications Close: 8 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Campus-Technology-Services-Team-Lead_JR51616-1": {
      "title": "Campus Technology Services Team Lead",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nOverview: Lead RMIT’s dedicated event technology support team HEW 7 | Continuing, full-time Combine people leadership, technology and service delivery in a highly visible role Lead the technology team behind outstanding university events Are you an experienced technology service delivery professional who knows how to lead people, coordinate competing priorities and keep services running when it matters most? RMIT is seeking a Campus Technology Services Team Lead to lead the day-to-day delivery of dedicated audiovisual and technology support for events. The role sits within End User Technology in Information Technology Services and supports conferences, presentations, lectures, executive engagements and other significant university events. You will lead a team of technology support specialists to deliver reliable onsite support, ensuring event organisers and presenters receive timely, professional assistance. This is an opportunity to combine technical service leadership with highly visible, customer-focused delivery in a varied university environment. What you will do In this role, you will: Lead, develop and coordinate a team of technology support specialists delivering high-quality onsite event and end-user technology services. Oversee daily schedules, service queues, resource allocation and technology support for conferences, presentations, executive engagements and other university events. Act as an escalation point for complex or high-impact issues, coordinating timely solutions with specialist teams, stakeholders and external partners. Manage IT Service Management activities, ensuring incidents and requests progress effectively and services perform against agreed measures. Use service data, customer feedback and root cause analysis to identify trends, reduce recurring issues and improve the customer experience. Strengthen service delivery through effective reporting, process improvement, automation and the introduction of relevant technology enhancements What will help you succeed To be successful, you will bring: At least five years’ experience in enterprise technology service delivery, with a strong focus on service improvement. Experience leading or coordinating technical specialists, including allocating work, setting expectations and supporting team performance. Demonstrated experience coordinating operational work across internal and external delivery teams and contributing to large-scale service and technology change initiatives. Experience managing end-user computing, audiovisual or event technology services within a large and complex organisation. Demonstrated experience managing technology services using ITIL Service Management processes, supported by ITIL Foundation certification or a qualification in a relevant industry framework. The ability to manage competing priorities and complex escalations using sound judgement, service data and structured problem-solving. Excellent communication and relationship-management skills, with the confidence to work with technical teams, senior stakeholders, customers and external partners. You will hold tertiary qualifications in Information Technology or bring equivalent relevant experience. Experience working in Agile operational or project teams will be advantageous. Working arrangements This is a continuing, full-time position primarily based at RMIT Melbourne City campus, with the potential to work across other campuses when required. As the team provides dedicated technology setup and operational support for events, this is a highly visible, onsite role. Flexibility may be required to accommodate event schedules, service demands and activities outside standard business hours. Why work at RMIT? RMIT is a global university of technology, design and enterprise, committed to creating transformative experiences for students and making a meaningful impact through research, innovation and engagement. Information Technology Services provides the systems and services that enable great experiences across the community. In this role, your leadership will directly influence the quality, reliability and professionalism of the technology support delivered at university events. Appointment requirements Appointment is subject to holding a valid Victorian Working with Children Check and completing any other checks required for the position. Maintaining a valid Working with Children Check is a condition of employment at RMIT. How to apply Please submit: Your current resume. A cover letter outlining your relevant technology service delivery and people leadership experience. Applications Close: 8 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Technology-Support-Specialist_JR51629": {
      "title": "Technology Support Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\nFull time\n\nOverview: Multiple continuing opportunities | HEW 5 and HEW 6 Information Technology Services Primarily based at RMIT’s Melbourne City campus Onsite, event-focused technology roles Help deliver outstanding technology experiences at RMIT events Join RMIT’s End User Technology team in Information Technology Services and help deliver seamless conferences, lectures, presentations and executive events. These hands-on roles support presenters and event organisers with reliable audiovisual and onsite technology services. We have opportunities available across the following roles: Senior Technology Support Specialist, HEW 6 Technology Support Specialist, HEW 5   About the opportunities Senior Technology Support Specialist, HEW 6 In this role you will provide technical expertise for complex and high-profile events, including executive and VIP engagements. You will resolve complex or recurring issues, coordinate escalations, guide colleagues and stakeholders, and improve event technology practices and service continuity. Technology Support Specialist, HEW 5 In this role you will deliver core onsite event support: prepare and operate audiovisual systems, troubleshoot live issues and work with presenters, event organisers and colleagues to keep events running smoothly. What you will do Depending on the level of the appointment, responsibilities will include: Set up, test, operate and pack down event audiovisual equipment, including sound, presentation, video conferencing and lighting systems. Monitor live events and troubleshoot audiovisual, computing, peripheral and connectivity issues. Guide users with varying technical knowledge and collaborate with event teams, technology specialists and vendors. Own incidents and service requests, keep stakeholders informed and escalate when needed. Support installations, workstation setups, relocations, proactive maintenance and technology lifecycle improvements. What will help you succeed You will bring practical experience in audiovisual, event technology, desktop support, end-user computing or a related environment. For HEW 6, you will need more extensive experience managing complex issues and supporting high-profile or VIP events. You will also demonstrate: Hands-on audiovisual and meeting-room technology knowledge, including sound, microphones, audio mixing, displays and video conferencing. Strong troubleshooting skills and a calm, responsive approach to live-event issues. Customer-focused service and clear communication with presenters, senior stakeholders, colleagues, vendors, staff and students. The ability to prioritise in a busy environment, work independently and contribute to a collaborative team. A commitment to continuous improvement and learning new technologies. A relevant qualification in Information Technology, Computer Science, audiovisual technology, event production or a related discipline is desirable. Equivalent practical experience will also be valued. Working arrangements Based primarily at Melbourne City campus, with travel to other campuses as required. These are dedicated onsite event-support roles, not primarily remote or standard service-desk positions. You must be available for rostered or split shifts within the 7:30 am–8:30 pm service window, with occasional event support outside standard business hours. Why work at RMIT? RMIT is a global university of technology, design and enterprise. Join a collaborative technology team in a varied, highly visible environment where your expertise directly contributes to successful university events and experiences. Appointment requirements Appointment is subject to a valid Victorian Working with Children Check and any other required checks. Maintaining a valid Working with Children Check is a condition of employment. How to apply Please submit: Your current resume. A brief cover letter outlining your relevant experience, including an example of resolving a technical issue under time pressure in an event or live environment. Confirmation of whether you wish to be considered for the HEW 5 role, HEW 6 role, or both levels.   Applications Close: 8 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Health---Safety-Senior-Business-Partner_JR51392": {
      "title": "Health & Safety Senior Business Partner",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-24\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Continuing position Hew 8+ 17% Superannuation and Flexible Working Arrangements Based at the Melbourne CBD & Brunswick campus, and hybrid ways of working About the role The Health & Safety Senior Business Partner is a specialist role responsible for managing a range of complex health and safety consultancies covering a wide range of legislation and risks. The role will encompass the management of key projects as identified by clients and legislative changes as well as the review, development and implementation of innovative health and safety strategies, policies and programs. The development and delivery of health and safety training packages and information sessions as well as regular reporting, analysis and monitoring of health and safety performance are also key aspects of the role.   Key responsibilities:   Provide expert OHS advice, complex consultancy and risk management guidance. Lead incident investigations and regulatory interventions using structured methodologies such as ICAM. Partner with senior leaders to embed health and safety into strategy, operations and culture. Develop and maintain H&S procedures, tools and plans aligned with legislative requirements. Analyse H&S data and provide insights and recommendations to senior leadership Conduct audits and inspections to identify and address compliance and performance risks. Monitor H&S metrics, data quality and emerging legislative/regulatory requirements. Support regulatory engagement, external audits and compliance assessments. Advise executives and managers on OHS legislation, policies and responsibilities. Facilitate consultation with HSRs, safety committees and governance groups. Build organisational H&S capability through coaching, training and targeted information sessions. Provide H&S expertise across cross-functional initiatives, new facilities, equipment and processes Lead and contribute to H&S projects, initiatives and enterprise-wide campaigns. Analyse H&S data to identify trends, emerging risks and improvement opportunities. To be successful in this position, you’ll have: Strong knowledge of health and safety legislation, risk management, hazard identification and incident investigation (e.g. ICAM). Experience in higher education, research, clinical or similarly complex environments. Proven ability to analyse complex H&S issues and develop practical, effective solutions. Strong communication, influencing and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to drive change and build a positive safety culture. Experience leading H&S projects, continuous improvement initiatives, training and safety communications. Ability to produce clear, high-quality reports, policies, proposals and investigation/audit documentation. Collaborative, flexible and able to work independently within a client-focused team. Relevant tertiary qualification in occupational health and safety, or equivalent experience. Desirable: Experience with ISO 45001/digital safety systems, psychosocial safety and ergonomics, plus training or qualifications in facilitation, auditing, investigations or coaching. Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check. About the Portfolio The Health, Safety & Risk (HSR) team are a team of strategic professionals providing outstanding, client focused, proactive and effective solutions and services for all RMIT staff. Our success is achieved by understanding our business and operating as a business partner to our clients. We deliver responsive, innovative and practical solutions and services. The HSR team operate in a manner that supports the RMIT values and achievement of the business objectives. By providing tailored, quality services and products and ensuring a high level of expert support and advice, the HSR team will enhance College/Portfolio and Groups ability to meet their business objectives. Thisin turn will allow the University staff to better support the current and future student population at the University. To Apply  Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing the Key Selection Criteria for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page. For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Bianca Jenkins via email bianca.jenkins@rmit.edu.au. Position Description Applications Close: 7 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Senior-Coordinator--Student-Services_JR51254": {
      "title": "Senior Coordinator, Student Services",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT is seeking two Senior Coordinators, Student Services (01 in Hanoi and 01 in Ho Chi Minh City) to lead and support the Student Connect advisory team in delivering exceptional student service experiences, while driving operational excellence, fostering team capability, and partnering with stakeholders to continuously enhance the effectiveness and quality of student support services. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile . WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Senior Coordinator, Student Services role within Student Connect provides leadership, guidance, and support to Student Connect advisory staff, ensuring the delivery of high-quality service and advice to students. In this dynamic role, you will collaborate with a team of advisory and other coordinators, sharing expertise and working together to continuously enhance the operations and effectiveness of the Student Connect team. KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES Team leadership & operations Manage student enquiries across approved service channels, including phone, walk-in, webchat, online portal and appointments…, ensuring timely support and the provision of clear, accurate and considered advice in accordance with University policies and procedures. Provide day-to-day leadership and support to assigned Student Connect advisory staff (Advisors, Officers, and/or Concierges), ensuring consistent and effective service delivery. Coach and develop team members through ongoing feedback, training, and performance management to build capability and maintain service standards. Monitor enquiry volumes and workload, leading the team to meet service quality targets and operational expectations. Collaborate with peer Senior Coordinators to manage service channels and staff operations, allocating resources to meet service demand and support a flexible, scalable service model. Escalation and complex case management Act as an escalation point for complex enquiries referred from team members, including those involving policy or procedure ambiguity, or sensitive and high-risk cases. Exercise sound judgement to interpret policies and determine appropriate outcomes. Coordinate with relevant stakeholders to support timely and consistent resolution of escalated matters. Stakeholder partnership Engage with stakeholders to ensure accurate and up-to-date information is available to staff and students. Work with key stakeholders (e.g. Academic Registrar’s Group, Schools, Global Mobility, and other student services) to identify and implement improvements to processes, systems, and the student experience. Lead or coordinate partnership forums (e.g. School partnerships), translating student enquiry trends into actionable recommendations to inform decisions and improve the student experience. Build and maintain effective working relationships to support collaboration and issue resolution. Service enablement & coordination Develop and maintain service resources and communication content (e.g. website content, student guides, internal guides, signage). Analyse service data and student feedback to identify improvement opportunities and lead initiatives to enhance service delivery, in collaboration with the Student & Family Connect Service Optimisation. Coordinate Student Connect activities and events, as well as support participation in broader University events(e.g. Orientation, enrolment support sessions, study plan workshops, experience days, family events) Escalate systemic or high-impact issues to the Manager, Student Connect or Head of Department, Student &Family Connect as appropriate. Undertake additional responsibilities as assigned by the Manager, Student Connect. KEY SELECTION CRITERIA A bachelor’s degree in a relevant discipline. At least 5 years of experience in a student services or customer-facing environment, with a strong understanding of service delivery in a high-volume, multi-channel context. Proven experience in leading, supervising, or coaching staff, with the ability to build capability, provide feedback, and support team performance. Demonstrated ability to manage complex or sensitive cases, including those requiring interpretation of policies, sound judgement, and escalation where appropriate. Strong problem-solving and decision-making skills, with the ability to assess situations, consider risks, and determine appropriate outcomes. Experience in monitoring service performance and workload, with the ability to allocate resources and support operational efficiency. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with a range of stakeholders, with experience influencing outcomes, resolving issues, and supporting process improvements. Experience analysing service data or feedback to identify trends, inform improvements, and support decision-making. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage effectively and professionally with staff, students, and stakeholders. High level of proficiency in professional English, with strong written and verbal communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a dynamic, service-oriented environment. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. More information is available in the Job Description . HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the University reserves the right to appoint prior to the closing date. COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 8 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Research-Fellow---Soil-and-Environmental-Geochemistry_JR51548": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Soil and Environmental Geochemistry",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nOverview:   Full-time, fixed-term position for 12 months with a possible extension Salary Academic Level B.1 $ 119,915 p.a. + 17% superannuation Primarily based at Melbourne City campus, with work across other RMIT campuses, including Bundoora, as required Occasional travel for fieldwork, with the possibility of international travel About the Role Advance research in soil and environmental geochemistry within RMIT’s Department of Chemical and Environmental Engineering. Working with Chief Investigator Associate Professor Dane Lamb, you will contribute your expertise in environmental mineralogy, soil chemistry and soil organic matter biogeochemistry, particularly mineral–organic interactions and mineral-mediated redox and catalytic processes. You will plan and deliver high-quality research independently and collaboratively, manage projects within agreed timelines and budgets, undertake field sampling and data collection, publish research findings and contribute to competitive funding applications. You will also supervise higher degree by research candidates and build productive networks with academic, industry and government partners. The role includes a 10% teaching and learning contribution aligned with your expertise. You will bring a collaborative approach, strong communication skills and a commitment to research that expands knowledge in your discipline. To be successful in this position, you will have: Demonstrated expertise in environmental mineralogy, soil chemistry and soil organic matter biogeochemistry, particularly fundamental mineral–organic interactions and mineral-mediated redox and catalytic processes. Experience in X-ray absorption spectroscopy and/or soil microbiology will be highly regarded. An emerging track record of quality research outputs and recognition, evidenced by publications, new research initiatives, competitive research funding and industry links. Demonstrated ability to supervise higher degree by research candidates. The ability to build effective professional networks and develop funding opportunities through liaison with industry and government. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with a strong commitment to teamwork and multidisciplinary collaboration. Qualifications Mandatory: A PhD or equivalent in Geochemistry, Soil Science or Environmental Engineering Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check. About the School of Engineering The School of Engineering is one of the largest Engineering Schools in Australia. It has over 350 staff and 7000 students, including 750 HDR students. The School is committed to driving innovation and collaboration through our industry partnerships. Our industry partners range from small companies to multinational organisations, and we work together on translating our research into impact for our partners and the wider community. The School has six Departments: Aerospace Engineering Biomedical Engineering Chemical and Environmental Engineering Civil and Infrastructure Engineering Electrical and Electronic Engineering Mechanical, Manufacturing and Mechatronics Engineering In 2023, the School developed a new strategic plan, which will see an increasing emphasis on engagement with industry and other external partners. The School is developing new industry-led degrees, where our students learn whilst working for companies, as well as innovation hubs where we will co-locate industry partners, our research teams and our undergraduate students. Over the next three to five years, the School of Engineering will support these new strategic plans through investments in new facilities. This will include reimaging our teaching laboratories, where we will use new digital technologies to enhance the student experience, as well as research labs where partnerships with industry will enable us to maintain leading research facilities. The STEM College is also developing plans for a large new building in the Melbourne City Campus, and the School of Engineering is expected to hold significant space in this new building. RMIT is a global university, and the School of Engineering has students and research partners across South East Asia and Europe. This includes two campuses in Vietnam, as well as partnerships in Hong Kong, Singapore and we recently entered into a partnership with the Birla Institute of Technology and Science in India. The School also has a research centre in Barcelona, which provides access to European funding and industry partners. The School will continue to grow our international activities with the aim of becoming a globally connected School that translates technologies and training across continents. https://www.rmit.edu.au/about/schools-colleges/stem-college To Apply  Please submit your CV and a covering letter addressing the key selection criteria for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page. For further information about this position, please refer to the Position Description below or contact Associate Professor Dane Lamb, Chief Investigator, via dane.lamb@rmit.edu.au For further information regarding recruitment processes, please contact Jennifer Pham, Senior Talent Acquisition Advisor via email at jennifer.pham2@rmit.edu.au Please do not share your application to this email address.   Position Description: Research Fellow – Soil and Environmental Geochemistry Applications Close: 18 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Expression-of-Interest---Interior-Design---Sessional-Academic_JR43418": {
      "title": "Expression of Interest - Interior Design - Sessional Academic",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nPart time\n\nOverview: We are seeking expressions of interest for sessional opportunities in the School of Architecture and Urban Design within the College of Design and Social Context Based at our City campus   Join RMIT as a Sessional Become part of RMIT's academic community as a sessional staff member. Enjoy flexibility in your schedule while contributing to our dynamic learning environment. Our sessional roles involve diverse teaching and support activities across various disciplines, following best practices and guidelines. This is an excellent opportunity for professionals passionate about education who wish to share their expertise flexibly. Our Interior Design discipline The Interior Design discipline at RMIT seeks expressions of interest for part-time sessional teaching positions across various content areas. Teaching opportunities are available in both the Bachelor of Interior Design (Honours), a four-year undergraduate degree, and the Master of Interior Design, a two-year coursework program.   A leader in interior design education and research, we position interior design as a critical practice that contributes to and transforms the social, cultural, material, technological and environmental conditions of the spaces in which we live. Our programs challenge assumptions about interior design through ideas-led design practice that addresses the dynamic relations between people and the surrounding environment.   We seek expressions of interest from interior designers, architects, and other spatial or design-related fields with an established or emerging body of innovative and experimental design work. We welcome applications from both experienced educators and practitioners interested in developing a teaching practice.   This competitive application process generates many applications beyond our available positions. By filling out this expressions of interest for sessional opportunities you will be added to our permanent database of potential sessional teachers. The Talent Pool is reviewed leading up to the commencement of Semester 1 and 2 each year. If you have gained new experience or have an updated portfolio please upload your latest CV and copy of your Portfolio to your profile. Please contact us if you would like to be removed at any point.  More information about the Interior Design programs can be found at:  Bachelor of Interior Design (Honours) Masters of Interior Design (Masters by Coursework) rmitinteriordesign.gallery @interiordesign.rmit  Important: Appointment requires relevant qualifications or industry equivalency, and candidates must pass a Working with Children check. To Apply  Please click the 'Apply' link below to submit your application documents (CV, cover letter, portfolio) as a PDF, ensuring you have used your Full Name in the name of the file. Applications Close: 30 Dec 2027 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Indigenous-Prospective-Student-Case-Manager_JR50837-1": {
      "title": "Indigenous Prospective Student Case Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Fixed Term position until 24 December 2027 HEW 6 ($97,647 p.a + 17% Superannuation), Cultural leave and Flexible/Hybrid Working Arrangements Based at the Melbourne CBD campus About the Role As the Indigenous Prospective Student Case Manager, you will play a key role in supporting Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander prospective students on their journey to RMIT. Within Global Student Recruitment, you will provide personalised, culturally safe support from initial enquiry through to enrolment, empowering students to make informed decisions and confidently pursue their educational goals.  This role combines relationship management, case management and student recruitment expertise to create a positive and supportive experience for prospective Indigenous students. Through proactive engagement, needs-based conversations and tailored guidance, you will help students overcome barriers, access opportunities and successfully transition to university. You will also work closely with the First Nations Ngarara Willim Centre and a range of internal and external stakeholders, providing insights and advice that inform Indigenous student recruitment activities and contribute to RMIT's strategic goals for Indigenous participation and success.  About You You are passionate about supporting Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples to achieve their educational aspirations and bring demonstrated experience working with Indigenous communities and stakeholders. The ideal candidate will have: Experience engaging with Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander communities and a strong understanding of Indigenous cultures, organisations and the barriers Indigenous peoples may experience when accessing higher education. Experience providing case management, advisory or support services, with the ability to manage competing priorities and maintain strong attention to detail. Excellent relationship-building and communication skills, with the ability to engage effectively with a diverse range of stakeholders. Demonstrated ability to collect and analyse information, identify issues, recommend solutions and contribute to reporting activities. Strong organisational skills and the ability to work independently while contributing positively within a collaborative team environment. Knowledge of the higher education sector and experience supporting Indigenous people to achieve educational outcomes. Experience in student recruitment, admissions or conversion activities is highly regarded but not essential.  About the Portfolio The Engagement Function brings together expertise from across RMIT to deliver inclusive, customer-centred and future-focused experiences for students and other key audiences. Through collaboration, data-driven decision-making and innovative engagement practices, the team supports meaningful connections and positive outcomes throughout the student lifecycle.  Position Description – Indigenous Case Manager What We Offer At RMIT, you'll be part of a university committed to reconciliation, Indigenous self-determination and creating pathways for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples to thrive. Our staff enjoy a wide range of benefits including: 17% employer superannuation contribution and cultural leave (up to 10 days) Flexible and hybrid work arrangements Professional development opportunities A welcoming and inclusive and culturally safe workplace  Opportunities to contribute to meaningful social impact and reconciliation outcomes Note: This is an Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Identified Position only for First Nations Australians. This is an Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander identified position and is classified under the special measures provisions of section 12 of the Equal Opportunity Act 2010 (Vic). Only Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander people are eligible to apply. Proof of Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander heritage will be required at interview stage.  Appointment to this position is subject to A valid Working with Children Check. Background checks (Police check, working rights, references) Ready to Apply? If you’re passionate about supporting Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students to access and succeed in education, and are committed to contributing to a culturally safe, inclusive and supportive student experience, we encourage you to apply. Please reach out to loretta.vaughan@rmit.edu.au for any further queries. Closing date: 11:55pm Sunday 8 November 2026 Applications Close: 9 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Manager--Product-Lifecycle_JR51325-2": {
      "title": "Manager, Product Lifecycle",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-23\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Fixed-Term Salary Level HEW 9 + 17% Superannuation Based at the Melbourne CBD campuses however, but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University About the role The Manager, Product Lifecycle is responsible for developing product strategies and managing the end-to-end lifecycle of Non-Award offerings within the College of Vocational Education. Drawing on market trends, industry needs and learner insights, the role drives new product development, enhances existing offerings and provides strategic advice to College Executives and Senior Management, ensuring a sustainable and market-responsive product portfolio aligned with RMIT’s strategic priorities.   This fixed-term opportunity will play a key role in establishing a new business unit within the College of Vocational Education. The position will support the development and implementation of key functions, explore future growth opportunities and contribute to evaluating and establishing a sustainable operating model.   To be successful in this position, you will have:   Essential: • Experience in product management, portfolio management or strategy development in tertiary, VET, non-award/short-course or related education/learning environments. • Ability to use market research, data and performance metrics to inform product decisions, identify opportunities and risks, and drive continuous improvement across a product suite. • Strong stakeholder engagement and communication skills, with experience working collaboratively across diverse internal and external stakeholders, including industry and employer partners. • Analytical and problem-solving skills, including the ability to balance commercial, educational and strategic considerations in product lifecycle decisions. • Experience leading or coordinating cross-functional teams or projects, fostering an inclusive, collaborative and high-performance culture aligned to organisational values. • High level of digital literacy, including experience with CRM, enrolment, learning or product management systems, and advanced Microsoft Office skills.   Desirable • Experience specifically in non-award, short-course or workforce training product development and management. • Knowledge of relevant regulatory, funding and quality assurance frameworks for vocational or non-award education, and their implications for product design and viability. • Experience working with industry clients to co-design learning solutions or tailor product offerings to workforce needs. • Experience in applying service design, product management or continuous improvement methodologies to education products or services. Qualifications • Relevant tertiary qualification and relevant operational leadership experience in a tertiary education environment. Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check.     To Apply  Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.   For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Diana via email at diana.ruiz@rmit.edu.au .   Position Description – Manager, Product Lifecycle    Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page.   #Li-Hybrid Applications Close: 8 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Service-Connect-Advisor---HR_JR51719": {
      "title": "Service Connect Advisor - HR",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nOverview: Casual hours, immediate start available Based at Melbourne CBD campus and the potential to work across other RMIT Campus as required. Why join RMIT? At RMIT, we're connected to industry and focused on preparing students for the future of work. As a casual educator, you'll enjoy flexible teaching opportunities while making a real impact on students, industry and the wider community.   About the role   The Service Connect Advisor will be responsible for providing advice for their skilled resolver group.   The primary objective is to resolve all enquiries at first point of contact whilst providing a high level of customer service skills across all customer contact channels. The Advisor will anticipate the customer needs and go above and beyond where possible. The role of the Advisor will be to conduct appropriate research and/ or identify root causes and provide advice or escalate specialist advice or high-risk enquiries.   Please note: there may also be a requirement to work staggered start times depending on business requirements to cover the University core support hours.    Reporting Line: Service Connect Team Lead(HR Skilled Resolver Group)   Engagement Type This role is engaged on a casual, as-required basis. There is no guarantee of ongoing or regular work. Hours will vary depending on operational requirements.   Key Selection Criteria:   1.Demonstrated customer service experience delivering professional support services specific to the skilled resolver group. 2. A strong customer centric mindset. 3. Demonstrated ability to fact find, provide advice and use logical thought process to support recommendations and advice. 4. Demonstrated ability to build and maintain partnerships and relationships in a collaborative manner with key internal clients and external stakeholders to support the University’s business objectives. 5. Proven ability to identify root cause of issue to recommend and deliver appropriate strategies and innovative solutions and solve any further complications that may be encountered. 6. Demonstrated ability in providing accurate and timely solutions and advice through multiple customer contact channels. 7. Demonstrated ability to work autonomously with minimal supervision in a fast-paced environment with the ability to prioritise multiple tasks to meet conflicting deadlines. 8. Strong problem solving, interpersonal and analytical skills, written and verbal communication across multiple mediums (i.e telephone, ticketing tools, web chat etc). 9. Demonstrated ability in the use of a range of computer applications and the ability to quickly learn new technologies.    Desirable but not essential if experienced with ServiceNow, Workday and/or ADP Payroll.   To Apply  Please submit your CV and short response to selection Criteria clicking on the ‘Apply’ link at the top of this page.    Please submit your documents as First_Last Name CV –JR51719 For further information about this position, please contact Adele Bothma via email adele.bothma@rmit.edu.au Applications Close: 14 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Casual-VE-Teacher---Cyber-Security-and-Networking--ICT-_JR51421": {
      "title": "Casual VE Teacher - Cyber Security and Networking (ICT)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nOverview: Job Posting Content •   Casual hours starting ASAP  •   Casual VE Teacher •   Based at  Melbourne CBD but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University or online.      About You   Join RMIT as a casual sessional employee and become part of a vibrant academic community. As a casual staff member, you’ll enjoy flexibility in your work schedule while contributing to our dynamic learning environment.      Casual roles at RMIT involve teaching and supporting students across various disciplines, while adhering to best practices and guidelines. This is an excellent opportunity for professionals who are passionate about education and eager to share their expertise on a flexible basis.   Key Selection Criteria:   1.        Demonstrated effective interpersonal, communication and problem solving skills relevant to teaching and consultancy environments. This includes effective presentation and facilitation skills, and in the use of flexible teaching methods. 2.        Skills and knowledge in the discipline areas of Information Technology or Cyber Security (E.g. CCNA Network Security) or Cloud Computing (E.g. AWS) or Networking (Cisco CCNA) or Database Management (E.g. MySQL or Oracle) or Programming (Java and Python). 3.        Demonstrated skills and experience in competency-based assessment. 4.        Demonstrated ability in ensuring current and contemporary vocational competence which meets and/or exceeds the education level being delivered and assessed. 5.        Demonstrated experience in relevant industry, and substantial discipline knowledge as it relates to this position. 6.        Demonstrated capacity to diagnose learning problems in students, propose and implement effective solutions. 7.        Demonstrated ability to contribute effectively as a constructive and proactive member of a team. 8.        Demonstrated skills in the use of relevant information and communication technologies.   Highly Desirable: Qualifications and/or industry experience in Artificial Intelligence (AI), including the practical application of AI technologies, automation, generative AI, or AI governance. Experience teaching and assessing AI-related subjects, and the ability to translate emerging AI concepts into engaging, industry-relevant learning experiences, will be highly regarded.       To be successful in this position, you’ll also have as a minimum:     Qualifications and/or industry experience in Artificial Intelligence (AI), including the practical application of AI technologies, automation, generative AI, or AI governance. Certificate IV in Training and Assessment (TAE40110 or higher) A valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check (WWCC)     Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Victorian Employee Working with Children check.       About the College of Vocational Education      The purpose of RMIT’s College of Vocational Education is to empower learners and our industry, community and government partners to succeed in the new world of work. Our five-year strategic roadmap, ALiVE@RMIT, purposefully guides everything we do in vocational education to deliver our vision: to position RMIT as a leading multi-sector provider with global impact and influence.       Led by our Deputy Vice Chancellor, the College of VE is reimagining how we deliver vocational education to create unique experiences for our students and partners, so we can:   Lead in practice-based learning Empower learners for the future of work Engage industry and community at scale Grow for impact and influence     The College of VE is delivering impact through transformation that creates long-term change.       To Apply      Please submit your CV and short response to selection Criteria clicking on the ‘Apply’ link at the top of this page.    Please submit your documents as First_Last Name CV –JR51421     For further information about this position, please contact  komal.tyagi@rmit.edu.au Applications Close: 12 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Casual-VE-Teacher--Sciences---Allied-Health_JR51429": {
      "title": "Casual VE Teacher, Sciences & Allied Health",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-22\nPart time\n\nOverview:   Casual hours, commencing Semester 1 2027 Teaching into Cert IV Allied Health Assistance Based at the Melbourne CBD campus, however, may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University.         About You As a Casual Sciences and Allied Health Teacher within Vocational Education, you will be mainly responsible for the delivery of course material, assessing students and the supervision of students enrolled in selected courses within the program.   You will participate in the program’s continuing review of course content and development, delivery, teaching methods (including online delivery methods) and methods of students’ assessment. Your performance will be underpinned by participation in relevant activities which ensure your vocational competence meets and/or exceeds the education level being delivered and assessed.    Our ideal candidate will have:      Certificate IV in Training and Assessment (TAE40110 or higher)   A qualification in Cert IV Allied Health Assistance   Minimum 3 years industry experience as an Allied Health Assistant   Demonstrated experience of teaching in Vocational Education is desirable     A valid Victorian Employee Working with Children Check (WWCC)     Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing an employee Working with Children    About the College of Vocational Education The purpose of RMIT’s College of Vocational Education is to empower learners and our industry, community and government partners to succeed in the new world of work. Our five-year strategic roadmap, ALiVE@RMIT, purposefully guides everything we do in vocational education to deliver our vision: to position RMIT as a leading multi-sector provider with global impact and influence. Led by our Deputy Vice Chancellor, the College of VE is reimagining how we deliver vocational education to create unique experiences for our students and partners, so we can: lead in practice-based learning empower learners for the future of work engage industry and community at scale grow for impact and influence     The College of VE is delivering impact through transformation that creates long-term change.   To Apply  Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing your interest and suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘Apply’ link at the top of this page.   For further information about this position, contact via email tracey.salter@rmit.edu.au  Applications Close: 12 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Technology-Vendor---Asset-Coordinator_JR50642": {
      "title": "Technology Vendor & Asset Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Technology Vendor & Asset Coordinator oversees the full lifecycle of IT assets, ensuring accurate asset tracking, inventory control, compliance, and operational readiness across the organization. The role also coordinates technology vendors and service providers, monitoring performance, supporting procurement and contract activities, and driving continuous service improvement through data analysis and stakeholder collaboration. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile. WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY This role is responsible for the day-to-day operations of Technology asset management and vendor contracts, ensuring seamless workflow coordination across internal teams, external stakeholders, and technology vendors. Acting as a bridge between management and operational execution, the position proactively resolves operational gaps to consistently deliver high-quality IT Services. Key Accountabilities Summary Technology Asset Management Coordinate the procurement, tracking, lifecycle management, commissioning, and disposal of technology assets in accordance with organisational policies, governance requirements, and operational needs. Maintain the accuracy and integrity of technology asset records across CMDB, Workday, and associated asset management systems, including asset registration, tagging, stocktaking, lifecycle updates, and related data administration. Support the development, implementation, and continuous improvement of technology asset management processes, procedures, and inventory controls to enhance operational efficiency and compliance. Plan, monitor, and coordinate technology asset refresh cycles, stock levels, and forward planning activities in collaboration with business units and ITS stakeholders to ensure operational readiness and positive customer experience. Coordinate asset audits, reconciliation activities, and associated financial asset recharge and transfer processes with Finance and relevant stakeholders to ensure accuracy, accountability, and compliance. Analyse and monitor asset data, usage trends, and operational risks to support informed decision-making, lifecycle planning, and continuous improvement initiatives. Vendor & Service Management Coordinate and monitor vendor and service provider performance to ensure services are delivered in accordance with agreed service levels, contractual obligations, and quality standards. Maintain and document vendor performance records, including formal performance feedback and reporting in alignment with RMIT procurement and governance requirements. Work closely with internal ITS teams and external service providers to coordinate the resolution of service issues, operational concerns, and vendor-related incidents. Develop and maintain effective working relationships with vendors, stakeholders, and service providers to support service delivery outcomes and operational continuity. Conduct service reviews, gather customer feedback, and analyse service performance trends to identify opportunities to improve staff and student experience. Monitor vendor compliance with contractual obligations and escalate potential risks, claims, disputes, or performance concerns as appropriate. Contract, Procurement & Governance Support Support all ITS procurement and contract lifecycle activities including RFx processes, vendor engagement, contract renewals, payments, budget forecasting documentation coordination, and governance compliance in partnership with Finance, Procurement, Legal, and relevant business stakeholders. Develop and maintain reporting mechanisms, dashboards, and service metrics relating to asset management, vendor performance, operational status, and risk management activities. Identify, track, and report risks relating to technology asset management, vendor performance, compliance, and service delivery. Undertake other duties commensurate with the scope and classification of the role. Key Selection Criteria A Bachelor’s degree relevant to business administration or relevant field  Familiarity with ServiceNow CMDB or other IT asset management tools. Working knowledge with PowerBI or other similar reporting tools. Knowledge of IT End-User-Technologies (EUT) such as laptops/desktops, monitors. communication devices etc. Advantageous to have knowledge of mobile device management solutions. At least 4 year of work experience in managing services for a large, multi-faceted organisations.  A proactive approach to planning, coordination and delivery of work.   Excellent interpersonal and negotiation skills, including the ability to communicate effectively with a diverse range of stakeholders.  Strong skills in coordination, organisation and customer/client liaison.  Familiarity with asset management procedures. Proven conceptual and analytical skills, and the ability to formulate and evaluate policy options.  Demonstrated knowledge and commitment to continuous improvement principles.  Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children check. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. More information is available in the Job Description . HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 10 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Audio-Visual-Specialist_JR51293": {
      "title": "Audio Visual Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking an Audio Visual Specialist ensures the seamless operation, maintenance, and enhancement of audiovisual technologies across learning and meeting spaces to support teaching, events, and collaboration. The role also leads AV projects, manages vendors and stakeholders, develops user training resources, and recommends innovative solutions to improve the university's AV environment. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile. WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Audio Visual Specialist will play a crucial role in ensuring the smooth operation and maintenance of audiovisual systems within RMIT Vietnam's classrooms, theaters, and meeting rooms. This role will involve liaising with the Australian team to uphold the university's high standards for AV infrastructure and services. The role will also be responsible for the day-to-day management of AV services, as well as leading and executing projects to fit out new AV spaces and implement innovative initiatives. Key Accountabilities Summary Oversee the operation and maintenance of all audio-visual equipment, including projectors, sound systems, video conferencing systems, and control systems. Monitor the performance of AV systems and troubleshoot technical issues promptly. Work with external vendors on the delivery, implementation and handover of new AV projects and room refresh. Collaborate with the Australian team to understand and implement the university's AV standards and guidelines. Provide recommendations on new AV initiatives and prepare plans and requirements for RMIT Vietnam. Create and maintain AV user educational literacy, such as room operational guides, training demo videos and online FAQ assistance for AV technologies. Liaise with customers and stakeholders requesting AV fit-out services, understand and capture the business needs and operational requirements. Complete regular and ongoing reassessments and analysis of AV and provide input and recommendation for continuous improvement of tools and or processes. Managing AV documentation resources to include room information, schematics, equipment lists, technical and operational manuals, and AV software. Maintain depth of knowledge and understanding of AV industry trends and the range of vendor technologies to meet the AV requirements for the University. Other duties commensurate with the scope of the role Key Selection Criteria A Bachelor degree in relevant field Significant experience within a Technical AV environment working on large scale projects including vendor management. Demonstrated AV installation experience, project management experience desirable. Demonstrated experience in AV technical knowledgebase, AV design, and CAD packages. Demonstrated ability to build effective relationships in a collaborative and engaging manner with a broad range of internal and external stakeholders. Proven ability to work autonomously with minimal supervision. Demonstrated superior analytical and communication skills. Demonstrated ability to prioritise tasks and delivery a quality service to the University. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position and RMIT Values. More information is available in the Job Description . HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 10 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Administration-Officer_JR51521-1": {
      "title": "Administration Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking an Administration Officer provides high-level administrative, operational, and coordination support to the Director of IT Services and the IT Leadership Team, ensuring the smooth day-to-day operation of the department. The role also manages budget administration, recruitment and onboarding coordination, document control, inventory management, and departmental events while working closely with stakeholders across the university. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile. WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Administration Officer is responsible for a broad range of administrative duties to support the IT Services department. The role provides high-level administrative and coordination support to the Director of IT Services and members of the IT Leadership team, including diary and meeting coordination, preparation of documents and reports, support for leadership team activities, and follow-up of key actions. The position is also responsible for supporting department budget administration, raising and following up job requisitions, coordinating hiring processes, and resource and service onboarding. In addition, the role supports the monitoring and maintenance of office equipment and inventory supplies, management of filing systems including financial records, and organisation and support of departmental functions and events. Key Accountabilities Summary Assist with a variety of daily administrative activities, including photocopying and scanning, preparation of purchase requests, purchase orders and payment vouchers for stationery, office equipment and office supplies for all RMIT Vietnam campuses. Provide executive-style administrative support to the Director of IT Services and members of the IT Leadership team, including calendar management, meeting scheduling, coordination of appointments, and support for leadership priorities. Prepare meeting agendas, coordinate meeting logistics, document meeting minutes where required, and follow up on action items to support timely completion. Assist in preparing reports, presentations, correspondence, briefing materials and other documentation for the Director of IT Services and IT Leadership team. Support department budget administration and update the line manager and finance partner on expenditure and accruals. Raise and follow up job requisitions and support the coordination of recruitment and hiring processes. Coordinate onboarding arrangements for new staff, contractors, resources and services within IT Services. Prepare travel requests and travel claims, and prepare monthly payment vouchers for taxi fares, mobile phone expenses, courier services and other office supplies. Input and track incoming and outgoing documents, both internally and externally to RMIT, via the Mail Tracking System on a daily basis. Organise departmental meetings, leadership meetings, semester functions, team building activities and other IT Services events. Support projects with quotations, purchase orders and payment vouchers. Support inventory management of ITS department assets and RMIT ITS equipment, licences and services. Maintain organised filing systems, records and administrative documentation to support operational efficiency and compliance. Prepare monthly reports on office administration status. Undertake other duties as required and directed by the Head of IT Services, in consultation with the Line Manager. Key Selection Criteria A tertiary degree in business, administration or a related field. Demonstrated experience of 4 to 5 years in a large office administration or executive support role. Strong administration experience with the ability to coordinate and prioritise competing work demands in a busy and dynamic environment. Financial acumen, including familiarity with budgets, expenditure tracking and expense management. Demonstrated ability to provide high-level administrative and executive support to senior leaders, including diary management, meeting coordination and preparation of reports and correspondence. Strong influencing and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to provide nuanced feedback, understand leadership direction and execute accordingly. Experience in coordinating hiring activities, including raising job requisitions and following up recruitment processes. Experience in coordinating onboarding for staff, contractors, resources or services. Proven ability to maintain confidentiality, exercise discretion and manage sensitive information appropriately. Ability to quickly learn and apply administration procedures and protocols in a timely manner. A highly motivated and proactive approach to work, with the ability to work independently and as part of a team. Acute attention to detail and accuracy when managing information, records and documentation. Prior experience and familiarity in using tracking systems and document control systems. Strong written and verbal communication skills in both Vietnamese and English. Excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to work effectively with stakeholders at all levels. Understanding of RMIT structure, policies and ability to navigate complex processes and procedures. Proficient use of Word, Excel, Outlook, SharePoint, Workday, PowerPoint, ChatGPT or similar AI tools. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position and RMIT Values. More information is available in the Job Description . HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 5.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 10 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Facilities-Officer_JR51555": {
      "title": "Facilities Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nOverview: Casual hours commencing ASAP    Professional HEW 5 + 17% Superannuation   Based at the Melbourne CBD campus, but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University   About the Role   The Facilities Officer supports day-to-day operational activities across the College of Vocational Education (VE) as part of the Planning & Resources team.   Working under the direction of the Facilities Coordinator, the role provides support across facilities and technology services to help staff access and maintain the equipment, spaces and resources they need to work effectively.   A significant focus of the role is supporting the College's technology assets and services, including staff onboarding, equipment deployment, asset record maintenance and responding to staff requests. The role also contributes to facilities projects, space management activities, technical spaces, events, showcases and other operational initiatives across the College   This role is well suited to someone who enjoys working with technology, solving practical problems, providing excellent customer service and supporting a diverse range of stakeholders.   This Role will Include:   Responding to requests submitted through RMIT's service management systems.   Assisting with the ordering, delivery, setup and replacement of technology equipment and assets.   Maintaining accurate asset records, documentation and registers.   Supporting staff onboarding through the provision of workplace technology and furniture etc.   Assisting with technology refresh activities and equipment lifecycle processes.   Supporting facilities projects, space management activities and minor works initiatives.   Working with staff and support teams to help resolve operational, facilities and technology-related issues.   Providing responsive customer service to staff across the College.   To Be Successful in This Position, You Will Have : Experience providing high-quality administrative, operational or customer-focused support services within a large and complex organisation.   Strong digital literacy and confidence working with technology, systems and equipment.   The ability to learn new systems, platforms and processes quickly.   Strong organisational skills and attention to detail, including the ability to maintain accurate records and manage competing priorities.   Excellent interpersonal skills and a genuine commitment to customer service.   Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain information clearly and work effectively with people of varying levels of technical confidence.   A calm, approachable and solutions-focused manner   Demonstrated initiative and problem-solving skills, including the ability to identify solutions and seek assistance or escalation when required.   Proven ability to work collaboratively as part of a team   Desirable   Experience working with service management, ticketing or request-tracking systems.   Experience supporting technology equipment, asset administration, facilities operations or related services.   Experience working within a tertiary education or similarly complex environment.     Please note that this position is an on-campus role due to the nature of the work.        Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children check.        About the College   The purpose of RMIT’s College of Vocational Education is to empower learners and our industry, community and government partners to succeed in the new world of work. Our five-year strategic roadmap, ALiVE@RMIT, purposefully guides everything we do in vocational education to deliver our vision: to position RMIT as a leading multi-sector provider with global impact and influence.       Led by our Pro Vice Chancellor, the College of VE is reimagining how we deliver vocational education to create unique experiences for our students and partners, so we can:       lead in practice-based learning   empower learners for the future of work   engage industry and community at scale   grow for impact and influence        The College of VE is delivering impact through transformation that creates long-term change.       To Apply    Please submit your CV and cover letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.        For further information about this position, contact Mykayla via mykayla.mccartin@rmit.edu.au .   Please do not submit your application via email.          #LI-Hybrid   Applications Close: 4 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Cloud-Platform-Engineer_JR51491": {
      "title": "Cloud Platform Engineer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for a Cloud Platform Engineer to design, build and operate secure, scalable and reliable cloud platforms on AWS. Working hands-on with infrastructure-as-code, automation, monitoring, security controls and CI/CD, the role will help deliver well-governed cloud services across the organisation. Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Cloud Platform Engineer is a highly skilled technical specialist responsible for designing, building and operating secure, scalable and resilient cloud platforms on Amazon Web Services (AWS). The role focuses on delivering complex technical solutions that enable reliable, cost-effective and well-governed cloud services for the organisation.   Working as a hands-on engineer, the Cloud Platform Engineer designs and implements core platform capabilities such as infrastructure-as-code, automation, monitoring, security controls and CI/CD pipelines. They collaborate closely with solution architects, developers, security specialists and operations teams to ensure that platform services are robust, standards-based and aligned to best practice.   This role provides technical leadership within a defined team, guiding peers on engineering standards, patterns and tooling, and assisting with the resolution of complex incidents and problems. While it does not carry the broad strategic remit of a Lead Engineer, the Cloud Platform Engineer significantly influences engineering quality, platform reliability and the adoption of modern cloud-native practices across their area of responsibility. Reporting Line  Reports to:   Systems Team Lead Reporting lines may be adjusted in line with organisational changes. Key Accountabilities Summary Design, implement and maintain cloud infrastructure services (IaaS, PaaS, SaaS) on AWS/Azure/GCP, including compute, storage, networking and platform services, in collaboration with the Solution Architect team, and support integration with related on-premises systems where required. Participate in technical discussions and evaluations of cloud-native services, container platforms (e.g. Docker, Kubernetes), virtualisation, storage and Windows/Linux operating systems, engaging with vendors and stakeholders to recommend fit-for-purpose solutions.  Support the implementation of secure, scalable and cost-effective cloud architectures (including hybrid and multi-cloud), contributing to the planning and execution of workload migrations from on-premises environments and post-migration optimisation. Maintain up-to-date knowledge of cloud computing, DevOps, Infrastructure as Code (IaC) and cloud security, and support the adoption of modern engineering practices, tools and patterns within the team.  Monitor, analyse and troubleshoot issues related to cloud infrastructure, networking, identity and access management, CI/CD pipelines and associated platforms, working with cross-functional teams to resolve incidents and implement long-term fixes. Develop, maintain and improve architecture artefacts, including design documents, runbooks, technical standards and configuration baselines for cloud platforms and their integration with on-premises systems, ensuring alignment with Solution Architect reference architectures and governance. Ensure the compliance of Cloud solutions and their alignment to agreed RMIT platform and security patterns Key Selection Criteria Bachelor's Degree in IT, Computer Science, Software engineering, Information systems, or any related technology discipline Minimum 3–5 years’ experience as a Cloud/System Engineer or equivalent; cloud certifications (AWS/Azure Associate/Professional) or MCSA/MCSE are preferred. Strong experience across cloud and on‑premises infrastructure: compute, storage, networking, virtualization and containerization; experience with databases (SQL/NoSQL) is an advantage. Hands‑on experience with cloud computing services: AWS (e.g. EC2, S3, RDS, IAM, VPC, Lambda), and/or Azure (e.g. Virtual Machines, Storage, SQL Database, Azure AD, VNets, Functions). Experience with directory and identity stacks: Active Directory, LDAP, DNS, GPO, SAML, ADFS, Multi‑Factor Authentication, Azure AD / Entra ID, Azure AD Connect, and integration of identity between on‑premises and cloud. Experience with virtualisation and cloud platforms: VMware, Hyper‑V and solutions integrating and migrating workloads to AWS/Azure. Experience producing logical and physical design documents for cloud and hybrid environments Experience working with multi‑vendor hardware, software and cloud solutions, including integration of services from multiple vendors. Working knowledge and hands‑on experience with automation, monitoring and Infrastructure as Code, including: Scripting: PowerShell, Python IaC: AWS CloudFormation, Terraform, ARM/Bicep CI/CD and DevOps tools, workload automation, and capacity and cost management in the cloud Ability to demonstrate behaviours consistent with the role and RMIT values, including collaboration, respect, accountability and a strong customer focus. Read more details at Job Description HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 7 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Hanoi/Learning-Success-Coordinator--Hanoi-Campus_JR50359": {
      "title": "Learning Success Coordinator, Hanoi Campus",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT is seeking a Learning Success Coordinator provides operational and administrative support to enable the effective delivery of services, projects, and events across the Student Academic Success WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile . WHAT WE OFFER Expatriates Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates Relocation allowance package of USD $6,000 Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate (and immediate family if applicable) International repatriation flights for the staff, their spouse, and children at the end of their contract. School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to $20,000 per child or $40,000 for two children per year. Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam. Vietnamese candidates Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY Student Academic Success (SAS) provides learning support services that promote academic achievement across RMIT Vietnam programs. The Learning Success Coordinator is responsible for the provision and delivery of learning advice through various study support services and resources offered by SAS including: individual and small group consultation sessions, workshop programs, peer-assisted learning and digital self-access materials through a range of media. In collaboration with the Manager and Learning Advisory team, the Learning Coordinator provides a variety of academic skills development experiences to RMIT students, developed in consultation with academic staff. The Coordinator will assist in maintaining the online presence of SAS and in addition, develop interactive digital resources. The position may involve supervision of project work by other SAS staff. KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES Facilitate face-to-face and online learning activities to support the development of academic literacies, English language, and academic skills across programs and Schools. Adapt, contextualize, and deliver learning activities based on program and student needs, and report on student feedback and the effectiveness of these sessions to key stakeholders. Undertake individual and group consultations with students to provide academic study support across undergraduate and postgraduate programs. Work with relevant staff to support \"At Risk\" students in developing their academic literacy and language skills. Facilitate individualized study planning sessions to help students identify and plan for the achievement of their personal learning goals. Consult with academic staff to analyse student support needs and develop learning experiences and resources aligned with course and program learning outcomes. Provide line management and professional development for direct reports within the Learning Advisory team. Plan, manage, and evaluate strategic projects that develop learning support services and programs, including functional oversight of other Student Academic Success (SAS) staff where required. Provide training, monitoring, and ongoing professional development opportunities for student leaders participating in SAS Peer Assisted Learning programs. Design, develop, and deliver content-integrated digital self-access resources to support academic literacies and language development. Provide project management oversight and reporting for strategic development initiatives aligned with SAS program goals. Actively promote SAS services to the RMIT student body and contribute to ongoing communication and promotional strategies. Provide feedback on student learning opportunities and challenges to SAS and academic teaching teams. Conduct literature reviews and develop recommendations to improve assessment design, communication, and student learning outcomes. Participate in the ongoing monitoring and evaluation of SAS study support services and initiatives. Accurately collect, analyse, and report quantitative and qualitative data using established reporting systems. Contribute to the analysis of service data and communicate findings to key stakeholders. Participate in projects to further develop the resources and services of Student Academic Success. Actively engage with the teaching and learning community within RMIT Vietnam and beyond. Engagement includes contribution to online and social media content produced, as well as special events such as those for prospective or current students, and relevant internal and external conferences and symposiums. Other relevant duties requested by Manager KEY SELECTION CRITERIA A Bachelor’s Degree with major relevant to supporting RMIT Vietnam students such as Commerce, Management, Professional Communications, Education, TESOL/Applied Linguistics, Communications etc. Master’s Degree with Educational focus preferred. At least five years of experience providing academic and study skills support within a secondary or tertiary education environment, or transferrable experience to the role. Well-rounded skills in learning support, English language instruction, and academic literacies development in higher and/or further education institutions. Proven ability to creatively design and engage students with activities that facilitate language and learning skills development in support of learners’ own study goals Research experience using qualitative and quantitative methods for evaluation of service delivery is desirable. Strong report-writing skills Proven ability to accurately maintain complex operational systems and reporting (high attention to detail) Demonstrated awareness of student obstacles in assessment design and constructive alignment. Proven ability to manage projects that deliver successful outcomes. Skilled in the use of technology as a teaching and learning tool with experience in use of educational software for creation of interactive digital resources for online access (e.g. Camtasia, Storyline, Captivate, etc.); experience in use of Learning Management Systems (e.g. Blackboard, Canvas) – especially with use of Learning Analytics tools. Demonstrated commitment to a skills-based, student-centred approach to instruction. Proven ability to creatively design and engage students in activities that facilitate language and learning skills development in support of learners’ own study goals. Strong interpersonal and cross-cultural communication skills for interacting with diverse learners and colleagues in an international university context. Classroom teaching experience (Preferred: Teaching Academic English to tertiary-level students or experience teaching in undergraduate programs) Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 7.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 19 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Casual-English-Language-Teacher--ELICOS--7_JR51717-1": {
      "title": "Casual English Language Teacher",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nPart time\n\nOverview: Casual hourly rates: Teaching – $98.68; non-teaching – $55.14. Both rates include the 25% casual loading. Employment type: Casual, providing ad hoc and emergency teaching cover. We are seeking two Casual English Language Teachers. Location: Work at our modern Melbourne CBD office on Franklin Street, within walking distance of Queen Victoria Market and close to public transport. Who we’re looking for: Experienced English language teachers with demonstrated experience teaching international students. Our values : Passion | Impact | Inclusion | Integrity | Courage | Imagination     About RMIT University Pathways (RMIT UP)    RMIT UP, owned by RMIT University, provides education solutions for students, academics, and professionals in Australia and globally.  Our mission is to offer transformative learning experiences and pathways that open global opportunities, guided by RMIT’s values of inclusion, imagination, integrity, courage, passion, and impact. We place student and customer experience at the forefront of everything we do.  Our key programs include Foundation Studies, ELICOS English for Academic Purposes (EAP), language testing, and Informit, a leading research database focused on Australasian content.  About the role    RMIT UP is seeking experienced and adaptable Casual English Language Teachers to support international students in developing the English language skills they need to succeed in their academic studies. In this role, you will deliver engaging English language classes across a range of levels and programs, primarily providing ad hoc and emergency teaching cover as required. You will create an inclusive and supportive learning environment that responds to students’ diverse learning needs and cultural backgrounds. Working collaboratively with Academic Coordinators and fellow educators, you will deliver the established curriculum, monitor student progress, provide constructive feedback and maintain accurate class records. You will also use appropriate digital learning technologies to support student engagement and contribute to a positive learning experience across face-to-face, online and blended learning environments, as required.  This is an opportunity to make a meaningful contribution to the academic success of international students while working within a collaborative and student-focused educational environment. About You    You are a motivated and student-centred English language educator who is passionate about helping learners achieve their academic goals. You bring recognised TESOL qualifications and teaching experience across different proficiency levels, with the ability to adapt your approach to meet diverse learning needs and cultural backgrounds. You have experience delivering effective English language teaching in face-to-face and online environments and are confident using digital learning technologies to engage students and enhance learning outcomes. You are reflective and committed to continuous professional development, with a proactive approach to improving your teaching practice, exploring new teaching strategies and sharing knowledge with colleagues. You also understand the importance of student wellbeing, inclusive teaching practices and creating a safe, respectful and supportive learning environment. To be successful in this role, you will have: A bachelor’s degree or diploma equivalent to at least three years of full-time study, together with a recognised TESOL qualification, such as CELTA or an equivalent qualification .  TESOL teaching experience in both face-to-face and online environments. Demonstrated ability to teach across a range of English language levels and programs. Confidence using digital learning platforms and educational technologies to support online and blended learning.  Strong interpersonal, communication, organisational and time management skills. A collaborative mindset and a commitment to reflective practice and ongoing professional development. Experience teaching English for Academic Purposes (EAP), offshore TESOL experience, teacher training, postgraduate qualifications in TESOL, Applied Linguistics or Education, and expertise in digital curriculum or assessment design will be highly regarded. What we offer you    We value our people and are committed to providing a supportive, inclusive, and rewarding work environment. As part of our team, you’ll enjoy:    Exclusive employee discounts at leading retailers.    A strong focus on health and wellbeing, Employee Assistance Program (EAP) and access to professional development training via LinkedIn Learning.   A positive workplace culture with a staff reward program, and a staff wellbeing program.   To Apply     Please submit your CV and a cover letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘Apply’ link. Cover letters should be addressed to HR.   Email HR:  applications.rmit.up@rmit.edu.au   (Please note: Applications will NOT be accepted via this email. To apply, submit your application via our website’s careers page  www.rmit.edu.au/up .)    Please note that we review and interview applications on a rolling basis, so we encourage you to apply as soon as possible rather than waiting until the closing date.   For more details, refer to the Position Description: https://www.rmit.edu.au/content/dam/rmit/au/en/careers/position-descriptions/pd-casual-english-language-teacher-rmitup.pdf Pre-employment Checks: Appointment is subject to a successful Working with Children Check and National Police Check.      Our Commitment to Inclusion    At RMIT UP, we foster a culture of safety, wellbeing, and inclusion, ensuring everyone feels valued and respected. We embrace diversity and treat all individuals with fairness, regardless of gender, gender identity, marital or family status, sexual orientation, age, ethnicity, religious beliefs, cultural or socio-economic background, perspectives, or experiences.   We are an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child-safe organisation. We actively encourage applications from all sectors of the community, including Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander candidates.   As a Disability Confident Recruitment Team, we are happy to adjust the recruitment process to meet accessibility needs. Please contact us at  applications.rmit.up@rmit.edu.au  with your preferred communication method, and we will be in touch to discuss your requirements.   Read our Child Safety Policy:  Child Safety Policy    We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to responding to every applicant.    Applications Close: 28 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Minor-Works-Coordinator_JR51386": {
      "title": "Minor Works Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\nFull time\n\nOverview: ​​Full-time​, ​Continuing position​  HEW 7 + 17% Superannuation and Flexible Working Arrangements Based at the ​Melbourne CBD​ campus, ​and hybrid ways of working​ Help shape and improve the spaces our staff and students use every day. As the Minor Works Coordinator, you will play a key role in delivering practical improvements across RMIT's campuses. From workplace moves and furniture upgrades to signage, services installations and small-scale facility improvements, you will help transform customer requests into real outcomes that enhance the University environment. The role is responsible for the coordination of a high volume of minor works requests, ensuring projects are delivered safely, efficiently and with a strong customer focus. About You   You are a proactive and highly organised professional who enjoys working with people, solving problems and managing competing priorities. You thrive in a fast-paced environment, build strong relationships with stakeholders and service providers, and take pride in delivering quality outcomes that make a visible difference to the campus experience. The role involves coordinating multiple project and service activities, working closely with stakeholders, contractors and service providers to deliver successful outcomes. To be successful in this position, you’ll have:   Demonstrated experience coordinating high-volume operational, service delivery or project activities within a complex environment.  Proven ability to manage multiple concurrent tasks, prioritise effectively and deliver outcomes within agreed timeframes.   Strong stakeholder engagement and communication skills, with the ability to build positive relationships and manage expectations across a diverse range of stakeholders.   Experience coordinating contractors, suppliers or service providers to achieve quality outcomes.   Strong organisational, analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to adapt to changing priorities and respond proactively to emerging issues.  Experience using systems and processes to manage workflow, reporting, documentation and service delivery.  Demonstrated ability to work independently while contributing positively to a collaborative team environment.  A commitment to delivering high-quality customer service, with strong attention to detail and a focus on continuous improvement.  Desirable   Experience in property, facilities management, workplace relocation or minor works environments.   Ability to interpret drawings, layouts or scope documentation.  A relevant qualification or equivalent experience in service management, project coordination, facilities, built environment or a related discipline. Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check. About the ​Portfolio​ Property Services has approximately 75 staff and has responsibility for the operation, maintenance, utilisation and enhancement of buildings owned and leased by RMIT University. Property Services oversees construction projects and ensures the provision of physical facilities services. The Group has an operating budget in excess of $75m and current capital projects are significant. RMIT's built environment involves approximately 124 buildings spread across all of RMIT's campuses and sites. The capital stock of the University is diverse and valued at approximately $2 billion and includes heritage and other classifications. Property Services (PSG) consists of the following areas: · Property Operations · Campus Strategy and Management · Strategic Programming · Capital Works & Development · Facilities and Asset Management · Commercial and Leasing To Apply  Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing ​the Key Selection Criteria​ for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.  For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact dustin.nguyen@rmit.edu.au.   Job Description - Minor Works Coordinator Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. #LI-Hybrid Applications Close: 4 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/IT-Security-Analyst_JR51538": {
      "title": "IT Security Analyst",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for an IT Security Analyst to help identify and resolve cyber threats that could affect the confidentiality, availability and integrity of RMIT services. The role also supports security tools, analyses and resolves cyber incidents, and works with operational teams in Vietnam and Australia to strengthen enterprise security and provide advice on the evolving cybersecurity threat landscape. Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The IT Security Analyst is responsible for supporting RMIT in the identification and work-to-resolution of cyber threats that may impact the confidentiality, availability and integrity of RMIT services. The role also supports the configuration and running of security tools to measure, manage and report on the state of Information Security across the enterprise, including the analysis and resolution of cyber incidents. This position actively collaborates with other operational teams in Vietnam and Australia to deliver a secure enterprise and advisory support to help RMIT manage today’s increasing cybersecurity threat landscape. Reporting Line  Reports to:   Security Team Lead Reporting lines may be adjusted in line with organisational changes. Key Accountabilities Summary Support the effective global operation of the Cybersecurity function (eg, Threat Management; Identity Management and Threat Intelligence technologies and processes) Provide advice to IT team with the configuration of Information Security controls across the operating environment Contributes to the design and implementation of pragmatic and efficient cybersecurity defenses Support the activities of Computer Security Incident Response Team (CSIRT) in RMIT Global Support in the monitoring of cybersecurity environmental threats; including periodic cyber technical compliance reporting of our operating environment Ensure the compliance of security standards, processes and procedures by continuously monitoring for vulnerabilities, periodic audits and identifying abnormality throughout the infrastructure Contribute to the continuous improvement of the IT Security function based on an in-depth knowledge of contemporary cybersecurity practices and trends Any other duties as required. Key Selection Criteria Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Security, or related discipline. At least 2 - 3 years of experience in security operations. CEH/Security+ certification is a plus. Well-developed understanding of cybersecurity technologies (eg, Threat Management / Intelligence; Identity management; User access review) Demonstrated good understanding of wide range of IT infrastructure components, from firewalls and intrusion detection systems to network and network protocols to variety of PC platform such as Windows/Linux and understand of their security capacity. Proven ability to prioritise tasks and delivery a quality service to the University. Demonstrated high level interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to liaise effectively with internal and external clients, in order to identify and solve issues. Proven capacity to work under stress and to adapt quickly in a rapidly changing environment. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position and RMIT Values. Read more details at Job Description HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 7 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Network-Engineer_JR51638": {
      "title": "Network Engineer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for a Network Engineer to deploy and maintain IT network infrastructure across its three campuses, including one data centre and one disaster recovery site. The role monitors wired and wireless networks, voice services, bandwidth management and UPS, optimises capacity, and handles network upgrades, incidents, tickets and problems. . Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Network Engineer deploys and maintains IT network infrastructure for RMIT Vietnam. The role monitors the wired and wireless networks, voice services, bandwidth management and UPS across three campuses, including one data centre and one disaster recovery site, and optimises capacity to manage the flow of information. The role also performs network upgrades and handles incidents, tickets and problems at RMIT locations. Reporting Line  Reports to:   Network Team Lead Reporting lines may be adjusted in line with organisational changes. Key Accountabilities Summary Manage day to day network infrastructure operations, design, and review as well as projects to ensure the timely delivery and the ongoing maintenance of network infrastructure to meet the requirements of the University. Manage individual/mini projects and/or enhancements to ensure the timely and cost-effective delivery of digital content that meets the quality standards initially agreed. This includes producing and maintaining detailed project documentation, keeping all key stakeholders up to date with project progress and evaluating the project outcomes. Work on the research into technology business solutions and support the implementation and/or review of systems and technology that support the RMIT Vietnam business, from network perspectives. Analyse, troubleshoot and provide systems business solutions to network related issues, with a view to increasing efficiency of corporate network infrastructure. As an IT team member, contribute to develop and/or enhance network policies, procedures and to support ‘best practice”. Determining company needs and coordinating the development and maintenance of network infrastructures, including but not limited to technologies: Wired, Wireless, Network Security, Voice, Traffic Management, UPS, AAA - Authentication, Authorization, Accounting. Ensuring secure and stable connectivity and analyse & optimize network traffic flows, network performance... Installing, updating, and configuring networking equipment. Monitoring network capacity and performance to keep up with demand in online traffic. Running diagnostic tests and performing repairs. Enhancing network security, as well as documenting network processes, network topology and cabling layouts. Keeping informed of developments in network technologies and infrastructure. Key Selection Criteria Bachelor's degree in computer science, information science, or similar. Certified Cisco CCNP, Aruba ACMP preferred. A minimum of 5-7 years' experience in enterprise networking area. 2-3 years’ experience as Network Engineer. Extensive knowledge of network connectivity, technologies, protocols, and security. Exceptional analytical and problem-solving skills. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and collaboration skills. Great organizational and time management skills. Willingness to be onsite in RMIT’s locations. Availability to perform works outside of business hours. Ability to work without or with minimal supervision from managers. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position and RMIT Values. Read more details at Job Description HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 7 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Senior-Specialist--Planning-and-Commercial_JR51598": {
      "title": "Senior Specialist, Planning and Commercial",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for a Senior Specialist, Planning and Commercial to lead campus and precinct master planning across its Vietnam portfolio, including major developments and redevelopments in Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City. Working with internal teams and external partners, the role will shape the planning, procurement and commercial processes that support long-term investment and delivery decisions. Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Senior Specialist, Planning and Commercial is a senior individual contributor responsible for leading campus and precinct master planning for RMIT’s Vietnam portfolio, including major new developments and redevelopments in Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City. The role translates pre-delivery infrastructure development requirements into regulatory, planning, scoping, supplier selection and oversight, and commercial processes and controls. Partnering with RMIT Procurement, Finance and Risk, and with third parties, the role shapes the planning and commercial foundations that underpin long‑term investment and delivery decisions. Operating in a complex planning, design and construction environment that is heavily reliant on consultants, developers and other contractors, the role plays a critical part in supporting the scoping of required works, sourcing oversight, shaping technical briefs, and supporting commercial and tender processes. A key component of the role is direct engagement with government and relevant authorities to support planning applications, approvals and regulatory compliance, ensuring that campus plans are deliverable within the local planning framework and aligned with RMIT’s global estate strategy and standards. Reporting Line  Reports to:   Head of Commercial Strategy and Planning Reporting lines may be adjusted in line with organisational changes. Key Accountabilities Summary Lead the development, review and refinement of campus and precinct master plans for RMIT Vietnam, providing expert technical advice to senior leaders and project teams Translate strategic objectives (academic plans, enrolment growth, research priorities, student experience, workplace strategy) into spatial concepts, functional briefs and phased development scenarios. Develop and maintain planning scenarios and capacity models (e.g. space demand, utilisation, growth forecasts) to inform business cases, investment planning and staging strategies. Work closely with the Head of Commercial Strategy and Planning to scope required works, define project envelopes and technical parameters, and contribute to robust procurement and delivery strategies. Prepare clear, technically sound input to commercial and tender documentation, including scopes of services, design briefs and evaluation criteria for consultants, developers and contractors. Ensure compliance with RMIT Procurement policies. Lead or coordinate master planning pre-delivery inputs into complex design and construction procurement, including participation in tender evaluation, design reviews and value‑engineering processes. Engage directly with government agencies and relevant authorities on planning applications, approvals, zoning, land‑use, infrastructure, transport and related regulatory matters Coordinate the preparation of planning submissions, support negotiation of planning outcomes, and ensure alignment between planning approvals and campus objectives Manage and coordinate external planning, urban design, architectural and specialist consultants, ensuring deliverables are integrated, technically robust and aligned with RMIT’s requirements and standards. Provide expert campus planning input to major projects through all phases (feasibility, concept, schematic, detailed design, delivery), including interface with project managers, developers and operations teams. Ensure campus planning and development frameworks support RMIT’s sustainability, accessibility, safety and user‑experience goals, and comply with relevant local regulations and international best practice. Produce high‑quality diagrams, plans, reports and presentations to communicate planning options, trade‑offs and recommendations to technical and non‑technical audiences. Collaborate with PMO to integrate master planning space utilisation data and capacity models into the overarching infrastructure performance dashboards. Manage the administration of consultant, contractor and vendor contracts from inception to completion, ensuring compliance with RMIT policies, legal standards and project requirements. Coordinate the drafting, review, approval, execution and archiving of contracts, engagements and variations using RMIT commercial templates and maintaining accurate contract registers. Oversee the commercial and financial administration of infrastructure projects, including business cases, procurement requests, budgets, cost analysis, reporting and payment milestones. Monitor contractual performance, obligations and security instruments; verify payment documentation, manage variations and identify and resolve commercial, financial and compliance risks with relevant stakeholders. Other relevant and supporting PMO projects and tasks, as assigned by the Head of Commercial Strategy and Planning, and the Executive Director, Vietnam Infrastructures Other duties commensurate with the scope of the role. Key Selection Criteria Tertiary qualification in Architecture, Urban Design, Urban Planning, Engineering, Project management or a related discipline; postgraduate qualifications in a relevant field highly desirable. Project management certification (e.g. PMP) is a plus. Significant experience (typically 8+ years) in campus, precinct or large‑scale urban master planning, ideally within higher education, research, health or similarly complex institutional environments. Demonstrated expertise in translating strategy into spatial plans, functional briefs and staged development frameworks, including capacity and scenario modelling. Proven experience working with and managing external planning, design and technical consultants in a complex, multi‑stakeholder environment. Demonstrated experience contributing to scoping and procurement for major design and construction projects, including preparation of technical briefs and input to tender evaluations. Demonstrated commercial acumen, with direct and relevant experience participating in tendering, bid evaluation, and commercial contract negotiation, and contract management for major capital works or property projects, complementing strong planning and technical capability. Deep, proven understanding of planning and regulatory frameworks in Vietnam (or similar jurisdictions), with demonstrated experience interacting with government and authorities on planning applications and approvals process.  Experience with both Hanoi and HCMC authorities in real estate projects is a major plus. High‑level analytical, problem‑solving and visual communication skills, with the ability to present complex planning issues clearly to senior, non‑technical stakeholders. Strong interpersonal, negotiation and influencing skills, with the ability to work effectively across cultures and with senior internal and external stakeholders. Proven capability to drive and manage changes, with a result-oriented mindset. Ability to work in a fast paced, lean team environment with the associated flexibility. Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English. Fluency in Vietnamese is mandatory to effectively negotiate with local authorities and government agencies. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. Read more details at Job Description HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 7 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Senior-Specialist--Performance-reporting-and-Commercial_JR51599": {
      "title": "Senior Specialist, Performance reporting and Commercial",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is looking for a Senior Specialist, Performance Reporting and Commercial to develop and maintain integrated performance reporting, analytics and governance across its infrastructure portfolio. The role will support major campus development programs in Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City. Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment. Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile WHAT WE OFFER Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! POSITION SUMMARY The Senior Specialist, Performance Reporting and Commercial is a senior individual contributor within the Vietnam Infrastructure function responsible for designing, implementing and maintaining integrated performance reporting, analytics and governance frameworks across RMIT Vietnam’s infrastructure portfolio, including major campus development programs in Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh City. The role consolidates project, commercial, operational and stakeholder data into clear, actionable insights that support executive decision-making, risk management, benefits realisation and portfolio performance oversight. Working closely with the Head of Commercial Strategy and Planning, Associate Director, Infrastructure Program Delivery and external delivery partners, the position also supports the development of performance requirements, reporting frameworks and data governance standards embedded within major infrastructure procurements and contracts. The role operates across all areas of the Vietnam Infrastructure function and contributes to strengthening commercial oversight, portfolio governance and data-driven decision-making across planning, design, construction and operationalisation activities. In addition to its technical and analytical focus, the role is expected to bring a commercial mindset — informed by exposure to tendering, bid evaluation or contract negotiation — so that performance frameworks are grounded in sound commercial judgement rather than technical reporting alone. Reporting Line  Reports to:   Head of Commercial Strategy and Planning Reporting lines may be adjusted in line with organisational changes. Key Accountabilities Summary Design and maintain an integrated performance reporting framework for Vietnam Infrastructure, covering capital project delivery, commercial performance, space utilisation, sustainability, safety and service outcomes. Define, track and continuously refine key performance indicators (KPIs) and metrics for major infrastructure programs, projects and external partners (consultants, developers, contractors). Actively audit and enforce data-reporting compliance from external Vietnamese developers, consultants, and contractors, ensuring data integrity at the source. Develop and maintain an Early Warning System within the PMO dashboards to flag potential commercial, regulatory, or schedule slippages in major programs. Work with the Head of Commercial Strategy and Planning and Associate Director, Infrastructure Program Delivery to scope performance and reporting requirements for major works, ensuring they are embedded in procurement documentation and contracts. Provide technical input into tender documentation (e.g. KPIs, reporting templates, data requirements, performance regimes) and participate in tender evaluations from a performance and analytics perspective. Consolidate and integrate data from multiple sources (project management systems, finance, contracts, facilities, consultants, surveys) into accurate, timely dashboards and reports for executive and governance audiences Analyse trends, variances and drivers of performance, providing clear insights and recommendations to support decision‑making, course corrections and continuous improvement. Support benefits realisation planning and tracking for major campus investments, including post‑occupancy and post‑implementation reviews Ensure robust data governance, quality assurance and consistency of definitions across the Vietnam Infrastructure portfolio, and align with global RMIT property and analytics standards where applicable. Develop and maintain self‑service reporting tools and visualisations (e.g. using Power BI, Tableau or similar) that enable leaders to access reliable performance information quickly. Act as a subject‑matter expert on performance reporting and analytics within Vietnam Infrastructure, advising project teams and senior leaders on measurement strategies and options.·       Collaborate closely with other PMO team members and cross-functional working groups (Finance, Legal and Contract management teams) to ensure that performance measurement and commercial frameworks are integrated and mutually reinforcing. Lead the definition, standardisation and alignment of data structures across Project Delivery (schedule), Commercial (cost/contracts) and project teams, establishing a single source of truth for the PMO’s executive reporting. Manage the administration of consultant, contractor and vendor contracts from inception to completion, ensuring compliance with RMIT policies, legal standards and project requirements. Coordinate the drafting, review, approval, execution and archiving of contracts, engagements and variations using RMIT commercial templates and maintaining accurate contract registers. Oversee the commercial and financial administration of infrastructure projects, including business cases, procurement requests, budgets, cost analysis, reporting and payment milestones. Monitor contractual performance, obligations and security instruments; verify payment documentation, manage variations and identify and resolve commercial, financial and compliance risks with relevant stakeholders. Contribute a commercial lens to major works tendering and bid evaluation processes, including reviewing commercial/pricing schedules, contract terms and value-for-money considerations alongside performance and KPI criteria. Support the Head of Commercial Strategy and Planning in developing commercial performance benchmarks and lessons-learned analysis from past tenders and contracts, to inform future procurement and negotiation strategy. Other relevant and supporting PMO projects and tasks, as assigned by the Head of Commercial Strategy and Planning, and the Executive Director, Vietnam Infrastructure. Other duties commensurate with the scope of the role. Key Selection Criteria Tertiary qualification in Business, Data Analytics, Engineering, Property/Construction, Finance, Statistics, Information Systems or a related discipline; postgraduate qualifications desirable. Significant experience (typically 8+ years) in performance reporting, business intelligence, data analytics or project controls; preferably with a background in Project Controls, Commercial Analytics, or PMO Consultancy within international real estate consultancies, major property developers, corporate infrastructure environments or higher education organisations.  Demonstrated expertise in designing and operating KPI frameworks and performance dashboards for large, complex programs, including external partner performance. Understanding of key metrics relevant to capital projects and property portfolios (time, cost, quality, risk, space utilisation, lifecycle costs, sustainability, safety and customer satisfaction). Demonstrated ability to clean, transform, and standardise unstructured or manual datasets from diverse third-party sources into a centralised reporting environment (Excel/BI or equivalent platform). Proven experience navigating the data and reporting constraints typical of the Vietnam construction and property sectors, including familiarity with local project documentation and progress claim processes. Demonstrated commercial acumen, with direct experience participating in tendering, bid evaluation, and commercial contract negotiation, and contract management for major capital works or property projects, complementing strong analytical and reporting capability. Working knowledge of commercial and contract management principles (e.g. contract terms, payment mechanisms, variations, claims) sufficient to embed commercial risk indicators within performance reporting frameworks. Experience contributing to scoping, procurement and assurance for major projects, including defining performance metrics, reporting requirements and data obligations in contracts. Strong skills in data modelling, analysis and visualisation, using modern BI tools (e.g. Power BI, Tableau) and advanced Excel or equivalent. Proven ability to synthesise complex datasets into clear, actionable insights and communicate them effectively to senior, non‑technical audiences. High attention to detail with strong data governance, validation and quality‑assurance practices. Excellent stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to work collaboratively across functions in a matrix environment (PMO, finance, legal, property, operations) and with external consultants and contractors. Proven capability to drive and manage changes, with a result-oriented mindset. Ability to work in a fast paced, lean team environment with the associated flexibility. Excellent written and verbal communication skills in both English and Vietnamese, to effectively interface with global RMIT executives and local external partners. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. Read more details at Job Description HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible. Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit. English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines). Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process. RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working. IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 7 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Lecturer-Associate-Lecturer-in-Digital-Media--HCI-Design-_JR51371": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Associate Lecturer in Digital Media (HCI Design)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Lecturer/ Associate Lecturer, Digital Media to join our academic community and deliver high-quality teaching, and student engagement. This is an exciting opportunity for an educator-scholar who is passionate about shaping future-ready graduates and contributing to impactful research.  WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER Expatriates   Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates  Relocation allowance package from US$6,000  Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate and direct dependents (if applicable)  International repatriation flights for the staff and direct dependents at the end of their contract.  School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to US$20,000 per child or US$40,000 for two children per year.  Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Vietnamese candidates   Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates.  13th month Tet bonus   Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Other benefits   Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays)  Professional development and career advancement  Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources  A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!  SCHOOL OF COMMUNICATION & DESIGN (SCD) The School of Communication & Design is committed to providing an international learning environment that encourages cultural awareness, critical thinking, experimentation and — above all — the ability to think differently. Our students develop the competence, confidence and professionalism needed for successful careers in communication, design, games, fashion, film and video, and languages. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us/schools-and-centres/school-communication-design THE BACHELOR OF DESIGN (DIGITAL MEDIA) PROGRAM In an increasingly digital world, driven by technological advancement, there is a profound need for professionals who understand timeless design principles and who can navigate future challenges as they arise. The Digital Media program provides a studio learning environment for the development of leading specialists in digital design across four main areas of action (pathways): • Interaction • Animation • Imaging • Sound ABOUT THE ROLE We are currently seeking applicants for an Associate Lecturer or Lecturer (full-time) in the BA Design (Digital Media) program with expertise in one or more areas related to digital design (see the Key Selection Criteria section below). To comply with Vietnam’s employment requirement, all overseas candidates must have at least 3 years University teaching experience. At the Associate Lecturer scale, the position will be required to teach and conduct classes in disciplines relevant to their field of expertise and assist in the academic and administrative, consultative and coordination tasks involved with these courses. Functions associated with the position include presentation of lectures and tutorials, assessment of students, and course administration in line with the University’s quality assurance requirements. The Associate Lecturer is expected to develop an emerging research profile aligned with the school’s research priorities and the University’s research strategy based on opportunity. It is expected that the Associate Lecturer will work under support and guidance to develop expertise in teaching and research with an increasing degree of autonomy. At the Lecturer scale, the position is expected to contribute to the teaching and research activities of the University, in disciplines related to their field of expertise. Specifically, the Lecturer is responsible for carrying out teaching activities within undergraduate programs and for maintaining and advancing their scholarly, research and/or professional capabilities. The lecturer is expected to contribute to the school’s research culture through research activities appropriate to career state. The Lecturer is also expected to actively promote the program by establishing and maintaining memberships, links, and partnerships with academic, industry and professional communities. The Lecturer is expected to work collaboratively and collegially with fellow academics within the teaching team, and update colleagues and students on developments in their subject area or specialisation. Reports to: Associate Program Manager, Digital Media Key Accountabilities: • Undergraduate teaching including designing, conducting and moderating assessment, implementing improvements informed by peer review, course evaluation and/or student feedback. • Undertake independent professional activities, scholarship and/or conduct high quality research activities appropriate to the profession or discipline, publishing research results (traditional and/or non-traditional) in high quality outlets as lead or co-author, preparing and submitting external research funding applications, and supervising higher degree by research candidates.  • Undertake administration duties and participate in University governance activities related to the position. • Adhere to the Academic Expectations and Development Framework of RMIT Vietnam. Key Selection Criteria: 1. For Associate Lecturer: A Master degree in the relevant discipline and having commenced or enrolled to commence in Doctoral course is preferred. 2. For Lecturer: PhD or equivalent relevant Doctoral qualification from a recognised institution, with an emerging to established track record and growing recognition for research. 3. Demonstrated ability to prepare and deliver programs at the undergraduate level, including online delivery, and the ability to produce high-quality curriculum or program materials. 4. Proven expertise in two or more of the following areas to be evidenced through the submission of a portfolio: a. UI/UX Human-Computer Interaction (HCI) Design b. Coding and development for the web c. Scripting and programming for Screen-based Interactions d. Digital Design Foundations and Principles   5. Ability to guide students in conceptual, aesthetic, and technical development related to their discipline. 6. Ability to undertake course coordination role. 7. Demonstrated capacity to work effectively with and negotiate sensitively with students, especially on issues related to effective learning. 8. For Lecturer, additionally: a. Emerging track record and recognition for quality research outputs that contribute to existing Discipline and School research areas evidenced by publications, development of new research initiatives, contribution to competitive research funding opportunities, and engagement with industry, community, and professional partners . b. Ability to supervise or develop capacity to supervise higher-degree research candidates. c. Ability to build effective networks with colleagues and generate alternative funding projects through effective liaison with industry and government. 9. Teaching experience: Recent and sustained performance regarding student outcomes, student experience, and feedback; combined with experience and skill in a range of teaching settings. 10. Excellent interpersonal and communications skills appropriate for interacting with higher degree by research candidates, staff, and industry, together with a strong commitment to teamwork and multidisciplinary collaboration. 11. Ability to operate within own discipline and cross-disciplinary/multidisciplinary teams to achieve department and University strategic outcomes. 12. Ability to work with external partners, industries, organisations, and communities and can operate effectively to address complex issues or seek opportunities. 13. Ability to motivate, develop, and inspire others through discipline leadership in the University environment. 14. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values, and RMIT Leadership Model. HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit  resume, cover letter and portfolio . Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible.  COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam   Applications Close: 14 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Lecturer-Associate-Lecturer-in-Digital-Media--Digital-Animation-_JR51370": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Associate Lecturer in Digital Media (Digital Animation)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Lecturer/ Associate Lecturer, Digital Media to join our academic community and deliver high-quality teaching, and student engagement. This is an exciting opportunity for an educator-scholar who is passionate about shaping future-ready graduates and contributing to impactful research.  WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER Expatriates   Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates  Relocation allowance package from US$6,000  Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate and direct dependents (if applicable)  International repatriation flights for the staff and direct dependents at the end of their contract.  School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to US$20,000 per child or US$40,000 for two children per year.  Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Vietnamese candidates   Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates.  13th month Tet bonus   Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance  Other benefits   Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays)  Professional development and career advancement  Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources  A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!  SCHOOL OF COMMUNICATION & DESIGN (SCD) The School of Communication & Design is committed to providing an international learning environment that encourages cultural awareness, critical thinking, experimentation and — above all — the ability to think differently. Our students develop the competence, confidence and professionalism needed for successful careers in communication, design, games, fashion, film and video, and languages. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us/schools-and-centres/school-communication-design THE BACHELOR OF DESIGN (DIGITAL MEDIA) PROGRAM In an increasingly digital world, driven by technological advancement, there is a profound need for professionals who understand timeless design principles and who can navigate future challenges as they arise. The Digital Media program provides a studio learning environment for the development of leading specialists in digital design across four main areas of action (pathways): • Interaction • Animation • Imaging • Sound ABOUT THE ROLE We are currently seeking applicants for an Associate Lecturer or Lecturer (full-time) in the BA Design (Digital Media) program with expertise in one or more areas related to digital design (see the Key Selection Criteria section below). To comply with Vietnam’s employment requirement, all overseas candidates must have at least 3 years University teaching experience. At the Associate Lecturer scale, the position will be required to teach and conduct classes in disciplines relevant to their field of expertise and assist in the academic and administrative, consultative and coordination tasks involved with these courses. Functions associated with the position include presentation of lectures and tutorials, assessment of students, and course administration in line with the University’s quality assurance requirements. The Associate Lecturer is expected to develop an emerging research profile aligned with the school’s research priorities and the University’s research strategy based on opportunity. It is expected that the Associate Lecturer will work under support and guidance to develop expertise in teaching and research with an increasing degree of autonomy. At the Lecturer scale, the position is expected to contribute to the teaching and research activities of the University, in disciplines related to their field of expertise. Specifically, the Lecturer is responsible for carrying out teaching activities within undergraduate programs and for maintaining and advancing their scholarly, research and/or professional capabilities. The lecturer is expected to contribute to the school’s research culture through research activities appropriate to career state. The Lecturer is also expected to actively promote the program by establishing and maintaining memberships, links, and partnerships with academic, industry and professional communities. The Lecturer is expected to work collaboratively and collegially with fellow academics within the teaching team, and update colleagues and students on developments in their subject area or specialisation. Reports to: Associate Program Manager, Digital Media Key Accountabilities: • Undergraduate teaching including designing, conducting and moderating assessment, implementing improvements informed by peer review, course evaluation and/or student feedback. • Undertake independent professional activities, scholarship and/or conduct high quality research activities appropriate to the profession or discipline, publishing research results (traditional and/or non-traditional) in high quality outlets as lead or co-author, preparing and submitting external research funding applications, and supervising higher degree by research candidates.  • Undertake administration duties and participate in University governance activities related to the position. • Adhere to the Academic Expectations and Development Framework of RMIT Vietnam. Key Selection Criteria: 1. For Associate Lecturer: A Master degree in the relevant discipline and having commenced or enrolled to commence in Doctoral course is preferred. 2. For Lecturer: PhD or equivalent relevant Doctoral qualification from a recognised institution, with an emerging to established track record and growing recognition for research. 3. Demonstrated ability to prepare and deliver programs at the undergraduate level, including online delivery, and the ability to produce high-quality curriculum or program materials. 4. Proven expertise in three or more of the following areas to be evidenced through the submission of a portfolio: a. 3D Design and Animation b. Digital Video and VFX (Digital Compositing and Postproduction) c. Previs and Art Design for Digital Storytelling d. Digital Time-based Narratives and Production e. Digital Design Foundations and Principles   5. Ability to guide students in conceptual, aesthetic, and technical development related to their discipline. 6. Ability to undertake course coordination role. 7. Demonstrated capacity to work effectively with and negotiate sensitively with students, especially on issues related to effective learning. 8. For Lecturer, additionally: a. Emerging track record and recognition for quality research outputs that contribute to existing Discipline and School research areas evidenced by publications, development of new research initiatives, contribution to competitive research funding opportunities, and engagement with industry, community, and professional partners . b. Ability to supervise or develop capacity to supervise higher-degree research candidates. c. Ability to build effective networks with colleagues and generate alternative funding projects through effective liaison with industry and government. 9. Teaching experience: Recent and sustained performance regarding student outcomes, student experience, and feedback; combined with experience and skill in a range of teaching settings. 10. Excellent interpersonal and communications skills appropriate for interacting with higher degree by research candidates, staff, and industry, together with a strong commitment to teamwork and multidisciplinary collaboration. 11. Ability to operate within own discipline and cross-disciplinary/multidisciplinary teams to achieve department and University strategic outcomes. 12. Ability to work with external partners, industries, organisations, and communities and can operate effectively to address complex issues or seek opportunities. 13. Ability to motivate, develop, and inspire others through discipline leadership in the University environment. 14. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values, and RMIT Leadership Model. HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit  resume, cover letter and portfolio . Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible.  COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam   Applications Close: 14 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Deputy-Dean--Research---Innovation_JR51646-1": {
      "title": "Deputy Dean, Research & Innovation",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-20\nPart time\n\nOverview: Part-time (0.5 FTE), 3-year fixed term position  Salary Academic Level E ($227,847 p.a. pro rata for part-time) + 17% Superannuation and Flexible Working Arrangements Based at the Bundoora West campus, with work at other RMIT campuses and clinical partner sites as required About the Role Shape the research and innovation agenda of RMIT’s School of Medicine. RMIT, in partnership with Northern Health and other stakeholders, is in the process of establishing a new progressive Medical School to train doctors of the future, driven by excellence through equity. The program combines the technological prowess of RMIT and the innovative and culturally diverse network of Northern Health to meet the needs of the communities we serve and address national health workforce needs.   As Deputy Dean, Research & Innovation, you will bring your research expertise and academic leadership to a role with scope to influence research excellence, research training and impact. Reporting directly to the Dean of Medicine and joining the School Executive, you will help shape and deliver RMIT’S Medical research vision, priorities and performance.  This opportunity will appeal to an established clinician research leader who combines strategic vision with the ability to bring people and partnerships together. Working with the Dean, School Executive, academic leaders, research centres, institutes and external partners, you will develop and deliver the School’s research and innovation strategy. You will foster a collaborative culture of research excellence, grow interdisciplinary and translational research, and strengthen RMIT’s national and international reputation for research impact. You will identify emerging research opportunities and build productive partnerships across RMIT’s interdisciplinary research community, Northern Health, the wider health sector, industry and community. By strengthening sustainable research capability and capacity, you will enable collaborations that translate discovery into improved health outcomes, inform policy and clinical practice, and deliver wider societal benefit. Central to your leadership will be championing research excellence and innovation, supporting higher degree by research (HDR) students to succeed, and developing the research workforce. You will align these efforts with School, College and University priorities, helping build the people and capability that underpin lasting research impact. To be successful in this position, you’ll have: Strong strategic leadership skills and demonstrated ability to build and lead transformational research initiatives and/or platforms for impact. A strong record of research, academic and professional achievement in an area relevant to the School, and the capacity to exercise research leadership to enhance the standing of RMIT nationally and internationally.  Demonstrated understanding of current/emerging government priorities and policies in relation to research and innovation.  Demonstrated capability in translating organisational goals into tangible impact through collaboration and innovation. High level interpersonal, communication, influencing and negotiating skills including the ability to work effectively in a collegiate environment and to build productive relationships within the organisation and externally.  Demonstrated leadership in relation to University governance, financial management, quality, safety and accreditation standards. Demonstrated record of achievement in establishing new programs, initiatives and platforms in line with organisational goals and optimising external partnerships, grant funding and research impact. Essential Registered medical practitioner with valid and unrestricted AHPRA registration. PhD in a relevant discipline combined with knowledge and achievements that meet the professorial criteria. Demonstrated senior experience in clinical research and academic leadership. Demonstrated success in securing research funding through grants, partnerships and philanthropy. Eligibility to work in Australia. Capacity to work across RMIT campuses and clinical partner sites as required. Desirable Fellowship of a relevant medical college or equivalent professional body is highly desirable. An extensive record of scholarly achievement in medical research. Experience in research in artificial intelligence, virtual health or medical technology development. An active clinician with clinical responsibilities.   Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check. About the RMIT STEM College LEARN! GROW! DO! Together transforming the world through STEM   The STEM College holds a leading position and expertise in the science, technology, engineering, mathematics, and health (STEM) fields. We are uniquely positioned to influence and partner with industry, as never before. STEM College is a community of exceptional STEM researchers, teachers, inventors, designers and game-changers, supported by talented professional staff.  We offer higher education programs across all STEM disciplines at the Bachelor, Master and PhD levels, and ensure our students experience an education that is work-aligned and life-changing.   The College is renowned for its exemplary research in many STEM areas including advanced manufacturing and design; computing technologies; health innovation and translational medicine; nano materials and devices; and sustainable systems. Our brilliant researchers attract funding from government and industry sources. Industry is at the heart of what we do. It ensures our research has real world impact, and our students are truly work-ready. We have established new hubs of industry-connected digital innovation and endeavour and are engaging with global STEM organisations at scale.   Our diversity and shared values empower our work, and we are proud of the College’s inclusive, caring culture. We offer a safe, dynamic work environment, and support every member of our community to achieve their potential.   For further information about the STEM College please visit the following site: https://www.rmit.edu.au/about/schools-colleges/stem-college     In STEM we CARE – Collaboration, Accountability, Respect & Empowerment To Apply  To apply, please submit your CV and covering letter using the ‘Apply’ link at the top of this page. In your covering letter, please address the following: Describe how you have used high- level interpersonal, communication, influencing and negotiation skills to work collaboratively and build productive relationships within and outside your organisation . Outline your research , academic and professional achievements relevant to the School, including your senior-level experience in clinical research and academic leadership. Use examples to show how you have improved research outcomes and how you would build on this experience to benefit the School and College and strengthen the School’s national and international standing . Provide examples of your senior-level experience in developing and establishing new programs or services , including the partnerships and infrastructure you built to support their delivery . For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Melissa Serrurier via email melissa.serrurier@rmit.edu.au    For further information regarding recruitment processes, please contact Jennifer Pham, Senior Talent Acquisition Advisor via email at jennifer.pham2@rmit.edu.au Please do not share your application to this email address.     Position Description – Deputy Dean, Research & Innovation Applications Close: 4 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Senior-Lecturer---Computing-Technologies_JR40983": {
      "title": "Lecturer/Senior Lecturer, Computing Technologies (Cyber Security)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a  Lecturer/Senior Lecturer, Computing Technologies  to join our academic community and deliver high-quality teaching, research, and student engagement. This is an exciting opportunity for an educator-scholar who is passionate about shaping future-ready graduates and contributing to impactful research.  WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER Expatriates Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates Relocation allowance package of USD $6,000 Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate (and immediate family if applicable) International repatriation flights for the staff, their spouse, and children at the end of their contract. School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to $20,000 per child or $40,000 for two children per year. Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam. Vietnamese candidates Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! ABOUT THE SCHOOL OF SCIENCE, ENGINEERING AND TECHNOLOGY (SSET) For further information about SSET, please visit our website: https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us/schools-and-centres/school-of-science-engineering-and-technology ABOUT THE ROLE The Lecturer/ Senior Lecturer is expected to contribute to the teaching and research efforts of the University, in disciplines related to their field of expertise. Specifically, the Lecturer/Senior Lecturer is responsible for carrying out teaching activities within undergraduate, Masters and Graduate Diploma programs and for maintaining and advancing their scholarly, research and/or professional capabilities. The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer is also expected to actively promote the program by establishing and maintaining memberships, links and partnerships with academic, industry and professional communities. The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer is expected to work collaboratively and collegially with fellow academics within the teaching team, and update colleagues and students on developments in their subject area or specialisation. The Lecturer/Senior Lecturer may be responsible for course coordination. Reports to: Senior Program Manager, Computing Technologies KEY ACCOUNTIBILITIES   Undertake independent teaching undergraduate level courses in the Bachelor of Information Technology program. Teaching duties include writing course materials; teaching lecture, lab, and tutorial sessions; helping students; designing, conducting, and grading assessments; implementing improvements informed by course evaluation activities and student feedback. Undertake administration duties, which may include course coordination role. Adhere to the requirements of the Academic Expectations and Development Framework of RMIT Vietnam. KEY SELECTION CRITERIA 1/ PhD or equivalent relevant Doctoral qualification in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering, or relevant disciplines. 2/ Minimum 3 years of teaching experience in English-speaking universities. 3/ Proven teaching proficiency and curriculum development in the following areas: Cyber Security and Cloud Technologies (preferred) Programming (Python, Java, C/C++, Web) 4/ Demonstrated ability to prepare and deliver programs at undergraduate level, including online delivery, and the ability to produce high quality curriculum or program materials. 5/ Ability to undertake course coordination role. 6/ Demonstrated capacity to work effectively with and to negotiate sensitively with students especially on issues related to effective learning. 7/ Recent and sustained performance regarding student outcomes, student experience and feedback; combined with experience and skill in a range of teaching settings. 8/ Recognised research profile including substantial record of research outputs in high quality journals. 9/ Ability to operate within own discipline and cross-disciplinary/multidisciplinary teams to achieve department and University strategic outcomes. 10/ Ability to work with external partners, industries, organisations, and communities and can operate effectively to address complex issues or seek opportunities. Details about the job and its key selection criteria can be found in this Job Description HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible.  COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application   is submitted through   our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant   about scams asking   for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 18 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Associate-Professor--Computing-Technologies_JR47870": {
      "title": "Associate Professor, Computing Technologies (AI/ Cyber Security)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking an Associate Professor, Computing Technologies  to join our academic community and foster excellence in teaching and research efforts of the School, within the RMIT Vietnam University and globally with the community, professional, commercial and industrial sectors. WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER Expatriates Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates Relocation allowance package of USD $6,000 Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate (and immediate family if applicable) International repatriation flights for the staff, their spouse, and children at the end of their contract. School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to $20,000 per child or $40,000 for two children per year. Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam. Vietnamese candidates Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! ABOUT THE SCHOOL OF SCIENCE, ENGINEERING AND TECHNOLOGY (SSET) The School of Science, Engineering & Technology (SSET) is a dynamic and forward-thinking institution dedicated to fostering innovation and addressing critical global and regional challenges. Our mission is twofold: to cultivate the next generation of leaders and innovators in technology and science within an international learning environment, and to pioneer world-class research that delivers tangible, real-world impact. We empower our students with the knowledge, critical thinking skills, and integrity required for successful careers in fields as diverse as computing, engineering, aviation, psychology, and health sciences. Our research strategy is focused on leveraging our expertise to make a significant difference in sectors vital to Vietnam's future, including healthcare, semiconductor, advanced manufacturing, mental health, education, food technology and smart cities. This commitment to applied innovation not only produces impactful outcomes, but also ensures our academic programs remain relevant, providing students with the skills and motivation to become future leaders and innovators. Our research activities are concentrated on five key interdisciplinary research clusters that represent our areas of strength and future ambition: -         Community, Health and Wellbeing -         Artificial Intelligence in Health Informatics -         Digital Innovation for Environmental and Societal Impact -         Emerging Technologies in Education -         Semiconductor and Industry 4.0 For further information about SSET, please visit our website: https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us/schools-and-centres/school-of-science-engineering-and-technology ABOUT THE ROLE The Associate Professor will provide leadership and foster excellence in learning & teaching, research, and industry engagement efforts of the School, within the University, and with the community, professional, commercial, and industrial sectors. More specifically, the Associate Professor is responsible for providing original, innovative, and distinguished contributions to the School’s programs, particularly in the disciplines of computer science, information technology, software engineering and artificial intelligence, and for maintaining and advancing their scholarly, research, and/or professional capabilities relevant to those disciplines at a national and international level. The Associate Professor can be expected to provide strategic leadership in learning and teaching or research and scholarship, teach, and make a significant contribution to teaching and learning in the disciplines to improve student learning outcomes. The Associate Professor will significantly contribute to the School's planning and strategic direction, by taking on academic leadership roles involving participation in various committees within the School, Program Portfolio, and University and external to the University, as appropriate. This position will provide leadership and support for partnerships and engagement activities ensuring they are appropriately and successfully coordinated, implemented, and continuously improved. These activities will involve industry partners, Government agencies, and University stakeholders. Reports to:   Senior Program Manager, Computing Technologies Portfolio Reporting lines may be adjusted in line with organisational changes. KEY ACCOUNTIBILITIES   Teaching delivery and student experience: Undertake independent teaching at undergraduate, honours, postgraduate, and corporate training levels. Design, deliver and continuously improve learning activities that enhance student engagement, wellbeing, and employability, informed by student feedback and course/program evaluation. Assessment design, moderation and academic standards: Design, conduct and moderate assessment in line with University policy and quality assurance requirements. Ensure assessment integrity, consistency of standards, and appropriate documentation, including moderation processes and continuous improvement actions. Program and curriculum leadership: Lead the advancement of teaching within the disciplines, including developing new courses/programs, initiating program improvements, strengthening academic standards, and supporting accreditation and regulatory compliance. Research leadership, impact and collaboration: Conduct impactful research and drive national and international contributions to the discipline. Build and lead interdisciplinary research teams; lead publication strategies and high-quality research outputs; develop and sustain collaborations with RMIT Melbourne and external partners; and support translation of research outcomes into practice, policy, industry or community impact. Research funding: Identify, attract and secure external research funding to support sustained research growth. HDR supervision and researcher development: Supervise and mentor HDR candidates and contribute to researcher development, including mentoring early career researchers and building capability within the discipline/research group. Governance, service and external engagement: Contribute significantly to internal and external university governance and collegial life, including participation in committees, Industry Advisor Committee, academic leadership roles, recruitment/outreach activities, and engagement with relevant professional bodies and partners. Alignment with academic expectations. Other duties commensurate with the scope of the role. Adhere to the requirements of the Academic Expectations and Development Framework of RMIT Vietnam. KEY SELECTION CRITERIA Qualifications: PhD (or equivalent doctoral qualification) in Computer Science, Information Technology, Software Engineering, or a closely related discipline. Expertise : Artificial Intelligence or Cyber Security .   International research profile and quality outputs: An internationally recognised research profile aligned to at least one of the School of Science, Engineering & Technology research clusters: (1) AI in Health Informatics, (2) Community Health and Wellbeing, (3) Digital Innovation for Environmental and Societal Impact, (4) Emerging Technologies in Education, and (5) Semiconductors and Industry 4.0. Evidence of sustained, high-quality research outputs in discipline-relevant leading journals and conferences; research impact and recognition appropriate to Associate Professor level (e.g., citations, invited talks, awards, leadership roles); and scholarly service such as editorial and peer-review activities. Research leadership and strategy: Demonstrated ability to lead research agendas and deliver outcomes, including establishing and nurturing interdisciplinary research teams, mentoring early-career researchers, setting a coherent 3-5 year research strategy aligned with School and University priorities, and contributing to national and international collaborations. Competitive funding and project delivery: Proven track record of identifying, securing and managing external research funding (or equivalent competitive funding), including oversight of budgets, reporting, milestones, risk management, and delivery of funded-project outcomes. Research integrity, ethics and governance: Commitment to responsible conduct of research, including ethics and compliance requirements, data management/governance, authorship and publication integrity, and adherence to relevant University and regulatory standards. Impact, translation and external engagement: Ability to translate research into real-world impact beyond academia, including engagement with industry, professional bodies, NGOs, government and community partners; evidence of influence on policy and practice where relevant (e.g., advisory roles, consultations, uptake, media engagement); and ability to communicate research effectively to non-academic audiences Vietnam and Asia-Pacific contribution: Capability in strengthening Vietnam’s and the Asia-Pacific region’s innovation ecosystem through capacity-building, technology adoption, partnership development, and/or international collaboration that strengthens RMIT’s research standing and local relevance. Teaching excellence and curriculum leadership: Proven teaching proficiency across relevant areas (e.g., Computer Science, IT, Software Engineering, AI, Data Science), with evidence of high-quality teaching practice, effective assessment design and moderation, and sustained improvement in student outcomes and student experience across diverse learning contexts. Program development, accreditation and quality assurance: Demonstrated experience in curriculum and program development and continuous improvement, including student-centred and inclusive learning design. Experience contributing to (or leading) accreditation and quality assurance processes (e.g., ACS, Engineers Australia), and a strong commitment to academic integrity. HDR supervision and researcher development: Significant experience supervising higher degree by research candidates, with evidence of effective supervision practices (e.g., timely milestones, completions, and/or high-quality outputs with candidates), and a commitment to researcher development and mentoring. Leadership and collegial contribution: Strong leadership capability, including the ability to motivate and develop staff, contribute effectively to the management of teams, lead through influence across disciplines, and support a positive, inclusive and high-performing culture. Stakeholder engagement, communication and negotiation: Exceptional interpersonal, communication and negotiation skills, with demonstrated ability to build productive relationships with senior stakeholders and external partners, manage complex collaborations, and achieve agreed outcomes. Governance, risk and resource stewardship: Demonstrated understanding of, and commitment to, University financial, governance and quality management systems, including prudent resource stewardship, compliance, and accountability Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model. For full details of the accountability, please refer to the Job Description HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible.  COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application   is submitted through   our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant   about scams asking   for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 18 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/XMLNAME--Casual--Associate-Lecturer--Digital-Media_JR45310-1": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer, Digital Media (3D Animation)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-19\nPart time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a  (Casual) Associate Lecturer, Digital Media to join our academic community and deliver high-quality teaching, and student engagement. This is an exciting opportunity for an educator-scholar who is passionate about shaping future-ready graduates and contributing to impactful research.  WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM?   At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.  Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the  RMIT Vietnam Profile .  WHAT WE OFFER Hourly rate: 694,000 VND gross for local and 39.24 USD gross for expat candidate Private medical insurance Accident and private health insurance Participation in statutory insurance schemes Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources including gym and library A vibrant and diverse campus life and more! SCHOOL OF COMMUNICATION & DESIGN (SCD) The School of Communication & Design is committed to providing an international learning environment that encourages cultural awareness, critical thinking, experimentation and — above all — the ability to think differently. Our students develop the competence, confidence and professionalism needed for successful careers in communication, design, games, fashion, film and video, and languages. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us/schools-and-centres/school-communication-design THE BACHELOR OF DESIGN (DIGITAL MEDIA) PROGRAM In an increasingly digital world, driven by technological advancement, there is a profound need for professionals who understand timeless design principles and who can navigate future challenges as they arise. The Digital Media program provides a studio learning environment for the development of leading specialists in digital design across four main areas of action (pathways): • Interaction • Animation • Imaging • Sound ABOUT THE ROLE The Casual Associate Lecturer/ Lecturer is expected to contribute primarily to the teaching efforts of the University in disciplines related to their field of expertise. The role focuses on delivering high-quality learning experiences within undergraduate programs in the BA Design (Digital Media) discipline. At the Associate Lecturer scale, the position will be required to teach and conduct classes in disciplines relevant to their field of expertise and assist in the academic and administrative, consultative and coordination tasks involved with these courses. Functions associated with the position include presentation of lectures and tutorials, assessment of students and course administration in line with the University’s quality assurance requirements. The Associate Lecturer is also required to undertake research activities in line with the University’s research strategy. It is expected that the Associate Lecturer will work under support and guidance to develop expertise in teaching and research with an increasing degree of autonomy. At the Lecturer scale, the position is expected to contribute to the teaching and research activities of the University, in disciplines related to their field of expertise. Specifically, the Lecturer is responsible for carrying out teaching activities within undergraduate programs and for maintaining and advancing their scholarly, research and/or professional capabilities. The Lecturer is also expected to actively promote the program by establishing and maintaining memberships, links and partnerships with academic, industry and professional communities. The Lecturer is expected to work collaboratively and collegially with fellow academics within the teaching team, and update colleagues and students on developments in their subject area or specialisation. Reports to: Associate Program Manager, Digital Media Key Accountabilities: • Undergraduate teaching including designing, conducting and moderating assessment, implementing improvements informed by peer review, course evaluation and/or student feedback. • Undertake independent professional activities, scholarship and/or conduct high quality research activities appropriate to the profession or discipline, publishing research results (traditional and/or non-traditional) in high quality outlets as lead or co-author, preparing and submitting external research funding applications, and supervising higher degree by research candidates.  • Undertake administration duties and participate in University governance activities related to the position. • Adhere to the Academic Expectations and Development Framework of RMIT Vietnam. Key Selection Criteria: Hourly Associate Lecturer: A Master's degree in the relevant discipline; have commenced or enrolled to commence in Doctoral course is preferred. For Lecturer: PhD or equivalent relevant Doctoral qualification from a recognised institution. Required:  - 2D Animation -  3D Modelling and animation (Blender) - Interaction (web/games/installations/XR/VR/AR) - Digital Video (motion graphics/videography/VFX) HOW TO APPLY   To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit  resume , cover letter and portfolio . Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.  Please note that we will be running a rolling recruitment process, so please apply as soon as possible.  COMPLIANCE REQUIREMENTS    All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.    English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (Academic) with a score of at least 7.0 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).    Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.  RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT    RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.  IMPORTANT NOTICE:    Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the  RMIT Careers  page. We do not accept applications through other means.   RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply.   For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at  employment@rmit.edu.vn   #RMITVietnam Applications Close: 30 thg 10 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Enterprise-Architect_JR49416": {
      "title": "Enterprise Architect",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nOverview: Dynamic Enterprise Architect position available: Full-time, permanent. Based at the Melbourne CBD campus (Hybrid role), with flexible working arrangements Ability to work at varying levels of detail, from high-level component/logical architecture to Solution design Technical leadership across a range of complex transformation projects. About the Portfolio The Operations Portfolio enables an integrated, enterprise wide delivery for best practice student and staff experiences.  The Portfolio incorporates the following business units:  Enterprise Projects and Business Performance (EPBP), Communications, People, Information and Technology Services (ITS), Office of the Chief Operating Officer, Procurement and Vietnam Operations. The Portfolio houses significant drivers and delivery components across the staff and student journeys and enables the overall experience for both groups.  The Portfolio is integral in bringing the RMIT strategy to life, across the globe.  Each of these functions supports the global operations of the University both directly as well as through its controlled entities. The Information Technology Services (ITS) function, provides RMIT University with current and emerging Technology systems and services. Our vision of “unleashing technologies to enable great experiences for RMIT communities” supports a proactive and leading-edge technology ecosystem, mindset and delivery empowering the advancement of the University’s commitment to advancing Lifelong Learners. The Role Reporting to the Associate Director, Architecture & Solutions, you will provide enterprise‑level architectural leadership across core operational platforms supporting Finance, People (HR), Property Services, Governance, Risk & Compliance, and research enablement. You will work closely with senior stakeholders, portfolio leaders, and delivery teams to define target‑state architectures, roadmaps, standards, and reference architectures that enable scalable, secure, and future‑ready enterprise services. The Enterprise Architect (EA) is integral to the Architecture & Software Engineering group, facilitating enterprise transformation in alignment with business objectives. The EA collaborates with IT Services, business units, and leadership to formulate and prioritise RMIT University's enterprise architecture. Key responsibilities encompass the development, maintenance, and governance of the university's architectural framework, including Reference Architectures, Blueprints, Roadmaps, and Technology Strategies. Furthermore, the EA provides support to Solution Architects by guiding platform and solution-level architecture. The EA ensures comprehensive stakeholder engagement across the organisation, ensuring that architecture aligns with future requirements and RMIT's strategic goals. Why join the RMIT Information Technology TEAM? Work on impactful digital transformation initiatives. Be part of a diverse and inclusive workplace where everyone belongs. Be part of an organisation that has large support networks and believes in a work-life culture. If you're passionate about the Architecture & Software Engineering group and facilitating enterprise transformation aligned with business objectives, we'd love to hear from you About You: To be successful in this position, you’ll have Over five years' experience as an Enterprise Architect in large, complex organisations, with a strong track record in Solution Architecture and enterprise-scale technology delivery. Capable of conveying new ideas and concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences. A good understanding and exposure to digital asset management, knowledge/document/records management, CRM, ERP, LMS, Commerce, and their value to the enterprise. Exposure to diverse Governance, Risk and Compliance, and an understanding of regulatory obligations. Highly collaborative and supportive of business strategies. Experienced in working with senior business executives and able to provide professional feedback. Define and maintain the comprehensive lifecycle of strategic architecture, including roadmaps, current and target state architectures, blueprints, principles, guidelines, and Reference Architecture, by collaborating with stakeholders across the university and IT Services. Guide and participate in Solution Architecture across various projects and initiatives, ensuring that solutions adhere to architectural principles and contribute to RMIT's target state architecture. Analyse the business's future-state capabilities and current IT environment to identify critical deficiencies and recommend improvements to support and enable value delivery for the organisation. To Apply  Please submit your CV addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link below. Please click on the Position Description to learn more about the role. https://www.rmit.edu.au/content/dam/rmit/au/en/careers/position-descriptions/pd-enterprise-architect261.pdf Please note that if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply ’, and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page. Due to recent upgrades, links to position descriptions may not work in LinkedIn advertisements.   We run a rolling recruitment process, so please don't wait until the closing date to apply.  When you join our team, you can access a range of benefits: www.rmit.edu.au/careers/employee-benefits . From travel to fitness, there's something for everyone! Applications Close: 27 Oct 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Lead--Workforce-Operations_JR50980-1": {
      "title": "Lead, Workforce Operations",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-28\nFull time\n\nOverview: Full-time, Fixed Term position until 31 December 2027 (Secondment Backfill) Salary HEW 8 ($121,213 - $136,507 p.a.) + 17% Superannuation and Flexible Working Arrangements Based at the Melbourne CBD campus, but may be required to work and/or be based at other campuses of the University About the Role We are seeking an experienced people leader to lead our Workforce Operations team and support the delivery of effective, responsive and continuously improving workforce services across STEM College. The ideal candidate will bring strong experience leading and developing teams within a service delivery environment, with the ability to manage competing priorities, plan and balance workloads, and build a positive and accountable team culture.   Experience within HR or workforce operations would be highly regarded; however, we are particularly interested in candidates who can demonstrate: Strong people leadership and team management experience Service delivery and operational management capability Workforce and workload planning Continuous improvement and service optimisation Using data and reporting to monitor performance, identify trends and inform priorities Strong stakeholder management and the ability to navigate complex service environments Experience leading teams through change and embedding new ways of working   This is an opportunity to lead an established and capable team, shaping and guiding the continued development of the Workforce Operations function. The role will focus on strengthening ways of working, building team capability, and driving continuous improvement in how workforce services are delivered across STEM College. To be successful in this position, you’ll have: Demonstrated experience leading service-based teams to deliver consistent, high-quality operational outcomes, including coaching, developing and managing team performance. Strong understanding of workforce processes, systems and compliance requirements, ideally within a higher education environment. Proven ability to establish and maintain governance frameworks, ensuring consistent application of policies, procedures and standards. Experience driving continuous improvement, including process standardisation, automation and service optimisation. Strong stakeholder engagement and advisory capability, with the ability to influence and guide senior stakeholders. Highly developed analytical skills, including the ability to interpret data, identify trends and provide insights to inform decision-making. Demonstrated capacity to exercise sound judgement, work independently and manage competing priorities in a high-volume operational environment. Demonstrated knowledge of, and ability to interpret and apply, relevant policies, procedures and standards, providing practical and consistent operational advice. Highly developed written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to prepare clear, concise reports, briefings and correspondence, and facilitate effective discussions. Strong relationship management and negotiation skills, with the ability to work effectively with College leadership, academic and professional staff, and central service partners. High-level digital and systems capability, including proficiency in business systems, spreadsheets, databases and reporting tools to support operational management and data integrity. Relevant qualification and/or relevant industry experience. Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check. About the STEM College The STEM College holds a leading position and expertise in the science, technology, engineering, mathematics, and health (STEM) fields.  We are uniquely positioned to influence and partner with industry as never before.    The STEM College is a community of exceptional STEM researchers, teachers, inventors, designers and game-changers, supported by talented professional staff. We offer higher education programs across all STEM disciplines at the Bachelor, Master and PhD levels, and ensure our students experience an education that is work-aligned and life-changing.   The College is renowned for its exemplary research in many STEM areas including advanced manufacturing and design; computing technologies; health innovation and translational medicine; nano materials and devices; and sustainable systems. Our brilliant researchers attract funding from government and industry sources.    Industry is at the heart of what we do. It ensures our research has real world impact and our students are truly work-ready.  We have established new hubs of industry-connected digital innovation and endeavour and are engaging with global STEM organisations at scale.    Our diversity and shared values empower our work, and we are proud of the College’s inclusive, caring culture. We offer a safe, dynamic work environment, and support every member of our community to achieve their potential. The College appointed Victoria’s first ever Dean of STEMM, Diversity & Inclusion in 2020, and this role drives gender equity, diversity and inclusion strategies across the College.   The STEM College employs 1,000 staff who deliver onshore and offshore programs to approximately 20,000 students.    We are here to positively impact the world and create the next generation of STEM leaders.  https://www.rmit.edu.au/about/schools-colleges/stem-college   STEM College Operations Under the leadership of the General Manager, the College Operations Group comprises the following functions Student Lifecycle Operations & Service Optimisation Facilities & Technical Services Program Lifecycle & Governance Business Development & Partnerships Together, they provide comprehensive, end-to-end professional support that underpins the strategic and operational success of the College, ensuring alignment with University policies and procedures. To Apply  Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page. For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Julie Nunn – Associate Director, Operations and Service Optimisation via email julie.nunn@rmit.edu.au    For further information regarding recruitment processes, please contact Jennifer Pham, Senior Talent Acquisition Advisor via email at jennifer.pham2@rmit.edu.au Please do not share your application to this email address.     Position Description – Lead, Workforce Operations Applications Close: 11 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Barcelona/Finance-Operations-Manager_JR51332": {
      "title": "Finance Operations Manager",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nOverview: Based in Barcelona, collaborative and dynamic international team High level proficiency in English Full time, continuing role   We are seeking a Finance Operations Manager to lead the Finance function for RMIT Europe, a separate legal entity and wholly owned subsidiary of RMIT University. The position is responsible for the operational management of all financial activities, ensuring compliance with Spanish statutory requirements, taxation obligations, University policies, and broader governance frameworks.   The position leads a small team that partners with the business to support operations, and provides financial leadership across a portfolio of European Union funded projects, ensuring compliance with funding regulations, effective financial management, successful audit outcomes, and high-quality reporting to funding agencies and stakeholders.   Success in this role requires extensive technical expertise in financial management, statutory reporting, taxation and governance, combined with demonstrated leadership capability, experience managing finance teams, strong stakeholder engagement skills, and the ability to influence decision-making in a complex international environment.   What will you be accountable for? Lead and manage RMIT Europe’s finance function, ensuring strong financial governance, compliance, and stewardship. Provide strategic financial advice and insights to support organisational planning, decision-making, and long-term sustainability. Oversee budgeting, forecasting, financial reporting, cash flow, payroll, and day-to-day financial operations. Ensure compliance with statutory, taxation, regulatory, and RMIT University reporting requirements. Manage the financial administration and compliance of EU-funded research and innovation projects. Lead financial risk management, internal controls, and audit activities to safeguard organisational resources. Drive continuous improvement of financial systems, processes, policies, and reporting frameworks. Develop and lead a high-performing finance team, fostering collaboration, capability development, and service excellence.   Let’s talk about you At least eight years’ experience in financial management, accounting, taxation, and statutory reporting within complex organisations. Strong expertise in budgeting, forecasting, financial analysis, management reporting, and business partnering. Sound knowledge of Spanish accounting, taxation, compliance, and corporate governance requirements. Experience managing the financial administration and compliance of EU-funded projects and audits. Proven ability to lead finance functions, manage risk and controls, and develop high-performing teams. Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with fluency in Spanish and English. Desirable Knowledge of financial reporting requirements of not-for-profit entities in Spain. Knowledge of European funding programmes. Knowledge of education sector, and experience working in a university or research centre.   Who is RMIT Europe? We’re the creative and dynamic European hub of RMIT University. Based in the heart of Barcelona, our focus is on successfully extending RMIT’s international engagement and strategically growing the University’s collaborative research and education activity in Europe. We facilitate RMIT's collaboration in the development of innovative pan-European projects attracting global knowledge from Europe, Australia, and Asia to deliver local impact. We’re a collaborative and dynamic international team, passionate about driving impact through our work, celebrating our achievement. About the team. You’ll be joining an ambitious team of experienced professionals who are passionate about making a difference and delivering real impact. Benefits of working at RMIT Europe include hybrid working arrangements, flexible salary benefits (transport, health insurance, childcare, and restaurants) and free languages classes. Here’s how to apply: Please submit your CV and covering letter outlining your suitability for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.   For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below. Position Description – Finance Operations Manager   Please note, if you are viewing this advert from an external site, please click ‘apply’ and you will be redirected to RMIT's Jobs website to access the Position Description at the bottom of the page.   Applications Close: 15 nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT Europe is the European hub of RMIT University, one of Australia's largest tertiary institutions. Based in Barcelona, we're focused on expanding RMIT’s reputation as a global university of technology, design and enterprise."
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Financial-and-Administrative-Coordinator_JR51877": {
      "title": "Financial and Administrative Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking a Financial and Administrative Coordinator to join our School of English and University Pathways (SEUP). In this role, you will support the School’s financial and administrative operations, including purchasing, contract coordination, financial reporting and process improvement. Working closely with School leadership and internal and external stakeholders, you will help ensure accurate financial information, efficient processes and effective operational decision-making.   In line with our current recruitment and selection guidelines, this role is open to Vietnamese candidates only.   Expected start date: at the earliest available opportunity.   WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.   Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile .   WHAT WE OFFER Competitive gross remuneration package for candidates. 13th month Tet bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance 20 days annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas break and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!   POSITION SUMMARY The Financial and Administrative Coordinator provides financial, purchasing, contract and administrative coordination for the School of English and University Pathways (SEUP). The role works closely with the Director, School Manager, Heads of Program, administrative staff and RMIT central service teams, including Finance, Legal, Procurement, ITS and Property Services. It also works with external stakeholders, including corporate clients, government, partner institutions, and international and foreign-based universities. The position coordinates information and documentation across different organisations, systems, processes, time zones and cultural contexts, ensuring information is accurate, timely, appropriately documented and progressed through the relevant approval and governance processes. The Financial and Administrative Coordinator provides accurate and timely financial information, supports effective financial controls and contributes to sound operational decision-making. The role provides financial and administrative advice to SEUP leadership, managers, and staff within its area of responsiblity and identifies opportunities to strengthen processes, improve efficiency and mitigate financial and operational risks. The role requires a high level of attention to detail, sound financial understanding, strong digital and technology capability, and the ability to work confidently with financial, administrative and business systems.   KEY ACCOUNTABILITIES SUMMARY 1. Financial management, budgeting and reporting Coordinate SEUP’s budgeting and forecasting cycles by entering budget items, gathering inputs from program teams and preparing reports for review by the School Manager and Central Finance. Monitor budgets, revenue and expenditure across SEUP programs and portfolios. Prepare regular financial reports, reconciliations and forecasts, including analysis and commentary to support informed financial and operational decision-making. Support year-end accrual processes and adjust budget line items as required, ensuring financial records accurately reflect commitments and expenditure. Maintain accurate and confidential financial records in accordance with RMIT policies, procedures and financial controls. Identify financial risks, discrepancies and emerging trends, escalating issues and recommending corrective actions where appropriate.   2. Purchasing, invoicing and financial administration Act as a key SEUP contact for purchasing, purchase orders, invoices, claims and related financial processes. Coordinate asset planning, purchasing, recording, maintenance and disposal in consultation with ITS, Finance and Property Services. Coordinate the timely and accurate processing of purchasing and payment transactions. Provide guidance and training to administrative staff on purchasing, invoicing and reconciliation processes. Identify opportunities to streamline purchasing and financial administration processes and improve efficiency. Ensure transactions comply with RMIT financial delegations, procurement requirements and relevant policies. Monitor outstanding financial transactions, approvals and actions, following up with relevant stakeholders to ensure timely resolution. Maintain appropriate financial records and documentation to support financial controls, audit requirements and business continuity.   3. Contracts and program administration Coordinate the documentation, review, approval and administration of service, goods, corporate training, memoranda of understanding (MOUs) and other relevant agreements, from initiation through to execution, renewal and closure. Liaise with Legal, Finance, Tax, Procurement and other relevant teams to support timely contract processing in accordance with RMIT requirements. Maintain an accurate contract register, including key dates, obligations, renewals and financial information, and proactively monitor upcoming milestones and actions. Liaise with external stakeholders, including government, corporate clients, partner institutions and international universities, in relation to contracts, MOUs and other programme arrangements. Coordinate the collection and maintenance of supporting documentation and evidence required for contractual, financial, compliance and audit purposes. Perform other duties commensurate with the scope of the role.   4. Governance, Compliance and Continuous Improvement  Support compliance with RMIT policies, procedures, delegated authorities and relevant governance requirements. Support to identify financial, operational and contractual risks, escalating issues and supporting agreed mitigation actions. Coordinate information required for school-level governance, audit and reporting purposes. Provide accurate and timely information to support accountability, planning and decision-making. Handle confidential, personal and commercially sensitive information appropriately. Identify opportunities to improve SEUP’s processes, systems and data quality, recommend practical solutions, and support staff in adopting consistent practices for system use, data management, documentation and reporting. Other duties commensurate with the scope of the role   Key Selection Criteria A. Qualifications and prerequisites A relevant undergraduate degree in accounting, finance, business administration or related discipline, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. Ability to satisfy RMIT English-language standards relevant to the position. Relevant training or experience in procurement, contract administration, business analysis or systems improvement.   B. Professional experience Experience supporting financial administration, budgeting, reporting, reconciliation, purchasing, invoicing and contract administration. Experience working with financial processes and records in an organisation, preferably in education or a similar environment. Experience preparing reports, checking financial information and assisting with identifying variances or issues. Experience using financial, administrative and business systems, including spreadsheets and reporting tools. Experience contributing to process improvements and supporting the use of systems and digital workflows. Experience coordinating information, stakeholders, priorities and deadlines. Experience handling confidential and commercially sensitive information appropriately. Experience working with education providers, government or corporate organisations would be advantageous. C. Competencies, skills and knowledge High level of attention to detail and accuracy. Sound understanding of financial management principles, including budgeting, forecasting, reconciliation, invoicing, revenue and expenditure monitoring. Strong analytical skills, with the ability to interpret financial information and provide practical recommendations. Strong digital and technology capability, including advanced spreadsheet skills and confidence learning and improving business systems. Demonstrated ability to identify inefficiencies and develop practical systems and process improvements. Strong written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work effectively with academic and professional staff, central service teams and external stakeholders; communicate financial and contractual information clearly; and handle sensitive information with discretion. Strong organisational skills and the ability to manage competing priorities. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a changing operational environment. Commitment to confidentiality, ethical conduct, continuous improvement and RMIT values. Ability to demonstrate behaviours consistent with RMIT’s values and policies. Ability to display appropriate behaviours in line with the position, RMIT Values and RMIT Leadership Model.   For full details of the accountability, please refer to the Job Description .   HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and the University reserves the right to appoint prior to the closing date.   Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.0 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.   RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.   IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at nhu.tranngocquynh@rmit.edu.vn Applications Close: 8 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Ho-Chi-Minh-City/Director--Infrastructure---Property_JR51759": {
      "title": "Director, Infrastructure & Property",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nOverview: RMIT Vietnam is seeking an accomplished Director, Infrastructure to join our senior leadership team. This is an exciting opportunity to shape the future of our campuses, drive infrastructure and operational excellence across Vietnam, and lead strategic property, facilities and capital works initiatives. The role will play a pivotal part in creating safe, sustainable and world-class environments that enhance the experience of our students and staff.   WHY JOIN RMIT VIETNAM? At RMIT Vietnam, international exposure meets real-world impact through strong industry and government collaboration. Working at RMIT means building a meaningful career while creating impact in a high-performing environment.   Further insight into our mission, impact and global connections is available in the RMIT Vietnam Profile .   WHAT WE OFFER Vietnamese candidates Competitive remuneration VND package for Vietnamese candidates. Annual Executive bonus Private Health insurance for you and your family, plus Personal Accident Insurance   Expatriates Competitive remuneration package USD for expatriate candidates Relocation allowance package of US$11,000 Relocation flights from home location to Vietnam for candidate and direct dependents (if applicable) International repatriation flights for the staff and direct dependents at the end of their contract. School tuition fees for children to attend the K-12 program in Vietnam, up to US$20,000 per child or US$40,000 for two children per year. Premium private medical insurance for employee and immediate family, plus Personal Accident Insurance Dedicated support from Global Mobility Team to support with immigration and relocation to Vietnam.   Other benefits Generous annual leave, sick leave, volunteer leave and public holidays (Christmas and Tet Holidays) Professional development and career advancement Access to state-of-the-art facilities and resources A vibrant and diverse campus life and more!   POSITION SUMMARY The position is a key executive leadership role with institutional accountability for the strategic vision, operational excellence, financial performance, and statutory compliance of RMIT Vietnam’s physical assets, operational services, and spatial environments across all campuses across Saigon South, Hanoi, and Da Nang campuses.   The position oversees the planning, optimization, and continuous enhancement of RMIT Vietnam’s campus infrastructure, ensuring the built environment effectively supports current and future academic, research, and operational objectives. Acting as a critical interface between operational execution and executive leadership, this position drives a customer-centric and sustainable campus culture, manages complex multi-million-dollar operating and capital budgets, and establishes robust regulatory compliance and safety standards.   The position provides high-level strategic counsel to the University Executives. The role guides long-term property plans, asset lifecycle modeling, and space allocation frameworks, ensuring that RMIT Vietnam’s physical footprint continuously aligns with and enables the university's academic, research, and enterprise strategies.   Key Accountabilities summary   Strategic Leadership, Alignment, and Governance Provide overarching strategic leadership and vision for the Infrastructure - BAU across all RMIT Vietnam campuses, driving measurable progress toward academic, research, and operational enablement. Formulate, implement, and report on the annual departmental business plan, strategic operational work plans, and multi-year infrastructure roadmap in accordance with the approved RMIT Vietnam Business Plan. Foster a high-performance, inclusive, and customer-centric culture within the division, establishing high standards of teamwork, transparency, and professional excellence. Drive effective coordination between the Infrastructure department, Academic Centres, and other supporting/functional divisions (e.g., ITS, Finance, HR) to ensure capital and operational plans support student learning outcomes. High-Level Stakeholder Management & Executive Advisory Act as the primary strategic interface on property operations, space allocation, and maintenance trends for the RMIT Vietnam Executive Team and University Leadership. Deliver executive-level recommendations and analytical policy options regarding space planning, capital programming, operational costing, tendering, commercial contracts, and design standards. Lead the campus engagement program, constructively consulting with Heads of Schools, academic departments, and supporting divisions to resolve spatial, operational, and facility transition issues. Represent the Infrastructure BAU division in high-level external forums, negotiating with developers, municipal authorities, state regulators, and joint venture partners. Strategic Facilities Management & Capital Asset Protection Governance Govern the strategic management of RMIT Vietnam’s equipment and physical asset portfolio, ensuring dynamic lifecycle modeling, rigorous condition assessments, and renewal forecasts are utilized to minimize whole-life asset costs and maximize long-term value. Oversee and authorize the planned preventive maintenance (PPM) framework, reactive technical services, statutory inspections, and essential building plant operations led by the AD Facilities Management & Capital Works. Direct the commercial procurement and contract execution of capital works, ensuring all facilities meet the functional, quality, and performance standards defined in project briefs, the RMIT University Design Standards Manual, and local statutory regulations. Partner with the Director, ITS to establish a coordinated and aligned minor works and technology integration program across RMIT Vietnam’s built environments. Establish clear commercial and operational boundaries, implementing formal financial thresholds to define when works are classified as Minor Capital Works/Refurbishments (FMCW) versus Major Developments (Project IPD). Campus Experience, Spatial Services, and Security Governance Govern the development and application of advanced space planning models to evaluate spatial impact on the property, asset management, and development plans across all RMIT Vietnam campuses. Direct RMIT Vietnam's academic timetabling operations, ensuring optimal, data-driven class scheduling (via Syllabus Plus and Archibus) to maximize built space efficiency and accommodate student enrollment growth. Strategically lead RMIT Vietnam's physical security, emergency response, and occupational health and safety (OHS) capabilities to ensure highly secure, compliant, and supportive campus environments for staff, students, and visitors. Exercise executive oversight over food and beverage commercial leasing and operations, ensuring strict compliance with local health, safety, and hygiene regulations and commercial performance targets. Provide high-level guidance for campus operational services, including the front-facing customer helpdesk, cleaning services, mail systems, storage, and integrated logistics support for university events. Ensure operational property services, safety protocols, and technical service standard consistency at the Hanoi and Da Nang campuses, aligning them with the standards established at the Saigon South campus   Corporate Services, Commercial Operations, and Sustainability Governance Direct and approve the development of annual and rolling facilities operating and capital budgets, ensuring multi-million-dollar funds are effectively allocated, cost-optimized, and compliant with approved financial procedures. Command the vendor and performance management framework across the entire Property and Places service and supply chain, conducting robust evaluations of specialist contractors. Lead and champion RMIT Vietnam's comprehensive sustainability program, actively integrating best-practice environmental management, waste reduction, energy efficiency, and carbon emissions tracking into daily campus operations and external vendor contracts. Oversee the centralized corporate support team, ensuring seamless execution of division-wide administration, HR coordination, procurement governance, and commercial risk mitigation. Project-to-BAU Handover and Operational Readiness Act as the principal operational content expert, providing strategic subject matter expertise to major campus investment programs led by the Project Delivery division. Direct transitional and operational readiness activities as new campus developments are completed, ensuring rigorous commissioning, spatial moves, and technical handovers support academic requirements with zero disruption Team Leadership and Talent Development Lead, mentor, and motivate a large, diverse team of associate directors, managers, technical specialists, and external contractors. Foster a high-performance culture by establishing clear roles, performance expectations, individual development pathways, and proactive change management. Key Selection Criteria Bachelor’s degree in Tertiary degree in Electrical or Mechanical Engineering or Property/ Facilities Management, Construction Management, Business Administration or related field. Postgraduate university degree qualifications in Business, Property, Construction or Project Management or related field are highly desirable. Minimum of 12 years of senior executive management and strategic leadership experience directing integrated portfolios of Facilities Management & Capital Asset Protection, Campus Experience & Spatial Services, and Corporate Support Operations within a large, multi-site, multi-cultural, or international corporate or higher education environment. Proven experience in governing complex, high-value physical asset portfolios, including directing multi-year planned preventative maintenance programs, strategic capital renewal modeling, lifecycle asset protection, and minor works refurbishment programs. Extensive experience directing institutional property plans, campus security operations, occupational health and safety (OHS) compliance governance, on-site retail lease management, and academic timetabling systems optimization (Syllabus Plus, Archibus) to maximize spatial efficiency and enhance campus life Substantive experience in authorizing, controlling, and optimizing complex multi-million-dollar operating and capital budgets, with advanced commercial procurement governance, contract administration, and executive-level vendor negotiation skills. Demonstrated success working collaboratively with international executive teams to seamlessly align local services with global strategies, acting as an authoritative counterpart to international C-suite leaders to co-design infrastructure and related policy and standardized enterprise environments. Demonstrated capacity for leading large-scale organizational change, managing ambiguity, and guiding multi-disciplinary teams through transitions in a rapidly changing environment. Strategic capability to leverage and govern enterprise property technology suites (such as CAFM/CMMS, CAD, Building Management Systems, Syllabus Plus, and Archibus) to drive data-informed executive decisions, operational efficiency, and spatial optimization. Highly developed conceptual and analytical skills with a proven ability to formulate institutional policies, evaluate complex investment options, and provide authoritative inputs to corporate strategy development [79]. Demonstrated success in championing an institutional, client-focused service culture and driving continuous service-improvement frameworks across complex operating departments. Outstanding executive people management skills, with a proven track record of recruiting, leading, mentoring, and inspiring high-performing, diverse, and multi-disciplinary management teams, fostering a culture of teamwork, psychological safety, and accountability. Uncompromising commitment to governing health, safety, physical security, environmental compliance, and strategic sustainability/carbon-reduction frameworks, ensuring ethical business conduct Excellent fluency in communication in English and well as organisational and administrative skills to effectively facilitate professional service delivery of large geographically dispersed teams.  Demonstrated alignment with RMIT Values and the RMIT Leadership Model    More information is available in the Job Description .   HOW TO APPLY To be considered for this role, it is mandatory to submit both a resume and a cover letter. Please click on the 'Apply' link provided in this Job Ads to initiate the application process.   Please note: This is a rolling recruitment process, and the position may close before the advertised closing date. We encourage candidates to apply early.   Compliance Requirements All academic appointments at RMIT Vietnam must meet University and local regulatory requirements, including English proficiency, background checks, and (for international candidates) eligibility for a work permit.  English is the language of teaching and communication at RMIT Vietnam. For this role, the minimum requirement is IELTS (General) with a score of at least 6.5 with no competency less than 6.5 (or equivalent, as outlined in the Recruitment, Selection and Onboarding Guidelines).  Further guidance will be provided during the recruitment process.   RMIT UNIVERSITY COMMITMENT RMIT is committed to the rights of students and staff to be safe, respected, valued, and treated as an equal in their place of study and work. All staff are expected to share this commitment and contribute to a safer community. While carrying out their role, staff are in a position of trust with students. Staff have a duty of care to report wellbeing concerns about students through the designated channels and uphold the code of conduct. RMIT Vietnam expects all staff members to comply with its Code of Conduct, policies and procedures, which relate to legal and regulatory requirements and our ways of working.   IMPORTANT NOTICE: Please ensure that your application is submitted through our Workday system on the RMIT Careers page. We do not accept applications through other means. RMIT Vietnam will never request any fees or payments during the application process. Be vigilant about scams asking for payment to apply. For any questions or support, feel free to reach out to our Talent Acquisition team at employment@rmit.edu.vn   Applications Close: 29 thg 11 2026 11.59 pm RMIT University Vietnam (RMIT Vietnam) is a campus of RMIT University. RMIT Vietnam is creating an innovative research, teaching and learning culture. We are committed to providing internationally recognised high-quality education and professional training for our students, clients and members of the community.   As an internationally recognised Australian university based in Asia, RMIT Vietnam is assisting in the development of human resources capability in Vietnam and the region. https://www.rmit.edu.vn/about-us"
    },
    "https://rmit.wd3.myworkdayjobs.com/RMIT_Careers/job/Melbourne/Manager--Gender-based-Violence-Prevention-and-Compliance_JR51681": {
      "title": "Manager, Gender-based Violence Prevention and Compliance",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-29\nFull time\n\nOverview: ​​Full-time​, ​Fixed Term position until​ July 2028 Hew 9 + 17% Superannuation and Flexible Working Arrangements Based at the ​Melbourne CBD​ campus, ​and hybrid ways of working​ About the role The Manager, Gender-based Violence Prevention and Compliance, will lead RMIT’s institutional implementation of the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence 2025 (The National Code). Working under broad direction, the role provides high-level strategic leadership, project management, stakeholder engagement, and compliance and policy expertise to ensure RMIT meets its legislative and regulatory obligations and delivers sustained cultural and organisational change. The position will manage a diverse project portfolio and liaise across senior governance committees, Internal and external stakeholders, and sector partners. The incumbent will oversee policy development, compliance reporting, evaluation frameworks, and the integration of prevention and response measures into RMIT’s systems, processes, and partnerships. The position will be responsible for maintaining up-to-date records of compliance activities. Key Responsibilities: Manage RMIT’s compliance with the National Code, which includes monitoring compliance, identifying compliance gaps and developing solutions, and reporting on compliance. Manage and coordinate implementation of the National Code requirements, ensuring delivery within agreed timelines, budgets and quality standards. Maintain up-to-date expertise in gender equity and gender-based violence legislation and compliance, providing timely advice to support RMIT’s regulatory obligations.  Support the planning and implementation of RMIT’s Gender-based Violence Prevention and Response Plan 2026–29 (RMIT’s Plan). Coordinate RMIT’s National Code Working Group, including chairing, governance, action tracking and cross-functional delivery.  Lead the development and review of policies, procedures and guidelines to ensure alignment with the National Code. Establish and maintain strong processes to track and monitor compliance, evaluation and annual reporting processes. Collaborate with the Prevention and Respect team and the Safer Community team to deliver National Code requirements and actions in RMIT’s Plan. Review third-party arrangements to ensure National Code compliance, working closely with RMIT legal teams. Represent RMIT in sector networks and external forums to share practice and contribute to policy development. To be successful in this position, you’ll have: Strong gender-based violence prevention and response expertise, with sound knowledge of relevant compliance and regulatory frameworks. Relevant background and experience in government, higher education, large complex organisations, consulting, or gender-based violence/family violence organisations. Demonstrated experience working in a role which involves overseeing regulatory obligations, compliance, and implementation. Ability to translate complex legislation and regulatory requirements into practical solutions and organisational action, rather than taking a purely policy or advocacy approach.  Strong project management and implementation capability, including strategy, risk, financial management and organisational change.  Proven experience developing and implementing organisation-wide policies, procedures and strategies.  Strong stakeholder management and influencing skills, particularly with senior leaders, government and external stakeholders. Excellent written and verbal communication, including developing executive-level reports, briefings and presentations.  Able to work collaboratively, flexibly and practically within a large, complex organisation. Government or higher education experience would be highly relevant. Relevant postgraduate qualification in areas such as public health, health promotion, gender-based violence, gender equity, social work or behavioural science, or equivalent relevant experience. Please Note: Appointment to this position is subject to passing a Working with Children and National Police Check. About the ​Portfolio​   The Operations Portfolio enables an integrated, enterprise-wide delivery for best practice audience experiences (student, staff and industry). The Portfolio incorporates the following business units: Enterprise Projects and Business Performance (EPBP), Communications, Global Marketing & Student Recruitment, People, Information and Technology Services (ITS), Office of the Chief Operating Officer, Procurement and Property Services Group (PSG). The Portfolio houses significant drivers and delivery components across our audience journeys and enables the overall experience. The Portfolio is integral in bringing the RMIT strategy to life, across the globe. Each of these functions supports the global operations of the University both directly as well as through its controlled entities. To Apply  Please submit your CV and covering letter addressing ​your suitability​ for this position by clicking on the ‘ Apply ’ link at the top of this page.  For further information about this position, please see the Position Description hyperlinked below or contact Bianca Jenkins via email bianca.jenkins@rmit.edu.au. Position Description Applications Close: 18 Nov 2026 11.59 pm RMIT is an equal opportunity employer committed to being a child safe organisation. We are dedicated to attracting, retaining and developing our people regardless of gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability and age. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community, and we strongly encourage applications from the Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander community.     In line with RMIT University’s commitment to a safe, respectful and inclusive environment, from 1 January 2026, the University will also consider gender-based violence (GBV) risk factors as part of our recruitment processes.  All applicants will be required to complete a gender‑based violence declaration in accordance with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence .  Preferred candidates will also be required to undertake relevant pre‑employment background checks, including Working With Children Checks. Information provided will be treated confidentially and considered only for its relevance to the role and RMIT’s safety obligations.   At RMIT, we are committed to supporting adjustments throughout the recruitment and selection process, as well as during employment. We actively support and encourage people with disability to apply to RMIT (including alternate formats of application forms). To discuss adjustment requirements, please contact Dani, via talentsupport@rmit.edu.au or visit our Careers page for more contact information - https://www.rmit.edu.au/careers.   We are a Circle Back Initiative Employer – we commit to respond to every applicant."
    }
  },
